  \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n73:     \"delta-*.jsonl\": \"write-once\",\n74:     \"research.md\": \"mutable\"\n75:   }\n76: }\n\n(End of file - total 76 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"topic\": \"Mobbin MCP developer surface for an mcp-tooling transport mode: the official Mobbin MCP server per https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server (tool surface, auth/API key model, transport, install) and the official Mobbin skills repo https://github.com/mobbin/skills — app/screen/flow/element design-research search workflows, plan gating (free vs Pro), everything needed to author the mcp-mobbin transport packet (read-only, Code Mode only, sk-design judgment pairing) and register a mobbin manual in .utcp_config.json\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 5,\n  \"minIterations\": 3,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 3,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n    \"divergent\": {},\n    \"note\": \"Convergence before maxIterations is telemetry only; broaden review angles instead of synthesizing early.\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n  \"minIdeaObservations\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": true,\n  \"specFolder\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json","text":"{\n  \"topic\": \"Mobbin MCP developer surface for an mcp-tooling transport mode: the official Mobbin MCP server per https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server (tool surface, auth/API key model, transport, install) and the official Mobbin skills repo https://github.com/mobbin/skills — app/screen/flow/element design-research search workflows, plan gating (free vs Pro), everything needed to author the mcp-mobbin transport packet (read-only, Code Mode only, sk-design judgment pairing) and register a mobbin manual in .utcp_config.json\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 5,\n  \"minIterations\": 3,\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n  \"antiConvergence\": {\n    \"minIterations\": 3,\n    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n    \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n    \"divergent\": {},\n    \"note\": \"Convergence before maxIterations is telemetry only; broaden review angles instead of synthesizing early.\"\n  },\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n  \"minIdeaObservations\": 2,\n  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n  \"progressiveSynthesis\": true,\n  \"specFolder\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research\",\n  \"artifactDir\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol\",\n  \"fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\": \".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol\",\n  \"resource_map_present\": false,\n  \"resource_map\": {\n    \"emit\": true\n  },\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-07-16T11:03:00Z\",\n  \"status\": \"complete\",\n  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"cli-codex\",\n    \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\",\n    \"reasoningEffort\": \"xhigh\",\n    \"serviceTier\": \"fast\",\n    \"sandboxMode\": \"workspace-write\",\n    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n  },\n  \"lineage\": {\n    \"sessionId\": \"fanout-sol-1784199634206-lfqjyo\",\n    \"parentSessionId\": null,\n    \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n    \"allowedModes\": [\"new\", \"resume\", \"restart\"],\n    \"deferredModes\": [\"fork\", \"completed-continue\"],\n    \"generation\": 1,\n    \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n    \"fanoutRole\": \"detached-parallel-lineage\"\n  },\n  \"reducer\": {\n    \"enabled\": true,\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"registryFile\": \"findings-registry.json\",\n    \"dashboardFile\": \"deep-research-dashboard.md\",\n    \"strategyFile\": \"deep-research-strategy.md\",\n    \"machineOwnedSections\": [\n      \"key-questions\",\n      \"answered-questions\",\n      \"what-worked\",\n      \"what-failed\",\n      \"exhausted-approaches\",\n      \"ruled-out-directions\",\n      \"divergence-frontier\",\n      \"next-focus\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"pauseSentinelPath\": \".deep-research-pause\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable-except-terminal-status\",\n    \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"delta-*.jsonl\": \"write-once\",\n    \"research.md\": \"mutable\"\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":76,"totalLines":76,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json","time":{"start":1785133710205,"end":1785133710446}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_032d183b70a23b24016a66fa8e04848191bba056d806639a19"}},"id":"prt_fa242bb73001KUcy7TzGNWaA8i","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242701d001i5piA7Vam2PW1e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133710570,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_ix2ysu3Sw0FeHqF9F1XZVnkY","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy — Mobbin MCP Sol Lineage\n3: description: Detached five-iteration research strategy for the Mobbin MCP developer surface.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Deep Research Strategy — Mobbin MCP Sol Lineage\n7: \n8: ## 1. Overview\n9: \n10: This is the persistent state for detached lineage `sol`. The loop is forced to five iterations by `stopPolicy: max-iterations`; convergence before iteration five is telemetry only.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Topic\n13: \n14: Verify the official Mobbin MCP server and skills repositories deeply enough to author a read-only, Code-Mode-only `mcp-mobbin` transport packet paired with `sk-design`, and to define an accurate name-keyed `mobbin` manual for `.utcp_config.json`.\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n17: ## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n18: \n19: - [x] What is the complete official MCP tool surface, including input fields, returned artifacts, read-only posture, transport, install path, and runtime prerequisites?\n20: - [x] What credential model does the server use, how is the key provisioned/stored, and what does a correct Code Mode manual need to expose?\n21: - [x] How do the official skills implement app, screen, flow, and element research workflows, including staged discovery and image/detail retrieval?\n22: - [x] Which capabilities are available to free users versus Pro subscribers, and what failure/upgrade behavior must the packet document without guessing?\n23: - [x] What exact transport packet, `sk-design` pairing, discovery-first calling convention, UTCP registration shape, and troubleshooting guidance should phases 002–003 author?\n24: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n25: \n26: ## 4. Non-Goals\n27: \n28: - Do not edit `.utcp_config.json`, the MCP tooling hub, or any future phase packet.\n29: - Do not invoke Mobbin tools with a real credential or expose secrets.\n30: - Do not treat the design-reference transport as a taste or implementation authority.\n31: - Do not infer undocumented pricing, quotas, response schemas, or mutation capabilities.\n32: \n33: ## 5. Stop Conditions\n34: \n35: - Complete exactly five evidence iterations unless state corruption or an unrecoverable source failure prevents valid artifacts.\n36: - Treat convergence before iteration five as telemetry and broaden into an uncovered angle.\n37: - Stop at iteration five with `maxIterationsReached`, retaining explicit unknowns.\n38: \n39: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n40: ## 6. Answered Questions\n41: \n42: - OAuth/DCR/PKCE is authoritative for MCP; a static Mobbin API key is not part of the MCP client setup. The eventual manual needs URL/OAuth handling, not a secret key field. (iteration 1)\n43: - The current official `mobbin-search` skill uses one `search_screens` call with query/platform/limit, ordered metadata plus inline images, followed by grounded visual analysis. App/flow/element research is expressed through queries and result analysis rather than separate documented tools. (iteration 2)\n44: - Free has no MCP access; Pro, Team, and Enterprise do. MCP uses OAuth, while the Team/Enterprise REST API uses a workspace API key. MCP is limited to 60 requests per 60 seconds per user. Exact Free denial payload and Finance+ MCP coverage remain UNKNOWN. (iteration 3)\n45: - The Code Mode manual is `mobbin` -> stdio `npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` with empty env. Calls are discovery-first through Code Mode; the packet is non-mutating evidence retrieval paired with `sk-design` for judgment. (iteration 4)\n46: - The complete public documented baseline is one read tool, `search_screens`, and live endpoint/OAuth metadata confirms the hosted protected resource. Authenticated tool-list completeness and exact server schemas remain validation-time UNKNOWNs. (iteration 5)\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n48: \n49: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n50: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n51: ## 7. What Worked\n52: \n53: - Official Mobbin repository manifests plus Mobbin-hosted docs: mutually consistent endpoint, transport, OAuth, and plan evidence. (iteration 1)\n54: - Reading the complete official skill: exposed exact planning inputs, response metadata, visual-analysis stages, and the optional-board boundary. (iteration 2)\n55: - Triangulating overview, MCP docs, API quick start, limits, and pricing: separated three easily conflated entitlement/credential surfaces. (iteration 3)\n56: - Local UTCP/Code Mode contracts plus the existing remote-manual precedent: yielded a paste-ready manual and exact discovery/calling lifecycle. (iteration 4)\n57: - Unauthenticated protocol probes plus official GitHub API trees: proved endpoint/auth metadata and bounded the current public tool catalog without crossing the credential boundary. (iteration 5)\n58: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n59: \n60: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n61: ## 8. What Failed\n62: \n63: - Generic web/code search: returned unrelated similarly named MCP servers and was discarded in favor of named primary sources. (iteration 1)\n64: - Search for hypothetical app/flow/element tool names: produced no official contracts and cannot substitute for authenticated `tools/list`. (iteration 2)\n65: - Pricing/help pages for protocol errors: describe eligibility but do not publish the wire-level Free denial payload. (iteration 3)\n66: - Static wiring review cannot prove the live OAuth handshake or authenticated `tools/list` surface. (iteration 4)\n67: - Unauthenticated endpoint probing cannot enumerate protected tools; public source review cannot substitute for a paid live schema. (iteration 5)\n68: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n69: \n70: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n71: ## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n72: \n73: - Static `MOBBIN_API_KEY` for MCP: official docs explicitly state no API key or manual token setup is needed. (iteration 1)\n74: - Local npm server package: official repository declares a hosted Streamable HTTP remote and publishes no runtime package. (iteration 1)\n75: - Public repository tool enumeration beyond `search_screens`: exhausted without authenticated live discovery; do not invent names. (iteration 2)\n76: - Exact Free entitlement response and Finance+ MCP coverage: public sources exhausted; retain UNKNOWN until live/proprietary evidence exists. (iteration 3)\n77: - Direct Code Mode HTTP transport: no current local manual proves it; use the established `mcp-remote` stdio adapter unless live infrastructure validation establishes a replacement. (iteration 4)\n78: - Public enumeration beyond `search_screens`: exhausted across the official skill tree, server registration tree, docs, and unauthenticated endpoint; move the remaining question to paid live validation. (iteration 5)\n79: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n80: \n81: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n82: ## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n83: \n84: - Static `MOBBIN_API_KEY` for MCP: contradicted by official OAuth documentation. (iteration 1)\n85: - Local npm/stdio Mobbin server: contradicted by official remote-server manifests. (iteration 1)\n86: - Separate `search_apps`, `search_flows`, `search_elements`, detail-fetch, or image-fetch tools: absent from the current public official contract. (iteration 2)\n87: - HTML evidence-board authoring inside `mcp-mobbin`: violates the read-only transport boundary. (iteration 2)\n88: - REST API key in the MCP manual: wrong authorization surface. (iteration 3)\n89: - Limited Free MCP inferred from limited Free website browsing: wrong entitlement surface. (iteration 3)\n90: - MCP secrets in `.env`, pre-discovery callable assumptions, and transport-owned design judgment: contradicted by Mobbin OAuth and local Code Mode/sk-design contracts. (iteration 4)\n91: - A 401 interpreted as a static-key failure, public docs represented as live `tools/list`, and bridge compatibility represented as a successful deployment: all exceed the evidence boundary. (iteration 5)\n92: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n95: ## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n96: \n97: - Completed pivots: 0\n98: - Failed pivots: 0\n99: - Audited overrides: 0\n100: - Saturated: official public tool-name enumeration; public free-denial/Finance+ detail; unauthenticated live schema enumeration\n101: - Remaining frontier: paid-account Code Mode OAuth/discovery validation and runtime schema capture\n102: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n103: \n104: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n105: ## 11A. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n106: \n107: - What exact tools does `tools/list` expose, and do official skill references match the live surface?\n108: - Does `search_screens` expose a public JSON Schema beyond the skill-level query/platform/limit contract?\n109: - Does a clean first run complete Mobbin OAuth through the current `mcp-remote` version in this environment?\n110: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n111: \n112: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n113: ## 11. Next Focus\n114: \n115: Synthesis. Preserve authenticated live schema, local OAuth round-trip, exact Free denial, and Finance+ coverage as downstream validation questions.\n116: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n117: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n118: \n119: ## 12. Known Context\n120: \n121: - Primary sources: `https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server` and `https://github.com/mobbin/skills`.\n122: - Local integration consumers are `.utcp_config.json`, the `mcp-tooling` transport packet pattern, Code Mode discovery/call conventions, and the `sk-design` judgment pairing.\n123: - `resource-map.md` was not present at init; the repository coverage gate is informationally skipped.\n124: - The phase specification requires all writes to stay within this research packet and defers actual packet/manual authoring.\n125: \n126: ## 13. Research Boundaries\n127: \n128: - Max iterations: 5\n129: - Convergence threshold: 0.05\n130: - Stop policy: max-iterations\n131: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n132: - Progressive synthesis: true\n133: - Executor provenance: `cli-codex`, model `gpt-5.6-sol`, effort `xhigh`, service tier `fast`\n134: - Session: `fanout-sol-1784199634206-lfqjyo`\n135: - Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol`\n\n(End of file - total 135 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy — Mobbin MCP Sol Lineage\ndescription: Detached five-iteration research strategy for the Mobbin MCP developer surface.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy — Mobbin MCP Sol Lineage\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nThis is the persistent state for detached lineage `sol`. The loop is forced to five iterations by `stopPolicy: max-iterations`; convergence before iteration five is telemetry only.\n\n## 2. Topic\n\nVerify the official Mobbin MCP server and skills repositories deeply enough to author a read-only, Code-Mode-only `mcp-mobbin` transport packet paired with `sk-design`, and to define an accurate name-keyed `mobbin` manual for `.utcp_config.json`.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n\n- [x] What is the complete official MCP tool surface, including input fields, returned artifacts, read-only posture, transport, install path, and runtime prerequisites?\n- [x] What credential model does the server use, how is the key provisioned/stored, and what does a correct Code Mode manual need to expose?","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy — Mobbin MCP Sol Lineage\ndescription: Detached five-iteration research strategy for the Mobbin MCP developer surface.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy — Mobbin MCP Sol Lineage\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nThis is the persistent state for detached lineage `sol`. The loop is forced to five iterations by `stopPolicy: max-iterations`; convergence before iteration five is telemetry only.\n\n## 2. Topic\n\nVerify the official Mobbin MCP server and skills repositories deeply enough to author a read-only, Code-Mode-only `mcp-mobbin` transport packet paired with `sk-design`, and to define an accurate name-keyed `mobbin` manual for `.utcp_config.json`.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n\n- [x] What is the complete official MCP tool surface, including input fields, returned artifacts, read-only posture, transport, install path, and runtime prerequisites?\n- [x] What credential model does the server use, how is the key provisioned/stored, and what does a correct Code Mode manual need to expose?\n- [x] How do the official skills implement app, screen, flow, and element research workflows, including staged discovery and image/detail retrieval?\n- [x] Which capabilities are available to free users versus Pro subscribers, and what failure/upgrade behavior must the packet document without guessing?\n- [x] What exact transport packet, `sk-design` pairing, discovery-first calling convention, UTCP registration shape, and troubleshooting guidance should phases 002–003 author?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. Non-Goals\n\n- Do not edit `.utcp_config.json`, the MCP tooling hub, or any future phase packet.\n- Do not invoke Mobbin tools with a real credential or expose secrets.\n- Do not treat the design-reference transport as a taste or implementation authority.\n- Do not infer undocumented pricing, quotas, response schemas, or mutation capabilities.\n\n## 5. Stop Conditions\n\n- Complete exactly five evidence iterations unless state corruption or an unrecoverable source failure prevents valid artifacts.\n- Treat convergence before iteration five as telemetry and broaden into an uncovered angle.\n- Stop at iteration five with `maxIterationsReached`, retaining explicit unknowns.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. Answered Questions\n\n- OAuth/DCR/PKCE is authoritative for MCP; a static Mobbin API key is not part of the MCP client setup. The eventual manual needs URL/OAuth handling, not a secret key field. (iteration 1)\n- The current official `mobbin-search` skill uses one `search_screens` call with query/platform/limit, ordered metadata plus inline images, followed by grounded visual analysis. App/flow/element research is expressed through queries and result analysis rather than separate documented tools. (iteration 2)\n- Free has no MCP access; Pro, Team, and Enterprise do. MCP uses OAuth, while the Team/Enterprise REST API uses a workspace API key. MCP is limited to 60 requests per 60 seconds per user. Exact Free denial payload and Finance+ MCP coverage remain UNKNOWN. (iteration 3)\n- The Code Mode manual is `mobbin` -> stdio `npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` with empty env. Calls are discovery-first through Code Mode; the packet is non-mutating evidence retrieval paired with `sk-design` for judgment. (iteration 4)\n- The complete public documented baseline is one read tool, `search_screens`, and live endpoint/OAuth metadata confirms the hosted protected resource. Authenticated tool-list completeness and exact server schemas remain validation-time UNKNOWNs. (iteration 5)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. What Worked\n\n- Official Mobbin repository manifests plus Mobbin-hosted docs: mutually consistent endpoint, transport, OAuth, and plan evidence. (iteration 1)\n- Reading the complete official skill: exposed exact planning inputs, response metadata, visual-analysis stages, and the optional-board boundary. (iteration 2)\n- Triangulating overview, MCP docs, API quick start, limits, and pricing: separated three easily conflated entitlement/credential surfaces. (iteration 3)\n- Local UTCP/Code Mode contracts plus the existing remote-manual precedent: yielded a paste-ready manual and exact discovery/calling lifecycle. (iteration 4)\n- Unauthenticated protocol probes plus official GitHub API trees: proved endpoint/auth metadata and bounded the current public tool catalog without crossing the credential boundary. (iteration 5)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. What Failed\n\n- Generic web/code search: returned unrelated similarly named MCP servers and was discarded in favor of named primary sources. (iteration 1)\n- Search for hypothetical app/flow/element tool names: produced no official contracts and cannot substitute for authenticated `tools/list`. (iteration 2)\n- Pricing/help pages for protocol errors: describe eligibility but do not publish the wire-level Free denial payload. (iteration 3)\n- Static wiring review cannot prove the live OAuth handshake or authenticated `tools/list` surface. (iteration 4)\n- Unauthenticated endpoint probing cannot enumerate protected tools; public source review cannot substitute for a paid live schema. (iteration 5)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n\n- Static `MOBBIN_API_KEY` for MCP: official docs explicitly state no API key or manual token setup is needed. (iteration 1)\n- Local npm server package: official repository declares a hosted Streamable HTTP remote and publishes no runtime package. (iteration 1)\n- Public repository tool enumeration beyond `search_screens`: exhausted without authenticated live discovery; do not invent names. (iteration 2)\n- Exact Free entitlement response and Finance+ MCP coverage: public sources exhausted; retain UNKNOWN until live/proprietary evidence exists. (iteration 3)\n- Direct Code Mode HTTP transport: no current local manual proves it; use the established `mcp-remote` stdio adapter unless live infrastructure validation establishes a replacement. (iteration 4)\n- Public enumeration beyond `search_screens`: exhausted across the official skill tree, server registration tree, docs, and unauthenticated endpoint; move the remaining question to paid live validation. (iteration 5)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n\n- Static `MOBBIN_API_KEY` for MCP: contradicted by official OAuth documentation. (iteration 1)\n- Local npm/stdio Mobbin server: contradicted by official remote-server manifests. (iteration 1)\n- Separate `search_apps`, `search_flows`, `search_elements`, detail-fetch, or image-fetch tools: absent from the current public official contract. (iteration 2)\n- HTML evidence-board authoring inside `mcp-mobbin`: violates the read-only transport boundary. (iteration 2)\n- REST API key in the MCP manual: wrong authorization surface. (iteration 3)\n- Limited Free MCP inferred from limited Free website browsing: wrong entitlement surface. (iteration 3)\n- MCP secrets in `.env`, pre-discovery callable assumptions, and transport-owned design judgment: contradicted by Mobbin OAuth and local Code Mode/sk-design contracts. (iteration 4)\n- A 401 interpreted as a static-key failure, public docs represented as live `tools/list`, and bridge compatibility represented as a successful deployment: all exceed the evidence boundary. (iteration 5)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: official public tool-name enumeration; public free-denial/Finance+ detail; unauthenticated live schema enumeration\n- Remaining frontier: paid-account Code Mode OAuth/discovery validation and runtime schema capture\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n\n- What exact tools does `tools/list` expose, and do official skill references match the live surface?\n- Does `search_screens` expose a public JSON Schema beyond the skill-level query/platform/limit contract?\n- Does a clean first run complete Mobbin OAuth through the current `mcp-remote` version in this environment?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. Next Focus\n\nSynthesis. Preserve authenticated live schema, local OAuth round-trip, exact Free denial, and Finance+ coverage as downstream validation questions.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## 12. Known Context\n\n- Primary sources: `https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server` and `https://github.com/mobbin/skills`.\n- Local integration consumers are `.utcp_config.json`, the `mcp-tooling` transport packet pattern, Code Mode discovery/call conventions, and the `sk-design` judgment pairing.\n- `resource-map.md` was not present at init; the repository coverage gate is informationally skipped.\n- The phase specification requires all writes to stay within this research packet and defers actual packet/manual authoring.\n\n## 13. Research Boundaries\n\n- Max iterations: 5\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Stop policy: max-iterations\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- Executor provenance: `cli-codex`, model `gpt-5.6-sol`, effort `xhigh`, service tier `fast`\n- Session: `fanout-sol-1784199634206-lfqjyo`\n- Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":135,"totalLines":135,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1785133710213,"end":1785133710448}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_032d183b70a23b24016a66fa8e049481919c5d89c1b682f4ed"}},"id":"prt_fa242bb83001v1jTWbQfqAdztv","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242701d001i5piA7Vam2PW1e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133710612,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_IBsU8RULDqUpRRjsJq7ADfOH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/*synth*"},"output":"No files found","metadata":{"count":0,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1785133710223,"end":1785133710582}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_032d183b70a23b24016a66fa8e04a0819185bcd8f2f2d33643"}},"id":"prt_fa242bb8b001vt9DTBO5UZeEaY","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242701d001i5piA7Vam2PW1e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133710612,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_Eem2yrsQgGoIZNFlBxAgMMgL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/*research*"},"output":"No files found","metadata":{"count":0,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1785133710218,"end":1785133710609}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_032d183b70a23b24016a66fa8e049c819185b2373bfa1d09ee"}},"id":"prt_fa242bb87001DYJfftW73t0wUf","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242701d001i5piA7Vam2PW1e"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1785133714025,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"id":"prt_fa242ca64001mQ0micyZhWBnhZ","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fa242701d001i5piA7Vam2PW1e","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":147151,"input":39500,"output":463,"reasoning":180,"cache":{"write":0,"read":107008}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785133721851,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"id":"prt_fa242e8f8001TPayTrJaY259TQ","messageID":"msg_fa242d1f7001m3St348OtWWs65","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133727979,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_KVn4XN38GE6dNOB1g0B4ApF9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","offset":960,"limit":190},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n960:     loop_type: loopType,\n961:     spec_folder: specFolder,\n962:   });\n963: \n964:   return { didWait: true, migrated: loaded.migrated };\n965: }\n966: \n967: async function persistPreDispatchWait({ checkpointPath, ledgerPath, runId, loopType, specFolder, waitMs }) {\n968:   const durationMs = normalizeWaitDurationMs(waitMs);\n969:   if (durationMs <= 0) {\n970:     return { didWait: false };\n971:   }\n972: \n973:   const checkpoint = buildWaitCheckpoint({ waitMs: durationMs, runId, loopType, specFolder });\n974:   atomicWriteJson(checkpointPath, checkpoint);\n975:   appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n976:     event: 'wait_checkpoint_persisted',\n977:     at: checkpoint.updatedAt,\n978:     run_id: runId,\n979:     loop_type: loopType,\n980:     spec_folder: specFolder,\n981:     nextRunAt: checkpoint.nextRunAt,\n982:     remainingDelayMs: checkpoint.remainingDelayMs,\n983:   });\n984: \n985:   await waitUntilCheckpointExpires({\n986:     checkpointPath,\n987:     checkpoint,\n988:     context: { runId, loopType, specFolder },\n989:   });\n990: \n991:   appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n992:     event: 'wait_checkpoint_cleared',\n993:     at: new Date().toISOString(),\n994:     run_id: runId,\n995:     loop_type: loopType,\n996:     spec_folder: specFolder,\n997:   });\n998: \n999:   return { didWait: true };\n1000: }\n1001: \n1002: /**\n1003:  * Build the \"run the full loop\" prompt text for a CLI lineage subprocess.\n1004:  * The subprocess reads this, loads the skill, and runs the requested stop policy\n1005:  * with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir overriding step_resolve_artifact_root.\n1006:  */\n1007: function buildLoopPrompt(loopType, specFolder, lineageDir, sessionId, lineage, researchTopic, options = {}) {\n1008:   assertActiveFanoutLoopType(loopType);\n1009:   const skillFile =\n1010:     loopType === 'review'\n1011:       ? '.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md'\n1012:       : '.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md';\n1013:   const agentName = loopType === 'review' ? 'deep-review' : 'deep-research';\n1014:   const detachedIntro = lineage.kind === 'cli-opencode'\n1015:     ? [\n1016:         `This is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode lineage, not a self-invocation of the parent session.`,\n1017:         `Use the separate lineage directory and session id below as the detached state boundary.`,\n1018:         ``,\n1019:       ]\n1020:     : lineage.kind === 'native'\n1021:       ? [\n1022:           `This is an explicit native fan-out adapter running through the command host's OpenCode CLI surface.`,\n1023:           `Use the separate lineage directory and session id below as the detached state boundary.`,\n1024:           ``,\n1025:         ]\n1026:       : [];\n1027:   const hasIterationCap = typeof lineage.iterations === 'number' && lineage.iterations > 0;\n1028:   const stopPolicy = options.stopPolicy || 'convergence';\n1029:   const stopClause = hasIterationCap && stopPolicy === 'max-iterations'\n1030:     ? 'until config.maxIterations is reached; treat convergence before that as telemetry only and broaden review angles instead of synthesizing early'\n1031:     : hasIterationCap\n1032:       ? 'to legal convergence OR config.maxIterations, whichever comes first'\n1033:       : 'to legal convergence';\n1034:   const params = [\n1035:     `  spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n1036:     `  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: ${lineageDir}`,\n1037:     `  session_id: ${sessionId}`,\n1038:     `  executor: ${lineage.kind} model=${lineage.model || 'default'}`,\n1039:     `  loop_type: ${loopType}`,\n1040:     `  config.stopPolicy: ${stopPolicy}`,\n1041:   ];\n1042:   if (researchTopic) {\n1043:     // A research lineage's phase_init binds research_topic from this line. Without it a\n1044:     // fan-out research loop has no question to investigate and degrades to an empty topic.\n1045:     // Review loops scope by spec_folder and intentionally pass no topic.\n1046:     params.push(`  research_topic: ${researchTopic}`);\n1047:   }\n1048:   if (hasIterationCap) {\n1049:     params.push(`  config.maxIterations: ${lineage.iterations}`);\n1050:   }\n1051:   if (options.convergenceThreshold !== null && options.convergenceThreshold !== undefined) {\n1052:     params.push(`  config.convergenceThreshold: ${options.convergenceThreshold}`);\n1053:   }\n1054:   // Review lineages scope by spec_folder but the auto-workflow preflight\n1055:   // still requires the same review setup bindings the native command path pre-binds.\n1056:   // Without these, a detached CLI lineage can fail first-run initialization or infer a\n1057:   // different setup contract than native lineages.\n1058:   const setupBindings =\n1059:     loopType === 'review'\n1060:       ? [\n1061:           ``,\n1062:           `Review setup bindings (emit before any writes, same as native PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS):`,\n1063:           `review_target: ${specFolder}`,\n1064:           `review_target_type: spec-folder`,\n1065:           `review_dimensions: all`,\n1066:           `spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n1067:           `execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS`,\n1068:           `lineage_mode: auto`,\n1069:           ``,\n1070:         ]\n1071:       : [];\n1072:   return [\n1073:     `You are orchestrating the ${agentName} workflow YAML as a detached fan-out lineage.`,\n1074:     ...detachedIntro,\n1075:     ``,\n1076:     `Read ${skillFile} and execute the ${loopType} loop with these parameters:`,\n1077:     ...params,\n1078:     ...setupBindings,\n1079:     `The step_resolve_artifact_root step will bind artifact_dir to ${lineageDir} via the`,\n1080:     `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir override — do NOT run the resolveArtifactRoot node`,\n1081:     `command; bind artifact_dir directly to the override value.`,\n1082:     ``,\n1083:     `Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (${stopClause}), and phase_synthesis.`,\n1084:     `Write all outputs to ${lineageDir}. Do not touch any path outside ${lineageDir}.`,\n1085:     ``,\n1086:     `When complete, output a single line: FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:${lineage.label}`,\n1087:   ].join('\\n');\n1088: }\n1089: \n1090: function buildNativeCommandInput(loopType, specFolder, lineageDir, lineage, options = {}) {\n1091:   assertActiveFanoutLoopType(loopType);\n1092:   const maxIterations = lineage.iterations || 12;\n1093:   const convergenceThreshold = options.convergenceThreshold ?? (loopType === 'research' ? 0.05 : 0.1);\n1094:   const stopPolicy = options.stopPolicy || 'convergence';\n1095:   const sessionId = options.sessionId || '';\n1096:   const args = [\n1097:     ':auto',\n1098:     JSON.stringify(specFolder),\n1099:     `--spec-folder=${specFolder}`,\n1100:     `--max-iterations=${maxIterations}`,\n1101:     `--convergence=${convergenceThreshold}`,\n1102:     `--stop-policy=${stopPolicy}`,\n1103:     `--fanout-lineage-artifact-dir=${lineageDir}`,\n1104:     '--lineage-mode=auto',\n1105:   ];\n1106:   if (loopType === 'research' && options.researchTopic) {\n1107:     args.push(`--research-topic=${JSON.stringify(options.researchTopic)}`);\n1108:   }\n1109: \n1110:   return [\n1111:     args.join(' '),\n1112:     '',\n1113:     'PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:',\n1114:     `review_target: ${specFolder}`,\n1115:     'review_target_type: spec-folder',\n1116:     'review_dimensions: all',\n1117:     `spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n1118:     ...(sessionId ? [`session_id: ${sessionId}`] : []),\n1119:     'execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS',\n1120:     'lineage_mode: auto',\n1121:     `maxIterations: ${maxIterations}`,\n1122:     `convergenceThreshold: ${convergenceThreshold}`,\n1123:     `stop_policy: ${stopPolicy}`,\n1124:     `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: ${lineageDir}`,\n1125:   ].join('\\n');\n1126: }\n1127: \n1128: // Full-lineage lifetime is non-disableable in autonomous mode: 4 hours is the hard\n1129: // ceiling and a positive override may only narrow it, never widen past it.\n1130: const LINEAGE_LIFETIME_HARD_MAX_HOURS = 4;\n1131: \n1132: function assertLineageTimeoutHoursOverrideWithinCeiling(ceilingHoursOverride) {\n1133:   if (Number.isFinite(ceilingHoursOverride) && ceilingHoursOverride > LINEAGE_LIFETIME_HARD_MAX_HOURS) {\n1134:     throw inputError(\n1135:       `lineageTimeoutHours override (${ceilingHoursOverride}) exceeds the hard maximum of `\n1136:         + `${LINEAGE_LIFETIME_HARD_MAX_HOURS} hours`,\n1137:     );\n1138:   }\n1139: }\n1140: \n1141: /**\n1142:  * Compute a generous timeout for a full lineage loop run.\n1143:  * A single iteration is timeoutSeconds; a full loop is up to iterations * timeoutSeconds.\n1144:  * We double it for safety and cap at 4 hours. A caller-provided ceiling override may only\n1145:  * narrow this hard ceiling, never widen it — full-lineage lifetime is non-disableable.\n1146:  */\n1147: function computeLineageTimeoutMs(lineage, ceilingHoursOverride) {\n1148:   assertLineageTimeoutHoursOverrideWithinCeiling(ceilingHoursOverride);\n1149:   const iters = lineage.iterations || 12;\n\n(Showing lines 960-1149 of 2325. Use offset=1150 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"    loop_type: loopType,\n    spec_folder: specFolder,\n  });\n\n  return { didWait: true, migrated: loaded.migrated };\n}\n\nasync function persistPreDispatchWait({ checkpointPath, ledgerPath, runId, loopType, specFolder, waitMs }) {\n  const durationMs = normalizeWaitDurationMs(waitMs);\n  if (durationMs <= 0) {\n    return { didWait: false };\n  }\n\n  const checkpoint = buildWaitCheckpoint({ waitMs: durationMs, runId, loopType, specFolder });\n  atomicWriteJson(checkpointPath, checkpoint);\n  appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n    event: 'wait_checkpoint_persisted',\n    at: checkpoint.updatedAt,\n    run_id: runId,\n    loop_type: loopType,","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","text":"    loop_type: loopType,\n    spec_folder: specFolder,\n  });\n\n  return { didWait: true, migrated: loaded.migrated };\n}\n\nasync function persistPreDispatchWait({ checkpointPath, ledgerPath, runId, loopType, specFolder, waitMs }) {\n  const durationMs = normalizeWaitDurationMs(waitMs);\n  if (durationMs <= 0) {\n    return { didWait: false };\n  }\n\n  const checkpoint = buildWaitCheckpoint({ waitMs: durationMs, runId, loopType, specFolder });\n  atomicWriteJson(checkpointPath, checkpoint);\n  appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n    event: 'wait_checkpoint_persisted',\n    at: checkpoint.updatedAt,\n    run_id: runId,\n    loop_type: loopType,\n    spec_folder: specFolder,\n    nextRunAt: checkpoint.nextRunAt,\n    remainingDelayMs: checkpoint.remainingDelayMs,\n  });\n\n  await waitUntilCheckpointExpires({\n    checkpointPath,\n    checkpoint,\n    context: { runId, loopType, specFolder },\n  });\n\n  appendFanoutStatusLedger(ledgerPath, {\n    event: 'wait_checkpoint_cleared',\n    at: new Date().toISOString(),\n    run_id: runId,\n    loop_type: loopType,\n    spec_folder: specFolder,\n  });\n\n  return { didWait: true };\n}\n\n/**\n * Build the \"run the full loop\" prompt text for a CLI lineage subprocess.\n * The subprocess reads this, loads the skill, and runs the requested stop policy\n * with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir overriding step_resolve_artifact_root.\n */\nfunction buildLoopPrompt(loopType, specFolder, lineageDir, sessionId, lineage, researchTopic, options = {}) {\n  assertActiveFanoutLoopType(loopType);\n  const skillFile =\n    loopType === 'review'\n      ? '.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-review/SKILL.md'\n      : '.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md';\n  const agentName = loopType === 'review' ? 'deep-review' : 'deep-research';\n  const detachedIntro = lineage.kind === 'cli-opencode'\n    ? [\n        `This is an explicit parallel-detached OpenCode lineage, not a self-invocation of the parent session.`,\n        `Use the separate lineage directory and session id below as the detached state boundary.`,\n        ``,\n      ]\n    : lineage.kind === 'native'\n      ? [\n          `This is an explicit native fan-out adapter running through the command host's OpenCode CLI surface.`,\n          `Use the separate lineage directory and session id below as the detached state boundary.`,\n          ``,\n        ]\n      : [];\n  const hasIterationCap = typeof lineage.iterations === 'number' && lineage.iterations > 0;\n  const stopPolicy = options.stopPolicy || 'convergence';\n  const stopClause = hasIterationCap && stopPolicy === 'max-iterations'\n    ? 'until config.maxIterations is reached; treat convergence before that as telemetry only and broaden review angles instead of synthesizing early'\n    : hasIterationCap\n      ? 'to legal convergence OR config.maxIterations, whichever comes first'\n      : 'to legal convergence';\n  const params = [\n    `  spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n    `  config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: ${lineageDir}`,\n    `  session_id: ${sessionId}`,\n    `  executor: ${lineage.kind} model=${lineage.model || 'default'}`,\n    `  loop_type: ${loopType}`,\n    `  config.stopPolicy: ${stopPolicy}`,\n  ];\n  if (researchTopic) {\n    // A research lineage's phase_init binds research_topic from this line. Without it a\n    // fan-out research loop has no question to investigate and degrades to an empty topic.\n    // Review loops scope by spec_folder and intentionally pass no topic.\n    params.push(`  research_topic: ${researchTopic}`);\n  }\n  if (hasIterationCap) {\n    params.push(`  config.maxIterations: ${lineage.iterations}`);\n  }\n  if (options.convergenceThreshold !== null && options.convergenceThreshold !== undefined) {\n    params.push(`  config.convergenceThreshold: ${options.convergenceThreshold}`);\n  }\n  // Review lineages scope by spec_folder but the auto-workflow preflight\n  // still requires the same review setup bindings the native command path pre-binds.\n  // Without these, a detached CLI lineage can fail first-run initialization or infer a\n  // different setup contract than native lineages.\n  const setupBindings =\n    loopType === 'review'\n      ? [\n          ``,\n          `Review setup bindings (emit before any writes, same as native PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS):`,\n          `review_target: ${specFolder}`,\n          `review_target_type: spec-folder`,\n          `review_dimensions: all`,\n          `spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n          `execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS`,\n          `lineage_mode: auto`,\n          ``,\n        ]\n      : [];\n  return [\n    `You are orchestrating the ${agentName} workflow YAML as a detached fan-out lineage.`,\n    ...detachedIntro,\n    ``,\n    `Read ${skillFile} and execute the ${loopType} loop with these parameters:`,\n    ...params,\n    ...setupBindings,\n    `The step_resolve_artifact_root step will bind artifact_dir to ${lineageDir} via the`,\n    `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir override — do NOT run the resolveArtifactRoot node`,\n    `command; bind artifact_dir directly to the override value.`,\n    ``,\n    `Run phase_init, phase_main_loop (${stopClause}), and phase_synthesis.`,\n    `Write all outputs to ${lineageDir}. Do not touch any path outside ${lineageDir}.`,\n    ``,\n    `When complete, output a single line: FANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:${lineage.label}`,\n  ].join('\\n');\n}\n\nfunction buildNativeCommandInput(loopType, specFolder, lineageDir, lineage, options = {}) {\n  assertActiveFanoutLoopType(loopType);\n  const maxIterations = lineage.iterations || 12;\n  const convergenceThreshold = options.convergenceThreshold ?? (loopType === 'research' ? 0.05 : 0.1);\n  const stopPolicy = options.stopPolicy || 'convergence';\n  const sessionId = options.sessionId || '';\n  const args = [\n    ':auto',\n    JSON.stringify(specFolder),\n    `--spec-folder=${specFolder}`,\n    `--max-iterations=${maxIterations}`,\n    `--convergence=${convergenceThreshold}`,\n    `--stop-policy=${stopPolicy}`,\n    `--fanout-lineage-artifact-dir=${lineageDir}`,\n    '--lineage-mode=auto',\n  ];\n  if (loopType === 'research' && options.researchTopic) {\n    args.push(`--research-topic=${JSON.stringify(options.researchTopic)}`);\n  }\n\n  return [\n    args.join(' '),\n    '',\n    'PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:',\n    `review_target: ${specFolder}`,\n    'review_target_type: spec-folder',\n    'review_dimensions: all',\n    `spec_folder: ${specFolder}`,\n    ...(sessionId ? [`session_id: ${sessionId}`] : []),\n    'execution_mode: AUTONOMOUS',\n    'lineage_mode: auto',\n    `maxIterations: ${maxIterations}`,\n    `convergenceThreshold: ${convergenceThreshold}`,\n    `stop_policy: ${stopPolicy}`,\n    `config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir: ${lineageDir}`,\n  ].join('\\n');\n}\n\n// Full-lineage lifetime is non-disableable in autonomous mode: 4 hours is the hard\n// ceiling and a positive override may only narrow it, never widen past it.\nconst LINEAGE_LIFETIME_HARD_MAX_HOURS = 4;\n\nfunction assertLineageTimeoutHoursOverrideWithinCeiling(ceilingHoursOverride) {\n  if (Number.isFinite(ceilingHoursOverride) && ceilingHoursOverride > LINEAGE_LIFETIME_HARD_MAX_HOURS) {\n    throw inputError(\n      `lineageTimeoutHours override (${ceilingHoursOverride}) exceeds the hard maximum of `\n        + `${LINEAGE_LIFETIME_HARD_MAX_HOURS} hours`,\n    );\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Compute a generous timeout for a full lineage loop run.\n * A single iteration is timeoutSeconds; a full loop is up to iterations * timeoutSeconds.\n * We double it for safety and cap at 4 hours. A caller-provided ceiling override may only\n * narrow this hard ceiling, never widen it — full-lineage lifetime is non-disableable.\n */\nfunction computeLineageTimeoutMs(lineage, ceilingHoursOverride) {\n  assertLineageTimeoutHoursOverrideWithinCeiling(ceilingHoursOverride);\n  const iters = lineage.iterations || 12;","lineStart":960,"lineEnd":1149,"totalLines":2325,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs","time":{"start":1785133727970,"end":1785133727977}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e158554e4c12008016a66fa9fd7b88191891301af7483666f"}},"id":"prt_fa24300ac001slJ5RsFWNSUabK","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242d1f7001m3St348OtWWs65"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133728318,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_e14HVsr0CH3H7FQuW6QyixqL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/research.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Mobbin MCP transport packet research\n2: \n3: Research topic: the official Mobbin MCP server and official Mobbin skills needed to author a read-only, Code Mode-only `mcp-mobbin` transport under `mcp-tooling`, register a `mobbin` manual in `.utcp_config.json`, and pair retrieved evidence with `sk-design` judgment.\n4: \n5: Evidence labels used below:\n6: \n7: - **Confirmed** — current official documentation/source, a verified local contract, or a direct unauthenticated observation.\n8: - **Inferred** — strongly supported but not exercised through authenticated Code Mode.\n9: - **Unknown** — requires a paid authenticated runtime or unpublished provider policy.\n10: \n11: ## 1. Executive Summary\n12: \n13: Author `mcp-mobbin` as a non-mutating evidence transport: `packetKind: \"transport\"`, `mutatesWorkspace: false`, Code Mode calls only, no Write/Edit/Task, and mandatory cross-hub pairing with `sk-design` whenever Mobbin evidence informs a design decision. The transport retrieves real-world design evidence; it never decides taste, accessibility, responsiveness, or readiness. [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:79] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263]\n14: \n15: The official server is hosted at `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` over Streamable HTTP. It uses browser OAuth, not a Mobbin API key. Public metadata and official docs confirm OAuth protected-resource discovery, Dynamic Client Registration, authorization-code flow, PKCE S256, access/refresh tokens, and `openid`. The official server repository contains registration/docs artifacts rather than a local runtime package. [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp]\n16: \n17: The complete public documented tool baseline at 2026-07-16 is one read tool: `search_screens`. Its official skill-level contract accepts a natural-language query, `ios` or `web`, and a conservative result limit; it returns ordered screen metadata plus inline images. App, screen, flow, and element research are search/analysis intents over those screen results, not four published MCP tool families. Authenticated `tools/list` completeness and the exact server JSON Schema remain runtime UNKNOWNs and must be captured during validation. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n18: \n19: Register a Code Mode manual named `mobbin` that launches `npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` with an empty environment. This adapts Code Mode's current stdio manual shape to Mobbin's remote HTTP/OAuth service. No API key, token, or client secret belongs in `.utcp_config.json` or `.env`. [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:468] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n20: \n21: MCP is unavailable on Free and included on Pro, Team, and Enterprise. The separately documented REST API is Team/Enterprise only and uses a workspace API key; it is not the MCP credential or transport. MCP is rate-limited to 60 requests per 60 seconds per user. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits]\n22: \n23: ## 2. Scope, Method, and Evidence Boundary\n24: \n25: Five evidence iterations were run because `stopPolicy: max-iterations` made early convergence telemetry non-terminal:\n26: \n27: 1. Hosted server, transport, authorization, and install baseline.\n28: 2. Official skill surface and app/screen/flow/element workflows.\n29: 3. Free/paid eligibility, MCP/API separation, and rate limits.\n30: 4. Local Code Mode manual, packet architecture, and `sk-design` pairing.\n31: 5. Live public protocol metadata, repository freshness, contradiction review, and terminal acceptance gates.\n32: \n33: Evidence was restricted to official Mobbin repositories/docs/endpoints, the `mcp-remote` maintainer repository, direct unauthenticated read-only protocol probes, and local integration contracts. No Mobbin login, paid authorization, token exchange, MCP tool call, OAuth-cache read/write, or remote mutation occurred. The 401/protected-resource checks prove endpoint/auth shape but cannot enumerate authenticated tools. [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n34: \n35: Freshness snapshot: the official server repository's latest observed commit was `bbee2a6be34d251c580ba80bb8b407c87587aba7` dated 2026-06-03; the skills repository's latest observed commit was `9657786338c5e7fed597031982398a8d99681fec` dated 2026-05-04, and `skills/` contained only `mobbin-search`. [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/commits?per_page=1] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/commits?per_page=1] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n36: \n37: ## 3. Server, Transport, Install, and Runtime\n38: \n39: | Concern | Confirmed contract | Packet implication |\n40: |---|---|---|\n41: | Server URL | `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` | Single remote endpoint |\n42: | Provider transport | Streamable HTTP | Do not describe Mobbin itself as stdio |\n43: | Local adapter | `mcp-remote` launched over stdio | Lets current Code Mode consume remote HTTP/OAuth |\n44: | Provider install | None | Do not clone/build/install a Mobbin server |\n45: | Adapter install | On-demand through `npx -y` | Avoid interactive package confirmation |\n46: | Runtime | Node.js 18+ and working `npx` | Doctor checks both before OAuth |\n47: | Network | Outbound HTTPS plus localhost OAuth callback | Headless sessions need operator-visible escalation |\n48: | Account | Pro, Team, or Enterprise | Free is not a reduced MCP mode |\n49: \n50: [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n51: \n52: `mcp-remote` defaults to HTTP-first and falls back to SSE only on an HTTP 404. Mobbin explicitly requires Streamable HTTP, so no forced SSE flag is needed. The adapter describes itself as experimental and is externally versioned; static compatibility does not equal a completed local OAuth/discovery run. [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote#transport-strategies] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other]\n53: \n54: ## 4. Authentication, Credential Storage, and Security\n55: \n56: Mobbin's official client flow requires no API key or manually copied token. On first use, the client opens a browser, the user signs in and authorizes access, and the client receives OAuth access/refresh tokens. Custom integrations use DCR and authorization code with PKCE S256. Client access is revocable. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect]\n57: \n58: A live unauthenticated request returned HTTP 401 and:\n59: \n60: ```text\n61: WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata=\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"\n62: {\"error\":{\"code\":\"unauthorized\",\"message\":\"Missing or invalid Authorization header\"}}\n63: ```\n64: \n65: The protected-resource document names resource `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp`, the Supabase authorization server, and `openid`. Authorization-server metadata publishes authorization, token, and registration endpoints plus PKCE S256. This matches the written integration contract. [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp] [SOURCE: https://ujasntkfphywizsdaapi.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server]\n66: \n67: Security rules for the packet:\n68: \n69: - Keep manual `env` empty; never add `MOBBIN_API_KEY`, the REST workspace key, access/refresh tokens, or a client secret.\n70: - Never accept credentials in prompts or tool arguments.\n71: - Never print Authorization headers, OAuth codes, token responses, adapter debug logs, or auth-cache contents.\n72: - Treat adapter auth state as operator-owned. Do not clear it automatically; reauthorization is an explicit operator action.\n73: - Use PKCE S256 even though live authorization metadata also advertises `plain`.\n74: - Interpret a pre-authorization 401 as the expected protected-resource challenge after reachability is proven, not as evidence that a static key is missing.\n75: \n76: [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration]\n77: \n78: ## 5. Official MCP Tool Surface\n79: \n80: ### Public documented baseline\n81: \n82: | Tool | Posture | Skill-level inputs | Skill-level result |\n83: |---|---|---|---|\n84: | `search_screens` | Read/search | `query`: natural language; `platform`: `ios` or `web`; `limit`: default 5, normally no more than about 15 when broader variety is requested | `screens[]` metadata, `failed[]`, then ordered inline image blocks |\n85: \n86: The official skill describes screen metadata as:\n87: \n88: ```text\n89: screens: [{ index, id, app_name, mobbin_url, image_url, platform }]\n90: failed:  []\n91: ```\n92: \n93: Inline images arrive in the same response after metadata, so the workflow can analyze visible screens without inventing a second image-download tool. Preserve metadata/image order and report partial image failures. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md]\n94: \n95: ### Completeness boundary\n96: \n97: The official `skills/` tree contains one skill, `mobbin-search`, and its instructions name only `search_screens`. The official server repository publishes endpoint/registration artifacts but no public server implementation or authenticated `tools/list` export. Therefore:\n98: \n99: - **Confirmed:** `search_screens` is the only public documented tool.\n100: - **Unknown:** whether authenticated `tools/list` currently contains only that tool.\n101: - **Unknown:** the exact MCP JSON Schema and callable name produced by current Code Mode.\n102: - **Not allowed:** inventing `search_apps`, `search_flows`, `search_elements`, detail, image, or mutation tools.\n103: \n104: [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills] [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp]\n105: \n106: The packet's read-only guarantee is an authorization boundary, not an unsupported universal claim about every future provider tool. Allow only verified read/search tools. If live discovery returns a mutation-capable tool, refuse it and require an explicit reviewed contract change.\n107: \n108: ## 6. Result Handling and Context Discipline\n109: \n110: Use conservative retrieval:\n111: \n112: 1. Clarify the product/surface, research intent, and required platform.\n113: 2. Start with `limit: 5`.\n114: 3. Inspect ordered metadata and images together.\n115: 4. Ask the user before widening materially; do not jump above about 15 merely to create variety.\n116: 5. Report `failed[]` and missing images as partial success, never silently discard them.\n117: 6. Retain `mobbin_url` as provenance for every selected reference.\n118: \n119: The provider skill's visual-analysis sequence is: observe content/structure/styling/interaction cues; compare repeated patterns and meaningful differences; synthesize principles; and answer with evidence tied to the returned screens. The transport may describe observable facts, but any design recommendation or acceptance conclusion belongs to `sk-design`. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:176]\n120: \n121: Do not create the upstream skill's optional HTML evidence board inside `mcp-mobbin`. The requested packet is non-mutating. Artifact authoring can occur only in a separate explicitly authorized workflow outside this transport.\n122: \n123: ## 7. App, Screen, Flow, and Element Research Workflows\n124: \n125: There are not four documented MCP tool families. Use one retrieval surface with intent-specific query design:\n126: \n127: ### App research\n128: \n129: Name the app/company/category and the comparison goal: for example, “banking apps onboarding identity verification.” Compare returned `app_name`, platform, screen structure, and visible patterns. Multiple results are evidence, not a design chooser.\n130: \n131: ### Screen research\n132: \n133: Use the concrete screen/state/job: “iOS subscription cancellation confirmation,” “web empty-state dashboard,” or “mobile checkout payment error.” Start at five results and cite each Mobbin URL used.\n134: \n135: ### Flow research\n136: \n137: Describe the user journey and target step: “first-run onboarding progression,” “card replacement flow,” or “forgot-password recovery.” The current public contract returns screens, not a first-class ordered flow object, so reconstruct sequence only when visual evidence supports it and label reconstruction as inference.\n138: \n139: ### Element research\n140: \n141: Name the component plus context/state: “bottom-sheet destructive confirmation,” “segmented control in analytics,” or “inline validation on signup.” Analyze how the element behaves within returned screens. Do not fabricate an element-detail tool or claim isolated component metadata.\n142: \n143: For all four intents, use deep semantic queries for complex requests, keep platform explicit, and perform grounded visual comparison only after results arrive. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md]\n144: \n145: ## 8. Plans, MCP/API Separation, and Rate Limits\n146: \n147: | Surface | Free | Pro | Team | Enterprise | Credential |\n148: |---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n149: | Mobbin website | Limited browsing | Full paid features | Included | Included | User session |\n150: | Mobbin MCP | No | Yes | Yes | Yes | Browser OAuth |\n151: | Mobbin REST API | No | No | Yes | Yes | Workspace API key |\n152: \n153: [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/pricing] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart]\n154: \n155: Do not conflate the Team/Enterprise REST API's Bearer API key or `POST /v1/screens/search` with MCP. No reviewed source documents different MCP tool sets for Pro versus Team versus Enterprise, so the stable packet should not invent per-tool tier gates. Exact Free-account MCP denial behavior is UNKNOWN: authorization might fail at different stages, and public docs do not publish its precise status/payload. Finance+ is a separate paid add-on, but public sources do not establish its MCP result coverage. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/pricing]\n156: \n157: MCP limit: 60 requests per 60 seconds per user. A 429 includes `Retry-After`; honor it, then use exponential backoff with jitter for continuing failures. Metadata-first, small-limit queries also reduce rate and context pressure. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits]\n158: \n159: ## 9. Code Mode Manual and Calling Convention\n160: \n161: Phase 002 should ship this paste-ready manual; phase 003 should add it to `manual_call_templates[]`:\n162: \n163: ```json\n164: {\n165:   \"name\": \"mobbin\",\n166:   \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n167:   \"config\": {\n168:     \"mcpServers\": {\n169:       \"mobbin\": {\n170:         \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n171:         \"command\": \"npx\",\n172:         \"args\": [\n173:           \"-y\",\n174:           \"mcp-remote\",\n175:           \"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\"\n176:         ],\n177:         \"env\": {}\n178:       }\n179:     }\n180:   }\n181: }\n182: ```\n183: \n184: [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:162] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other]\n185: \n186: The mandatory runtime sequence is:\n187: \n188: 1. `list_tools()` or `search_tools({ task_description: \"Mobbin screen design research\", limit: 10 })`.\n189: 2. Filter to the `mobbin` manual.\n190: 3. Run `tool_info()` on the exact dotted discovery name.\n191: 4. Only then call through `call_tool_chain({ code })` with the callable syntax `tool_info()` reports.\n192: \n193: Code Mode's general convention predicts dotted discovery `mobbin.mobbin.search_screens` and callable `mobbin.mobbin_search_screens(...)`, but both are **INFERRED** until live discovery. The skill-level argument example below is illustrative until `tool_info()` confirms its schema:\n194: \n195: ```typescript\n196: call_tool_chain({\n197:   code: `\n198:     const result = await mobbin.mobbin_search_screens({\n199:       query: \"iOS banking app onboarding identity verification\",\n200:       platform: \"ios\",\n201:       limit: 5\n202:     });\n203:     return { success: true, data: result, errors: [], timestamp: new Date().toISOString() };\n204:   `\n205: });\n206: ```\n207: \n208: [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md:252] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md:365]\n209: \n210: ## 10. `mcp-mobbin` Packet Architecture and `sk-design` Pairing\n211: \n212: Recommended skill permission surface:\n213: \n214: ```text\n215: Read, Glob, Grep,\n216: mcp__code_mode__list_tools,\n217: mcp__code_mode__search_tools,\n218: mcp__code_mode__tool_info,\n219: mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain\n220: ```\n221: \n222: Do not grant Write, Edit, Task, or a direct Mobbin MCP tool. The remote call path is Code Mode only. Shell-based doctor/install scripts may be shipped as user-invoked assets if phase standards require them, but the transport skill itself does not need Bash to query Mobbin.\n223: \n224: Registry/hub contract:\n225: \n226: - `workflowMode: \"mcp-mobbin\"`\n227: - `packetKind: \"transport\"`\n228: - `backendKind`: a Mobbin Code Mode transport discriminator chosen consistently across registry/docs\n229: - `routingClass: \"metadata\"`\n230: - `toolPolicy.mutatesWorkspace: false`\n231: - `extensions.transport-axis.transports[]` contains `mcp-mobbin`\n232: - `crossHubPairing: mcp-mobbin -> sk-design`\n233: \n234: [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md:79]\n235: \n236: Pairing lifecycle for design-affecting research:\n237: \n238: 1. `sk-design` gathers goal, surface, inputs, constraints, and proof expectations.\n239: 2. It selects the smallest design-judgment mode (interface, foundations, motion, or audit).\n240: 3. `mcp-mobbin` retrieves cited screens through Code Mode.\n241: 4. Results return to the selected judgment mode.\n242: 5. `sk-design`, not transport rank or images alone, owns taste, accessibility, responsive, and ready decisions.\n243: \n244: Pure setup/doctor or factual tool-surface reporting does not make a design verdict, but the registry still declares the pairing. [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:20] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:172] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263]\n245: \n246: ## 11. Recommendations\n247: \n248: 1. Treat `search_screens` as the only stable documented tool and make live discovery the runtime authority.\n249: 2. Fail closed on missing, renamed, expanded, or mutation-capable tool surfaces; do not silently widen permissions.\n250: 3. Register exactly one `mobbin` manual using the stdio `mcp-remote` bridge and empty environment.\n251: 4. Document Node 18+, `npx`, outbound HTTPS, browser/localhost OAuth, and paid account prerequisites.\n252: 5. Put no Mobbin credential in `.env`; keep auth state operator-owned and outside packet logic.\n253: 6. Separate website, OAuth MCP, and API-key REST entitlements everywhere.\n254: 7. Route app/flow/element intents through semantic screen searches; never manufacture separate tools or structured flow semantics.\n255: 8. Keep limits small, preserve result/image ordering and failures, cite `mobbin_url`, and honor 429 `Retry-After`.\n256: 9. Make `mcp-mobbin` transport owner and `sk-design` judgment owner; transport output is evidence, not acceptance.\n257: 10. Split deterministic packet/hub tests from operator-authorized paid OAuth smoke tests.\n258: \n259: ## Eliminated Alternatives\n260: \n261: | Alternative | Reason eliminated | Evidence | Iteration |\n262: |---|---|---|---:|\n263: | Static `MOBBIN_API_KEY` for MCP | MCP uses browser OAuth; no manual key setup | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] | 1 |\n264: | Reuse the REST workspace key | REST and MCP are separate surfaces and plans | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] | 3 |\n265: | Clone/install a local Mobbin server | Official repository declares a hosted remote and has no runtime package | [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] | 1 |\n266: | Describe Mobbin itself as stdio | Stdio belongs to the local adapter; provider transport is HTTP | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other] | 4 |\n267: | Direct unproven Code Mode HTTP manual | Current local precedent uses stdio plus `mcp-remote` for hosted OAuth | [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] | 4 |\n268: | Separate app/flow/element/detail/image tools | Current official skill names only `search_screens` | [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] | 2 |\n269: | Free as a limited MCP tier | MCP begins at Pro; Free browsing is a different product surface | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] | 3 |\n270: | Per-tool Pro/Team/Enterprise claims | No reviewed source documents paid-tier tool differences | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] | 3 |\n271: | HTML evidence-board creation in transport | Violates non-mutating packet boundary | [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:81] | 2 |\n272: | Guess `mobbin.mobbin_search_screens` | Code Mode requires discovery and `tool_info()` | [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md:256] | 4 |\n273: | Treat public catalog as authenticated `tools/list` | Protected endpoint prevents public enumeration | [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp] | 5 |\n274: | Treat transport results as taste authority | `sk-design` owns judgment and acceptance | [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263] | 4 |\n275: | Auto-clear adapter auth state | Destructive to operator-owned sessions | [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote#troubleshooting] | 5 |\n276: \n277: ## Divergence Map\n278: \n279: | Direction | Status | Evidence resolution | Remaining frontier |\n280: |---|---|---|---|\n281: | API key vs OAuth | Saturated | Docs plus live protected-resource metadata agree on OAuth/DCR/PKCE | Paid local round trip only |\n282: | Local package vs hosted server | Saturated | Official manifests/tree contain registration assets, no runtime | None for architecture |\n283: | One tool vs app/flow/element families | Saturated for public contract | Official skill tree contains one skill naming `search_screens` | Authenticated live list drift |\n284: | Free vs paid | Saturated for eligibility | Free excluded; Pro/Team/Enterprise included | Exact Free denial payload |\n285: | MCP vs REST API | Saturated | OAuth MCP versus Team/Enterprise workspace-key REST | None for manual design |\n286: | Direct HTTP vs stdio bridge | Resolved by local precedent | Current Code Mode remote examples and `refero` manual use `mcp-remote` | End-to-end local OAuth/refresh |\n287: | Transport vs judgment authority | Saturated | Phase specs and `sk-design` require non-mutating transport/pairing | Downstream graph and playbook proof |\n288: | Finance+ coverage | Public sources exhausted | Pricing documents add-on but not MCP inclusion | Provider/paid runtime evidence |\n289: \n290: No formal divergent-mode pivot or Council artifact was produced. Breadth came from successive evidence angles: provider metadata, official skill behavior, entitlements, local integration contracts, and adversarial live public probes. The remaining frontier is operator-authorized runtime validation, not additional unauthenticated searching.\n291: \n292: ## 12. Open Questions\n293: \n294: No open question blocks phase-002 packet authorship. Preserve these as explicit downstream UNKNOWNs:\n295: \n296: 1. What exact names and JSON Schemas do authenticated Code Mode `list_tools()` and `tool_info()` expose on the validation date?\n297: 2. Does the current local Code Mode + `mcp-remote` version complete first-use Mobbin OAuth, refresh, and reconnect reliably?\n298: 3. What precise status/payload/UX does a Free account receive during MCP authorization or tool use?\n299: 4. Does Finance+ change the dataset returned through standard MCP search?\n300: \n301: ## 13. Verification Plan\n302: \n303: ### Deterministic no-account checks\n304: \n305: - JSON-parse the ready-to-paste manual and confirm one name-keyed `mobbin` entry.\n306: - Assert endpoint, `npx -y mcp-remote`, stdio adapter, and empty `env` exactly.\n307: - Assert no `MOBBIN_API_KEY`, REST key, token, secret, Authorization header, or `.env` requirement appears.\n308: - Assert packet frontmatter/registry forbid Write/Edit/Task and declare `mutatesWorkspace:false`.\n309: - Assert only Code Mode discovery/execution meta-tools are allowed for remote calls.\n310: - Fixture the public `search_screens` query/platform/limit and ordered metadata/failed/images contract, labeled skill-level rather than live schema.\n311: - Negative fixtures reject invented app/flow/element/detail/image/mutation tools and pre-discovery callable guesses.\n312: - Routing holdouts distinguish Mobbin evidence search from Figma transport, browser inspection, generic `sk-design`, and unrelated MCP setup.\n313: - Verify hub registry/router/description/graph metadata, transport list, pairing edge, and manual name remain synchronized.\n314: - Verify every design-affecting scenario returns evidence to `sk-design` before acceptance.\n315: \n316: ### Operator-authorized paid live checks\n317: \n318: 1. Confirm Node/npx and load the new manual; restart Code Mode.\n319: 2. Observe the expected 401/protected-resource challenge before authorization without treating it as key failure.\n320: 3. Complete browser OAuth with an eligible account; capture no tokens/log secrets.\n321: 4. Run `list_tools()`, filter `mobbin`, and record exact dated dotted names.\n322: 5. Run `tool_info()` for every exposed tool and compare the read-only allow-boundary.\n323: 6. Execute one minimal `search_screens` call with `limit: 1`; verify query/platform schema, metadata, image order, and Mobbin URL.\n324: 7. Run app-, flow-, and element-intent queries and confirm they remain screen-search workflows rather than fabricated tool families.\n325: 8. Verify partial image failures remain visible.\n326: 9. If safely observable, validate 429/`Retry-After` behavior without deliberately exhausting service quotas.\n327: 10. Record unexpected tools/schema drift as a fail-closed packet update requirement.\n328: \n329: Paid/OAuth scenarios should allow `SKIP` with the missing entitlement/operator authorization stated.\n330: \n331: ## 14. Troubleshooting, Risks, and Mitigations\n332: \n333: | Symptom/risk | Interpretation | Safe action |\n334: |---|---|---|\n335: | Endpoint returns 401 before auth | Expected protected-resource challenge | Complete browser OAuth; do not add an API key |\n336: | Browser does not open/callback fails | Headless session, port, timeout, or client problem | Move to interactive session or request operator action; never ask for token paste |\n337: | No `mobbin.*` tools | Manual load/start/auth/plan failure | Validate JSON, name, Node/npx, restart, OAuth, then eligibility |\n338: | Tool name/schema mismatch | Provider/adapter drift | Re-run `list_tools` + `tool_info`; fail closed and update reviewed docs |\n339: | 429 | Per-user request window exceeded | Honor `Retry-After`; exponential backoff with jitter; reduce query volume |\n340: | Free account cannot connect/use tools | Expected entitlement boundary | Explain MCP starts at Pro; do not guess precise failure semantics |\n341: | Token refresh/stale state | Operator-owned adapter auth state | Use diagnostics without printing secrets; clear only with explicit reauthorization consent |\n342: | Unexpected mutation tool | Provider surface expanded | Refuse; read-only packet requires explicit contract review |\n343: | Large image/result response | Context pressure | Default five; preserve/compare metadata first; widen only deliberately |\n344: | Individual images fail | Partial provider/storage failure | Preserve `failed[]`, return usable results plus errors |\n345: | Unpinned experimental adapter changes | Compatibility drift | Smoke-test after dependency change; consider pinning only in a separately reviewed change |\n346: | Design copied or generic | Transport mistaken for authority | Cite evidence; use `sk-design` critique/judgment; never copy wholesale |\n347: \n348: [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:642]\n349: \n350: ## 15. Phase 002–003 Authoring Checklist\n351: \n352: Phase 002 creates `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-mobbin/` only:\n353: \n354: - `SKILL.md` — transport identity, Code Mode-only permissions, discovery gate, read-only rules, pairing boundary.\n355: - `README.md` — user-facing purpose, prerequisites, public surface, plan/auth caveats.\n356: - `INSTALL_GUIDE.md` — Node/npx, manual snippet, first-use OAuth, discovery verification; no provider server install.\n357: - `assets/` — paste-ready `mobbin` UTCP manual with empty env; no secret template.\n358: - `references/mcp-wiring.md` — remote HTTP versus local stdio adapter, discovery/call naming, confirmed/inferred labels.\n359: - `references/tool-surface.md` — single public documented baseline, response shape, authenticated-live UNKNOWNs.\n360: - `references/workflows.md` or equivalent — app/screen/flow/element semantic query recipes and grounded analysis.\n361: - `references/troubleshooting.md` — 401, OAuth callback, manual discovery, plan, 429, drift, partial images.\n362: - `feature_catalog/` — capability inventory marked read-only.\n363: - `scripts/` — non-mutating doctor/snippet helpers that print no auth state.\n364: - `manual_testing_playbook/` — positive routing, at least two holdouts, negative/troubleshoot, deterministic and paid-live splits.\n365: - `mcp-servers/mobbin-mcp/README.md` — explicitly document hosted provider server and absence of local package source.\n366: - `changelog/` and package metadata required by the skill-authoring standard.\n367: - Run `package_skill.py --check` (and strict gate in phase 004) with every tool claim traced here.\n368: \n369: Phase 003 owns shared integration after sibling serial dependencies:\n370: \n371: - add `mcp-mobbin` to `mode-registry.json` as transport/metadata/non-mutating;\n372: - add transport-axis membership and `mcp-mobbin -> sk-design` cross-hub pairing;\n373: - add narrow router signals for Mobbin/app-screen-flow-element design-reference research plus holdouts;\n374: - update parent SKILL/README/description/graph metadata and hub changelog/playbook;\n375: - paste the `mobbin` manual into `.utcp_config.json` once;\n376: - regenerate the advisor skill graph and sweep all references for key/name/count consistency.\n377: \n378: [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:70] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md:68]\n379: \n380: ## 16. References\n381: \n382: Primary Mobbin sources:\n383: \n384: - [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server]\n385: - [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/mcp.json]\n386: - [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/server.json]\n387: - [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/skills]\n388: - [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md]\n389: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction]\n390: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other]\n391: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration]\n392: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect]\n393: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview]\n394: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart]\n395: - [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits]\n396: - [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/mcp]\n397: - [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/pricing]\n398: - [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp]\n399: - [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp]\n400: - [SOURCE: https://ujasntkfphywizsdaapi.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server]\n401: - [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/commits?per_page=1]\n402: - [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n403: - [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/commits?per_page=1]\n404: \n405: Transport and local sources:\n406: \n407: - [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n408: - [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147]\n409: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md]\n410: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md]\n411: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/naming_convention.md]\n412: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/SKILL.md]\n413: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/mcp-wiring.md]\n414: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md]\n415: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md]\n416: - [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md]\n417: \n418: ## 17. Convergence Report\n419: \n420: - Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`.\n421: - Total iterations: 5.\n422: - Questions answered: 5 / 5 to the public/static evidence boundary.\n423: - Remaining authoring-blocking questions: 0.\n424: - Runtime/provider UNKNOWNs retained: 4 (authenticated schema, local OAuth/refresh, exact Free denial, Finance+ coverage).\n425: - Last three iterations: run 3 — plan gating/API separation/rate limits (0.88); run 4 — Code Mode manual/packet architecture (0.82); run 5 — adversarial completeness/risk audit (0.58).\n426: - New-information ratios: 1.00, 0.93, 0.88, 0.82, 0.58.\n427: - Last-three rolling average: 0.76, above threshold 0.05.\n428: - MAD noise floor: 0.089; latest ratio 0.58 remained above it.\n429: - Question coverage: 1.00; composite stop telemetry did not supersede the configured hard-cap reason.\n430: - Stop-policy interpretation: all five required iterations ran; early convergence was telemetry only and review broadened through product, workflow, entitlement, local architecture, and adversarial protocol angles.\n431: - Divergence summary: no formal pivot/Council artifacts; public tool enumeration, static auth/install, entitlement, and packet placement were saturated. Paid runtime validation is the remaining frontier.\n432: - Confidence: high for the published endpoint/auth/plan/rate/public-tool/local architecture contract; medium for adapter compatibility; unknown for authenticated live schema and paid-runtime behavior.\n\n(End of file - total 432 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Mobbin MCP transport packet research\n\nResearch topic: the official Mobbin MCP server and official Mobbin skills needed to author a read-only, Code Mode-only `mcp-mobbin` transport under `mcp-tooling`, register a `mobbin` manual in `.utcp_config.json`, and pair retrieved evidence with `sk-design` judgment.\n\nEvidence labels used below:\n\n- **Confirmed** — current official documentation/source, a verified local contract, or a direct unauthenticated observation.\n- **Inferred** — strongly supported but not exercised through authenticated Code Mode.\n- **Unknown** — requires a paid authenticated runtime or unpublished provider policy.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nAuthor `mcp-mobbin` as a non-mutating evidence transport: `packetKind: \"transport\"`, `mutatesWorkspace: false`, Code Mode calls only, no Write/Edit/Task, and mandatory cross-hub pairing with `sk-design` whenever Mobbin evidence informs a design decision. The transport retrieves real-world design evidence; it never decides taste, accessibility, responsiveness, or readiness. [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:79] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263]\n\nThe official server is hosted at `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` over Streamable HTTP. It uses browser OAuth, not a Mobbin API key. Public metadata and official docs confirm OAuth protected-resource discovery, Dynamic Client Registration, authorization-code flow, PKCE S256, access/refresh tokens, and `openid`. The official server repository contains registration/docs artifacts rather than a local runtime package. [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp]\n\nThe complete public documented tool baseline at 2026-07-16 is one read tool: `search_screens`. Its official skill-level contract accepts a natural-language query, `ios` or `web`, and a conservative result limit; it returns ordered screen metadata plus inline images. App, screen, flow, and element research are search/analysis intents over those screen results, not four published MCP tool families. Authenticated `tools/list` completeness and the exact server JSON Schema remain runtime UNKNOWNs and must be captured during validation. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n\nRegister a Code Mode manual named `mobbin` that launches `npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` with an empty environment. This adapts Code Mode's current stdio manual shape to Mobbin's remote HTTP/OAuth service. No API key, token, or client secret belongs in `.utcp_config.json` or `.env`. [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:468] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/research.md","text":"# Mobbin MCP transport packet research\n\nResearch topic: the official Mobbin MCP server and official Mobbin skills needed to author a read-only, Code Mode-only `mcp-mobbin` transport under `mcp-tooling`, register a `mobbin` manual in `.utcp_config.json`, and pair retrieved evidence with `sk-design` judgment.\n\nEvidence labels used below:\n\n- **Confirmed** — current official documentation/source, a verified local contract, or a direct unauthenticated observation.\n- **Inferred** — strongly supported but not exercised through authenticated Code Mode.\n- **Unknown** — requires a paid authenticated runtime or unpublished provider policy.\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\nAuthor `mcp-mobbin` as a non-mutating evidence transport: `packetKind: \"transport\"`, `mutatesWorkspace: false`, Code Mode calls only, no Write/Edit/Task, and mandatory cross-hub pairing with `sk-design` whenever Mobbin evidence informs a design decision. The transport retrieves real-world design evidence; it never decides taste, accessibility, responsiveness, or readiness. [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:79] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263]\n\nThe official server is hosted at `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` over Streamable HTTP. It uses browser OAuth, not a Mobbin API key. Public metadata and official docs confirm OAuth protected-resource discovery, Dynamic Client Registration, authorization-code flow, PKCE S256, access/refresh tokens, and `openid`. The official server repository contains registration/docs artifacts rather than a local runtime package. [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp]\n\nThe complete public documented tool baseline at 2026-07-16 is one read tool: `search_screens`. Its official skill-level contract accepts a natural-language query, `ios` or `web`, and a conservative result limit; it returns ordered screen metadata plus inline images. App, screen, flow, and element research are search/analysis intents over those screen results, not four published MCP tool families. Authenticated `tools/list` completeness and the exact server JSON Schema remain runtime UNKNOWNs and must be captured during validation. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n\nRegister a Code Mode manual named `mobbin` that launches `npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` with an empty environment. This adapts Code Mode's current stdio manual shape to Mobbin's remote HTTP/OAuth service. No API key, token, or client secret belongs in `.utcp_config.json` or `.env`. [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:468] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n\nMCP is unavailable on Free and included on Pro, Team, and Enterprise. The separately documented REST API is Team/Enterprise only and uses a workspace API key; it is not the MCP credential or transport. MCP is rate-limited to 60 requests per 60 seconds per user. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits]\n\n## 2. Scope, Method, and Evidence Boundary\n\nFive evidence iterations were run because `stopPolicy: max-iterations` made early convergence telemetry non-terminal:\n\n1. Hosted server, transport, authorization, and install baseline.\n2. Official skill surface and app/screen/flow/element workflows.\n3. Free/paid eligibility, MCP/API separation, and rate limits.\n4. Local Code Mode manual, packet architecture, and `sk-design` pairing.\n5. Live public protocol metadata, repository freshness, contradiction review, and terminal acceptance gates.\n\nEvidence was restricted to official Mobbin repositories/docs/endpoints, the `mcp-remote` maintainer repository, direct unauthenticated read-only protocol probes, and local integration contracts. No Mobbin login, paid authorization, token exchange, MCP tool call, OAuth-cache read/write, or remote mutation occurred. The 401/protected-resource checks prove endpoint/auth shape but cannot enumerate authenticated tools. [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n\nFreshness snapshot: the official server repository's latest observed commit was `bbee2a6be34d251c580ba80bb8b407c87587aba7` dated 2026-06-03; the skills repository's latest observed commit was `9657786338c5e7fed597031982398a8d99681fec` dated 2026-05-04, and `skills/` contained only `mobbin-search`. [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/commits?per_page=1] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/commits?per_page=1] [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n\n## 3. Server, Transport, Install, and Runtime\n\n| Concern | Confirmed contract | Packet implication |\n|---|---|---|\n| Server URL | `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp` | Single remote endpoint |\n| Provider transport | Streamable HTTP | Do not describe Mobbin itself as stdio |\n| Local adapter | `mcp-remote` launched over stdio | Lets current Code Mode consume remote HTTP/OAuth |\n| Provider install | None | Do not clone/build/install a Mobbin server |\n| Adapter install | On-demand through `npx -y` | Avoid interactive package confirmation |\n| Runtime | Node.js 18+ and working `npx` | Doctor checks both before OAuth |\n| Network | Outbound HTTPS plus localhost OAuth callback | Headless sessions need operator-visible escalation |\n| Account | Pro, Team, or Enterprise | Free is not a reduced MCP mode |\n\n[SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n\n`mcp-remote` defaults to HTTP-first and falls back to SSE only on an HTTP 404. Mobbin explicitly requires Streamable HTTP, so no forced SSE flag is needed. The adapter describes itself as experimental and is externally versioned; static compatibility does not equal a completed local OAuth/discovery run. [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote#transport-strategies] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other]\n\n## 4. Authentication, Credential Storage, and Security\n\nMobbin's official client flow requires no API key or manually copied token. On first use, the client opens a browser, the user signs in and authorizes access, and the client receives OAuth access/refresh tokens. Custom integrations use DCR and authorization code with PKCE S256. Client access is revocable. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect]\n\nA live unauthenticated request returned HTTP 401 and:\n\n```text\nWWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata=\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"\n{\"error\":{\"code\":\"unauthorized\",\"message\":\"Missing or invalid Authorization header\"}}\n```\n\nThe protected-resource document names resource `https://api.mobbin.com/mcp`, the Supabase authorization server, and `openid`. Authorization-server metadata publishes authorization, token, and registration endpoints plus PKCE S256. This matches the written integration contract. [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp] [SOURCE: https://ujasntkfphywizsdaapi.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server]\n\nSecurity rules for the packet:\n\n- Keep manual `env` empty; never add `MOBBIN_API_KEY`, the REST workspace key, access/refresh tokens, or a client secret.\n- Never accept credentials in prompts or tool arguments.\n- Never print Authorization headers, OAuth codes, token responses, adapter debug logs, or auth-cache contents.\n- Treat adapter auth state as operator-owned. Do not clear it automatically; reauthorization is an explicit operator action.\n- Use PKCE S256 even though live authorization metadata also advertises `plain`.\n- Interpret a pre-authorization 401 as the expected protected-resource challenge after reachability is proven, not as evidence that a static key is missing.\n\n[SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration]\n\n## 5. Official MCP Tool Surface\n\n### Public documented baseline\n\n| Tool | Posture | Skill-level inputs | Skill-level result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `search_screens` | Read/search | `query`: natural language; `platform`: `ios` or `web`; `limit`: default 5, normally no more than about 15 when broader variety is requested | `screens[]` metadata, `failed[]`, then ordered inline image blocks |\n\nThe official skill describes screen metadata as:\n\n```text\nscreens: [{ index, id, app_name, mobbin_url, image_url, platform }]\nfailed:  []\n```\n\nInline images arrive in the same response after metadata, so the workflow can analyze visible screens without inventing a second image-download tool. Preserve metadata/image order and report partial image failures. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md]\n\n### Completeness boundary\n\nThe official `skills/` tree contains one skill, `mobbin-search`, and its instructions name only `search_screens`. The official server repository publishes endpoint/registration artifacts but no public server implementation or authenticated `tools/list` export. Therefore:\n\n- **Confirmed:** `search_screens` is the only public documented tool.\n- **Unknown:** whether authenticated `tools/list` currently contains only that tool.\n- **Unknown:** the exact MCP JSON Schema and callable name produced by current Code Mode.\n- **Not allowed:** inventing `search_apps`, `search_flows`, `search_elements`, detail, image, or mutation tools.\n\n[SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills] [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp]\n\nThe packet's read-only guarantee is an authorization boundary, not an unsupported universal claim about every future provider tool. Allow only verified read/search tools. If live discovery returns a mutation-capable tool, refuse it and require an explicit reviewed contract change.\n\n## 6. Result Handling and Context Discipline\n\nUse conservative retrieval:\n\n1. Clarify the product/surface, research intent, and required platform.\n2. Start with `limit: 5`.\n3. Inspect ordered metadata and images together.\n4. Ask the user before widening materially; do not jump above about 15 merely to create variety.\n5. Report `failed[]` and missing images as partial success, never silently discard them.\n6. Retain `mobbin_url` as provenance for every selected reference.\n\nThe provider skill's visual-analysis sequence is: observe content/structure/styling/interaction cues; compare repeated patterns and meaningful differences; synthesize principles; and answer with evidence tied to the returned screens. The transport may describe observable facts, but any design recommendation or acceptance conclusion belongs to `sk-design`. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:176]\n\nDo not create the upstream skill's optional HTML evidence board inside `mcp-mobbin`. The requested packet is non-mutating. Artifact authoring can occur only in a separate explicitly authorized workflow outside this transport.\n\n## 7. App, Screen, Flow, and Element Research Workflows\n\nThere are not four documented MCP tool families. Use one retrieval surface with intent-specific query design:\n\n### App research\n\nName the app/company/category and the comparison goal: for example, “banking apps onboarding identity verification.” Compare returned `app_name`, platform, screen structure, and visible patterns. Multiple results are evidence, not a design chooser.\n\n### Screen research\n\nUse the concrete screen/state/job: “iOS subscription cancellation confirmation,” “web empty-state dashboard,” or “mobile checkout payment error.” Start at five results and cite each Mobbin URL used.\n\n### Flow research\n\nDescribe the user journey and target step: “first-run onboarding progression,” “card replacement flow,” or “forgot-password recovery.” The current public contract returns screens, not a first-class ordered flow object, so reconstruct sequence only when visual evidence supports it and label reconstruction as inference.\n\n### Element research\n\nName the component plus context/state: “bottom-sheet destructive confirmation,” “segmented control in analytics,” or “inline validation on signup.” Analyze how the element behaves within returned screens. Do not fabricate an element-detail tool or claim isolated component metadata.\n\nFor all four intents, use deep semantic queries for complex requests, keep platform explicit, and perform grounded visual comparison only after results arrive. [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md]\n\n## 8. Plans, MCP/API Separation, and Rate Limits\n\n| Surface | Free | Pro | Team | Enterprise | Credential |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|\n| Mobbin website | Limited browsing | Full paid features | Included | Included | User session |\n| Mobbin MCP | No | Yes | Yes | Yes | Browser OAuth |\n| Mobbin REST API | No | No | Yes | Yes | Workspace API key |\n\n[SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/pricing] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart]\n\nDo not conflate the Team/Enterprise REST API's Bearer API key or `POST /v1/screens/search` with MCP. No reviewed source documents different MCP tool sets for Pro versus Team versus Enterprise, so the stable packet should not invent per-tool tier gates. Exact Free-account MCP denial behavior is UNKNOWN: authorization might fail at different stages, and public docs do not publish its precise status/payload. Finance+ is a separate paid add-on, but public sources do not establish its MCP result coverage. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/pricing]\n\nMCP limit: 60 requests per 60 seconds per user. A 429 includes `Retry-After`; honor it, then use exponential backoff with jitter for continuing failures. Metadata-first, small-limit queries also reduce rate and context pressure. [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits]\n\n## 9. Code Mode Manual and Calling Convention\n\nPhase 002 should ship this paste-ready manual; phase 003 should add it to `manual_call_templates[]`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"mobbin\",\n  \"call_template_type\": \"mcp\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"mcpServers\": {\n      \"mobbin\": {\n        \"transport\": \"stdio\",\n        \"command\": \"npx\",\n        \"args\": [\n          \"-y\",\n          \"mcp-remote\",\n          \"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\"\n        ],\n        \"env\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n[SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:162] [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other]\n\nThe mandatory runtime sequence is:\n\n1. `list_tools()` or `search_tools({ task_description: \"Mobbin screen design research\", limit: 10 })`.\n2. Filter to the `mobbin` manual.\n3. Run `tool_info()` on the exact dotted discovery name.\n4. Only then call through `call_tool_chain({ code })` with the callable syntax `tool_info()` reports.\n\nCode Mode's general convention predicts dotted discovery `mobbin.mobbin.search_screens` and callable `mobbin.mobbin_search_screens(...)`, but both are **INFERRED** until live discovery. The skill-level argument example below is illustrative until `tool_info()` confirms its schema:\n\n```typescript\ncall_tool_chain({\n  code: `\n    const result = await mobbin.mobbin_search_screens({\n      query: \"iOS banking app onboarding identity verification\",\n      platform: \"ios\",\n      limit: 5\n    });\n    return { success: true, data: result, errors: [], timestamp: new Date().toISOString() };\n  `\n});\n```\n\n[SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md:252] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md:365]\n\n## 10. `mcp-mobbin` Packet Architecture and `sk-design` Pairing\n\nRecommended skill permission surface:\n\n```text\nRead, Glob, Grep,\nmcp__code_mode__list_tools,\nmcp__code_mode__search_tools,\nmcp__code_mode__tool_info,\nmcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain\n```\n\nDo not grant Write, Edit, Task, or a direct Mobbin MCP tool. The remote call path is Code Mode only. Shell-based doctor/install scripts may be shipped as user-invoked assets if phase standards require them, but the transport skill itself does not need Bash to query Mobbin.\n\nRegistry/hub contract:\n\n- `workflowMode: \"mcp-mobbin\"`\n- `packetKind: \"transport\"`\n- `backendKind`: a Mobbin Code Mode transport discriminator chosen consistently across registry/docs\n- `routingClass: \"metadata\"`\n- `toolPolicy.mutatesWorkspace: false`\n- `extensions.transport-axis.transports[]` contains `mcp-mobbin`\n- `crossHubPairing: mcp-mobbin -> sk-design`\n\n[SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md:79]\n\nPairing lifecycle for design-affecting research:\n\n1. `sk-design` gathers goal, surface, inputs, constraints, and proof expectations.\n2. It selects the smallest design-judgment mode (interface, foundations, motion, or audit).\n3. `mcp-mobbin` retrieves cited screens through Code Mode.\n4. Results return to the selected judgment mode.\n5. `sk-design`, not transport rank or images alone, owns taste, accessibility, responsive, and ready decisions.\n\nPure setup/doctor or factual tool-surface reporting does not make a design verdict, but the registry still declares the pairing. [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:20] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:172] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263]\n\n## 11. Recommendations\n\n1. Treat `search_screens` as the only stable documented tool and make live discovery the runtime authority.\n2. Fail closed on missing, renamed, expanded, or mutation-capable tool surfaces; do not silently widen permissions.\n3. Register exactly one `mobbin` manual using the stdio `mcp-remote` bridge and empty environment.\n4. Document Node 18+, `npx`, outbound HTTPS, browser/localhost OAuth, and paid account prerequisites.\n5. Put no Mobbin credential in `.env`; keep auth state operator-owned and outside packet logic.\n6. Separate website, OAuth MCP, and API-key REST entitlements everywhere.\n7. Route app/flow/element intents through semantic screen searches; never manufacture separate tools or structured flow semantics.\n8. Keep limits small, preserve result/image ordering and failures, cite `mobbin_url`, and honor 429 `Retry-After`.\n9. Make `mcp-mobbin` transport owner and `sk-design` judgment owner; transport output is evidence, not acceptance.\n10. Split deterministic packet/hub tests from operator-authorized paid OAuth smoke tests.\n\n## Eliminated Alternatives\n\n| Alternative | Reason eliminated | Evidence | Iteration |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n| Static `MOBBIN_API_KEY` for MCP | MCP uses browser OAuth; no manual key setup | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] | 1 |\n| Reuse the REST workspace key | REST and MCP are separate surfaces and plans | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] | 3 |\n| Clone/install a local Mobbin server | Official repository declares a hosted remote and has no runtime package | [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server] | 1 |\n| Describe Mobbin itself as stdio | Stdio belongs to the local adapter; provider transport is HTTP | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other] | 4 |\n| Direct unproven Code Mode HTTP manual | Current local precedent uses stdio plus `mcp-remote` for hosted OAuth | [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147] | 4 |\n| Separate app/flow/element/detail/image tools | Current official skill names only `search_screens` | [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md] | 2 |\n| Free as a limited MCP tier | MCP begins at Pro; Free browsing is a different product surface | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction] | 3 |\n| Per-tool Pro/Team/Enterprise claims | No reviewed source documents paid-tier tool differences | [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview] | 3 |\n| HTML evidence-board creation in transport | Violates non-mutating packet boundary | [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:81] | 2 |\n| Guess `mobbin.mobbin_search_screens` | Code Mode requires discovery and `tool_info()` | [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md:256] | 4 |\n| Treat public catalog as authenticated `tools/list` | Protected endpoint prevents public enumeration | [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp] | 5 |\n| Treat transport results as taste authority | `sk-design` owns judgment and acceptance | [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md:263] | 4 |\n| Auto-clear adapter auth state | Destructive to operator-owned sessions | [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote#troubleshooting] | 5 |\n\n## Divergence Map\n\n| Direction | Status | Evidence resolution | Remaining frontier |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| API key vs OAuth | Saturated | Docs plus live protected-resource metadata agree on OAuth/DCR/PKCE | Paid local round trip only |\n| Local package vs hosted server | Saturated | Official manifests/tree contain registration assets, no runtime | None for architecture |\n| One tool vs app/flow/element families | Saturated for public contract | Official skill tree contains one skill naming `search_screens` | Authenticated live list drift |\n| Free vs paid | Saturated for eligibility | Free excluded; Pro/Team/Enterprise included | Exact Free denial payload |\n| MCP vs REST API | Saturated | OAuth MCP versus Team/Enterprise workspace-key REST | None for manual design |\n| Direct HTTP vs stdio bridge | Resolved by local precedent | Current Code Mode remote examples and `refero` manual use `mcp-remote` | End-to-end local OAuth/refresh |\n| Transport vs judgment authority | Saturated | Phase specs and `sk-design` require non-mutating transport/pairing | Downstream graph and playbook proof |\n| Finance+ coverage | Public sources exhausted | Pricing documents add-on but not MCP inclusion | Provider/paid runtime evidence |\n\nNo formal divergent-mode pivot or Council artifact was produced. Breadth came from successive evidence angles: provider metadata, official skill behavior, entitlements, local integration contracts, and adversarial live public probes. The remaining frontier is operator-authorized runtime validation, not additional unauthenticated searching.\n\n## 12. Open Questions\n\nNo open question blocks phase-002 packet authorship. Preserve these as explicit downstream UNKNOWNs:\n\n1. What exact names and JSON Schemas do authenticated Code Mode `list_tools()` and `tool_info()` expose on the validation date?\n2. Does the current local Code Mode + `mcp-remote` version complete first-use Mobbin OAuth, refresh, and reconnect reliably?\n3. What precise status/payload/UX does a Free account receive during MCP authorization or tool use?\n4. Does Finance+ change the dataset returned through standard MCP search?\n\n## 13. Verification Plan\n\n### Deterministic no-account checks\n\n- JSON-parse the ready-to-paste manual and confirm one name-keyed `mobbin` entry.\n- Assert endpoint, `npx -y mcp-remote`, stdio adapter, and empty `env` exactly.\n- Assert no `MOBBIN_API_KEY`, REST key, token, secret, Authorization header, or `.env` requirement appears.\n- Assert packet frontmatter/registry forbid Write/Edit/Task and declare `mutatesWorkspace:false`.\n- Assert only Code Mode discovery/execution meta-tools are allowed for remote calls.\n- Fixture the public `search_screens` query/platform/limit and ordered metadata/failed/images contract, labeled skill-level rather than live schema.\n- Negative fixtures reject invented app/flow/element/detail/image/mutation tools and pre-discovery callable guesses.\n- Routing holdouts distinguish Mobbin evidence search from Figma transport, browser inspection, generic `sk-design`, and unrelated MCP setup.\n- Verify hub registry/router/description/graph metadata, transport list, pairing edge, and manual name remain synchronized.\n- Verify every design-affecting scenario returns evidence to `sk-design` before acceptance.\n\n### Operator-authorized paid live checks\n\n1. Confirm Node/npx and load the new manual; restart Code Mode.\n2. Observe the expected 401/protected-resource challenge before authorization without treating it as key failure.\n3. Complete browser OAuth with an eligible account; capture no tokens/log secrets.\n4. Run `list_tools()`, filter `mobbin`, and record exact dated dotted names.\n5. Run `tool_info()` for every exposed tool and compare the read-only allow-boundary.\n6. Execute one minimal `search_screens` call with `limit: 1`; verify query/platform schema, metadata, image order, and Mobbin URL.\n7. Run app-, flow-, and element-intent queries and confirm they remain screen-search workflows rather than fabricated tool families.\n8. Verify partial image failures remain visible.\n9. If safely observable, validate 429/`Retry-After` behavior without deliberately exhausting service quotas.\n10. Record unexpected tools/schema drift as a fail-closed packet update requirement.\n\nPaid/OAuth scenarios should allow `SKIP` with the missing entitlement/operator authorization stated.\n\n## 14. Troubleshooting, Risks, and Mitigations\n\n| Symptom/risk | Interpretation | Safe action |\n|---|---|---|\n| Endpoint returns 401 before auth | Expected protected-resource challenge | Complete browser OAuth; do not add an API key |\n| Browser does not open/callback fails | Headless session, port, timeout, or client problem | Move to interactive session or request operator action; never ask for token paste |\n| No `mobbin.*` tools | Manual load/start/auth/plan failure | Validate JSON, name, Node/npx, restart, OAuth, then eligibility |\n| Tool name/schema mismatch | Provider/adapter drift | Re-run `list_tools` + `tool_info`; fail closed and update reviewed docs |\n| 429 | Per-user request window exceeded | Honor `Retry-After`; exponential backoff with jitter; reduce query volume |\n| Free account cannot connect/use tools | Expected entitlement boundary | Explain MCP starts at Pro; do not guess precise failure semantics |\n| Token refresh/stale state | Operator-owned adapter auth state | Use diagnostics without printing secrets; clear only with explicit reauthorization consent |\n| Unexpected mutation tool | Provider surface expanded | Refuse; read-only packet requires explicit contract review |\n| Large image/result response | Context pressure | Default five; preserve/compare metadata first; widen only deliberately |\n| Individual images fail | Partial provider/storage failure | Preserve `failed[]`, return usable results plus errors |\n| Unpinned experimental adapter changes | Compatibility drift | Smoke-test after dependency change; consider pinning only in a separately reviewed change |\n| Design copied or generic | Transport mistaken for authority | Cite evidence; use `sk-design` critique/judgment; never copy wholesale |\n\n[SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits] [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md:642]\n\n## 15. Phase 002–003 Authoring Checklist\n\nPhase 002 creates `.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-mobbin/` only:\n\n- `SKILL.md` — transport identity, Code Mode-only permissions, discovery gate, read-only rules, pairing boundary.\n- `README.md` — user-facing purpose, prerequisites, public surface, plan/auth caveats.\n- `INSTALL_GUIDE.md` — Node/npx, manual snippet, first-use OAuth, discovery verification; no provider server install.\n- `assets/` — paste-ready `mobbin` UTCP manual with empty env; no secret template.\n- `references/mcp-wiring.md` — remote HTTP versus local stdio adapter, discovery/call naming, confirmed/inferred labels.\n- `references/tool-surface.md` — single public documented baseline, response shape, authenticated-live UNKNOWNs.\n- `references/workflows.md` or equivalent — app/screen/flow/element semantic query recipes and grounded analysis.\n- `references/troubleshooting.md` — 401, OAuth callback, manual discovery, plan, 429, drift, partial images.\n- `feature_catalog/` — capability inventory marked read-only.\n- `scripts/` — non-mutating doctor/snippet helpers that print no auth state.\n- `manual_testing_playbook/` — positive routing, at least two holdouts, negative/troubleshoot, deterministic and paid-live splits.\n- `mcp-servers/mobbin-mcp/README.md` — explicitly document hosted provider server and absence of local package source.\n- `changelog/` and package metadata required by the skill-authoring standard.\n- Run `package_skill.py --check` (and strict gate in phase 004) with every tool claim traced here.\n\nPhase 003 owns shared integration after sibling serial dependencies:\n\n- add `mcp-mobbin` to `mode-registry.json` as transport/metadata/non-mutating;\n- add transport-axis membership and `mcp-mobbin -> sk-design` cross-hub pairing;\n- add narrow router signals for Mobbin/app-screen-flow-element design-reference research plus holdouts;\n- update parent SKILL/README/description/graph metadata and hub changelog/playbook;\n- paste the `mobbin` manual into `.utcp_config.json` once;\n- regenerate the advisor skill graph and sweep all references for key/name/count consistency.\n\n[SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md:70] [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md:68]\n\n## 16. References\n\nPrimary Mobbin sources:\n\n- [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server]\n- [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/mcp.json]\n- [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/server.json]\n- [SOURCE: https://github.com/mobbin/skills]\n- [SOURCE: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/overview]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart]\n- [SOURCE: https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits]\n- [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/mcp]\n- [SOURCE: https://mobbin.com/pricing]\n- [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/mcp]\n- [SOURCE: https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp]\n- [SOURCE: https://ujasntkfphywizsdaapi.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server]\n- [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/commits?per_page=1]\n- [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills]\n- [SOURCE: https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/commits?per_page=1]\n\nTransport and local sources:\n\n- [SOURCE: https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote]\n- [SOURCE: file:.utcp_config.json:147]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/naming_convention.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/SKILL.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/mcp-tooling/mcp-figma/references/mcp-wiring.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md]\n- [SOURCE: file:.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md]\n\n## 17. Convergence Report\n\n- Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached`.\n- Total iterations: 5.\n- Questions answered: 5 / 5 to the public/static evidence boundary.\n- Remaining authoring-blocking questions: 0.\n- Runtime/provider UNKNOWNs retained: 4 (authenticated schema, local OAuth/refresh, exact Free denial, Finance+ coverage).\n- Last three iterations: run 3 — plan gating/API separation/rate limits (0.88); run 4 — Code Mode manual/packet architecture (0.82); run 5 — adversarial completeness/risk audit (0.58).\n- New-information ratios: 1.00, 0.93, 0.88, 0.82, 0.58.\n- Last-three rolling average: 0.76, above threshold 0.05.\n- MAD noise floor: 0.089; latest ratio 0.58 remained above it.\n- Question coverage: 1.00; composite stop telemetry did not supersede the configured hard-cap reason.\n- Stop-policy interpretation: all five required iterations ran; early convergence was telemetry only and review broadened through product, workflow, entitlement, local architecture, and adversarial protocol angles.\n- Divergence summary: no formal pivot/Council artifacts; public tool enumeration, static auth/install, entitlement, and packet placement were saturated. Paid runtime validation is the remaining frontier.\n- Confidence: high for the published endpoint/auth/plan/rate/public-tool/local architecture contract; medium for adapter compatibility; unknown for authenticated live schema and paid-runtime behavior.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":432,"totalLines":432,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/research.md","time":{"start":1785133728030,"end":1785133728315}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e158554e4c12008016a66fa9fd7d88191bf1816426e4be86b"}},"id":"prt_fa2430108001nSwnLecTN0YnYg","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242d1f7001m3St348OtWWs65"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133728328,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_FZSZtpSejxyw0CXfw4m7z6q5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/*.md"},"output":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-005.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md","metadata":{"count":5,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1785133728001,"end":1785133728319}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e158554e4c12008016a66fa9fd7c88191bdc52d0f4fa7b243"}},"id":"prt_fa24300f7001G2fo6WQbGQvXT5","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242d1f7001m3St348OtWWs65"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133728328,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"glob","callID":"call_IY5QhCoH7I1fBpSNKlcGr0Ik","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/*.jsonl"},"output":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-003.jsonl\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-005.jsonl\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-004.jsonl","metadata":{"count":5,"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1785133728007,"end":1785133728322}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e158554e4c12008016a66fa9fd7d48191bf07ba4564515307"}},"id":"prt_fa2430102001XAVVs08KZt2doo","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa242d1f7001m3St348OtWWs65"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133728328,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_JppOwiAw4fng1LZVu1OnstHz","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"openQuestions\": [],\n3:   \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n4:     {\"id\":\"q-auth\",\"text\":\"What credential model does the server use, how is the key provisioned/stored, and what does a correct Code Mode manual need to expose?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":1,\"evidence\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n5:     {\"id\":\"q-workflows\",\"text\":\"How do the official skills implement app, screen, flow, and element research workflows, including staged discovery and image/detail retrieval?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":2,\"evidence\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n6:     {\"id\":\"q-gating\",\"text\":\"Which capabilities are available to free users versus Pro subscribers, and what failure/upgrade behavior must the packet document without guessing?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":3,\"evidence\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/overview\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits\",\"https://mobbin.com/pricing\"]},\n7:     {\"id\":\"q-packet\",\"text\":\"What must the transport packet and UTCP manual contain?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":4,\"evidence\":[\".utcp_config.json\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other\",\"https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote\"]},\n8:     {\"id\":\"q-tool-surface\",\"text\":\"What is the complete MCP tool surface, transport, install path, and read-only contract?\",\"status\":\"resolved-with-bounded-unknowns\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":5,\"evidence\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"]}\n9:   ],\n10:   \"keyFindings\": [\n11:     {\"id\":\"finding-1-remote\",\"text\":\"The official Mobbin MCP is a hosted Streamable HTTP remote at https://api.mobbin.com/mcp; the official repository publishes registration metadata, not a local server package.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/server.json\"]},\n12:     {\"id\":\"finding-1-oauth\",\"text\":\"MCP clients authorize with browser OAuth; custom clients use DCR, PKCE S256, access tokens, and refresh tokens. No static Mobbin API key is required for MCP.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n13:     {\"id\":\"finding-1-plans\",\"text\":\"The MCP server is available to Pro, Team, and Enterprise accounts.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n14:     {\"id\":\"finding-1-revoke\",\"text\":\"OAuth access is account-scoped and revocable per connected MCP client.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect\"]},\n15:     {\"id\":\"finding-2-single-tool\",\"text\":\"The current official public skill documents one retrieval tool, search_screens; no separate app, flow, element, detail, or image tool is named.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n16:     {\"id\":\"finding-2-contract\",\"text\":\"The skill-level search contract uses a natural-language query, ios|web platform, and a conservative limit (default 5, about 15 for requested variety).\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n17:     {\"id\":\"finding-2-response\",\"text\":\"search_screens returns ordered screen metadata plus inline image blocks; visual analysis needs no secondary download/read step.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\"]},\n18:     {\"id\":\"finding-2-boundary\",\"text\":\"App, flow, and element work are query/analysis dimensions over screen results; optional HTML evidence-board authoring stays outside the read-only transport.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://mobbin.com/mcp\"]},\n19:     {\"id\":\"finding-3-entitlement\",\"text\":\"Free has no MCP access; MCP is included for Pro, Team, and Enterprise, with no documented per-tool differences among those paid tiers.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://mobbin.com/mcp\"]},\n20:     {\"id\":\"finding-3-api-split\",\"text\":\"The Team/Enterprise REST API uses a workspace API key and is distinct from OAuth MCP; its key must not be placed in the MCP manual.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/overview\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart\"]},\n21:     {\"id\":\"finding-3-rate\",\"text\":\"MCP rate limit is 60 requests per 60 seconds per user; 429 responses include Retry-After and should use backoff with jitter.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits\"]},\n22:     {\"id\":\"finding-3-unknown\",\"text\":\"The exact Free-plan OAuth/tool-call denial payload and Finance+ MCP coverage are undocumented and must remain UNKNOWN.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://mobbin.com/pricing\"]},\n23:     {\"id\":\"finding-4-manual\",\"text\":\"The mobbin Code Mode manual should launch npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp over stdio with an empty env object.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".utcp_config.json\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other\"]},\n24:     {\"id\":\"finding-4-oauth-storage\",\"text\":\"No MCP secret belongs in .env; browser OAuth is completed on first use and mcp-remote owns local OAuth state.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote\"]},\n25:     {\"id\":\"finding-4-discovery\",\"text\":\"Code Mode must run list/search, then tool_info, then call_tool_chain; mobbin.mobbin_search_screens is inferred until that live discovery succeeds.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n26:     {\"id\":\"finding-4-boundary\",\"text\":\"mcp-mobbin is a non-mutating evidence transport; sk-design owns taste, critique, proof expectations, and acceptance.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md\"]},\n27:     {\"id\":\"finding-5-challenge\",\"text\":\"The live endpoint returns a 401 Bearer challenge pointing to its protected-resource metadata; this proves reachability before authorization.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"]},\n28:     {\"id\":\"finding-5-oauth-metadata\",\"text\":\"Live metadata confirms the Mobbin resource, openid scope, authorization server, DCR endpoint, and PKCE S256 support.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\",\"https://ujasntkfphywizsdaapi.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server\"]},\n29:     {\"id\":\"finding-5-public-completeness\",\"text\":\"At the evidence date the complete public documented baseline is one read tool, search_screens; authenticated tools/list completeness and exact JSON Schema remain validation-time UNKNOWNs.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n30:     {\"id\":\"finding-5-acceptance\",\"text\":\"Deployment acceptance requires a paid-account browser OAuth round-trip, Code Mode list/search/tool_info discovery, a minimal read, and explicit read-only/sk-design/hub graph proof.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md\",\".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md\"]}\n31:   ],\n32:   \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n33:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-static-api-key\",\"text\":\"Static MOBBIN_API_KEY as the official MCP credential\",\"reason\":\"Official MCP docs specify browser OAuth and no manual key setup.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1},\n34:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-local-package\",\"text\":\"An npm-installed local Mobbin server as the official transport\",\"reason\":\"Official manifests declare a hosted Streamable HTTP remote.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1},\n35:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-invented-tools\",\"text\":\"Invented app/flow/element/detail tool names\",\"reason\":\"Current public official repositories name only search_screens.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2},\n36:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-board-write\",\"text\":\"HTML evidence-board creation inside the transport packet\",\"reason\":\"The requested transport is read-only; optional artifact authoring belongs to a separate authorized workflow.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2},\n37:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-rest-key\",\"text\":\"REST API key reused for MCP\",\"reason\":\"Official overview separates API-key REST from OAuth MCP.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3},\n38:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-free-mcp\",\"text\":\"Free described as a limited MCP tier\",\"reason\":\"Official MCP eligibility begins at Pro; website browsing limits are a separate surface.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3},\n39:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-direct-http\",\"text\":\"An unproven direct HTTP Code Mode manual\",\"reason\":\"Current repository manuals and the hosted-OAuth precedent adapt remote servers through mcp-remote stdio.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4},\n40:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-mcp-env-secret\",\"text\":\"A Mobbin API key or OAuth token in the manual environment\",\"reason\":\"Mobbin MCP uses browser OAuth and mcp-remote manages local OAuth state.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4},\n41:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-transport-judgment\",\"text\":\"Transport-owned design judgment or local evidence-board writes\",\"reason\":\"The packet is non-mutating evidence retrieval and sk-design owns acceptance.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4},\n42:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-public-live-equivalence\",\"text\":\"Public skill catalog represented as authenticated live tools/list\",\"reason\":\"The protected endpoint prevents unauthenticated enumeration and no public live schema export exists.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5},\n43:     {\"id\":\"ruled-out-bridge-proven\",\"text\":\"mcp-remote integration declared operational from static compatibility alone\",\"reason\":\"A clean paid-account Code Mode OAuth/discovery run is still required.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5}\n44:   ],\n45:   \"coverageBySources\": {\"github.com\":10,\"docs.mobbin.com\":12,\"mobbin.com\":4,\"local\":10},\n46:   \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n47:   \"graphConvergenceScore\": 1.0,\n48:   \"graphDecision\": \"STOP\",\n49:   \"graphBlockers\": [],\n50:   \"divergence\": {\"completed\":[],\"failures\":[],\"overrides\":[],\"saturatedDirections\":[]},\n51:   \"metrics\": {\"iterationsCompleted\":5,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":5,\"keyFindings\":20,\"convergenceScore\":1.0,\"coverageBySources\":{\"github.com\":10,\"docs.mobbin.com\":12,\"mobbin.com\":4,\"local\":10}},\n52:   \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-07-16T11:17:52Z\"\n53: }\n\n(End of file - total 53 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    {\"id\":\"q-auth\",\"text\":\"What credential model does the server use, how is the key provisioned/stored, and what does a correct Code Mode manual need to expose?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":1,\"evidence\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-workflows\",\"text\":\"How do the official skills implement app, screen, flow, and element research workflows, including staged discovery and image/detail retrieval?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":2,\"evidence\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-gating\",\"text\":\"Which capabilities are available to free users versus Pro subscribers, and what failure/upgrade behavior must the packet document without guessing?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":3,\"evidence\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/overview\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits\",\"https://mobbin.com/pricing\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-packet\",\"text\":\"What must the transport packet and UTCP manual contain?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":4,\"evidence\":[\".utcp_config.json\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other\",\"https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-tool-surface\",\"text\":\"What is the complete MCP tool surface, transport, install path, and read-only contract?\",\"status\":\"resolved-with-bounded-unknowns\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":5,\"evidence\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"]}\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-remote\",\"text\":\"The official Mobbin MCP is a hosted Streamable HTTP remote at https://api.mobbin.com/mcp; the official repository publishes registration metadata, not a local server package.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/server.json\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-oauth\",\"text\":\"MCP clients authorize with browser OAuth; custom clients use DCR, PKCE S256, access tokens, and refresh tokens. No static Mobbin API key is required for MCP.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-plans\",\"text\":\"The MCP server is available to Pro, Team, and Enterprise accounts.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-revoke\",\"text\":\"OAuth access is account-scoped and revocable per connected MCP client.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-single-tool\",\"text\":\"The current official public skill documents one retrieval tool, search_screens; no separate app, flow, element, detail, or image tool is named.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-contract\",\"text\":\"The skill-level search contract uses a natural-language query, ios|web platform, and a conservative limit (default 5, about 15 for requested variety).\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-response\",\"text\":\"search_screens returns ordered screen metadata plus inline image blocks; visual analysis needs no secondary download/read step.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-boundary\",\"text\":\"App, flow, and element work are query/analysis dimensions over screen results; optional HTML evidence-board authoring stays outside the read-only transport.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://mobbin.com/mcp\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-3-entitlement\",\"text\":\"Free has no MCP access; MCP is included for Pro, Team, and Enterprise, with no documented per-tool differences among those paid tiers.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://mobbin.com/mcp\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-3-api-split\",\"text\":\"The Team/Enterprise REST API uses a workspace API key and is distinct from OAuth MCP; its key must not be placed in the MCP manual.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/overview\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart\"]},","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","text":"{\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\n    {\"id\":\"q-auth\",\"text\":\"What credential model does the server use, how is the key provisioned/stored, and what does a correct Code Mode manual need to expose?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":1,\"evidence\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-workflows\",\"text\":\"How do the official skills implement app, screen, flow, and element research workflows, including staged discovery and image/detail retrieval?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":2,\"evidence\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-gating\",\"text\":\"Which capabilities are available to free users versus Pro subscribers, and what failure/upgrade behavior must the packet document without guessing?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":3,\"evidence\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/overview\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits\",\"https://mobbin.com/pricing\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-packet\",\"text\":\"What must the transport packet and UTCP manual contain?\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":4,\"evidence\":[\".utcp_config.json\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other\",\"https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"q-tool-surface\",\"text\":\"What is the complete MCP tool surface, transport, install path, and read-only contract?\",\"status\":\"resolved-with-bounded-unknowns\",\"resolvedAtIteration\":5,\"evidence\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"]}\n  ],\n  \"keyFindings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-remote\",\"text\":\"The official Mobbin MCP is a hosted Streamable HTTP remote at https://api.mobbin.com/mcp; the official repository publishes registration metadata, not a local server package.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/mobbin-mcp-server/main/server.json\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-oauth\",\"text\":\"MCP clients authorize with browser OAuth; custom clients use DCR, PKCE S256, access tokens, and refresh tokens. No static Mobbin API key is required for MCP.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-plans\",\"text\":\"The MCP server is available to Pro, Team, and Enterprise accounts.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/build-an-integration\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-1-revoke\",\"text\":\"OAuth access is account-scoped and revocable per connected MCP client.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/disconnect\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-single-tool\",\"text\":\"The current official public skill documents one retrieval tool, search_screens; no separate app, flow, element, detail, or image tool is named.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://github.com/mobbin/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-contract\",\"text\":\"The skill-level search contract uses a natural-language query, ios|web platform, and a conservative limit (default 5, about 15 for requested variety).\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-response\",\"text\":\"search_screens returns ordered screen metadata plus inline image blocks; visual analysis needs no secondary download/read step.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-2-boundary\",\"text\":\"App, flow, and element work are query/analysis dimensions over screen results; optional HTML evidence-board authoring stays outside the read-only transport.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2,\"sources\":[\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\",\"https://mobbin.com/mcp\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-3-entitlement\",\"text\":\"Free has no MCP access; MCP is included for Pro, Team, and Enterprise, with no documented per-tool differences among those paid tiers.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://mobbin.com/mcp\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-3-api-split\",\"text\":\"The Team/Enterprise REST API uses a workspace API key and is distinct from OAuth MCP; its key must not be placed in the MCP manual.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/overview\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/api/quickstart\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-3-rate\",\"text\":\"MCP rate limit is 60 requests per 60 seconds per user; 429 responses include Retry-After and should use backoff with jitter.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/rate-limits\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-3-unknown\",\"text\":\"The exact Free-plan OAuth/tool-call denial payload and Finance+ MCP coverage are undocumented and must remain UNKNOWN.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://mobbin.com/pricing\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-4-manual\",\"text\":\"The mobbin Code Mode manual should launch npx -y mcp-remote https://api.mobbin.com/mcp over stdio with an empty env object.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".utcp_config.json\",\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/references/configuration.md\",\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/clients/other\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-4-oauth-storage\",\"text\":\"No MCP secret belongs in .env; browser OAuth is completed on first use and mcp-remote owns local OAuth state.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\"https://docs.mobbin.com/mcp/introduction\",\"https://github.com/geelen/mcp-remote\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-4-discovery\",\"text\":\"Code Mode must run list/search, then tool_info, then call_tool_chain; mobbin.mobbin_search_screens is inferred until that live discovery succeeds.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-4-boundary\",\"text\":\"mcp-mobbin is a non-mutating evidence transport; sk-design owns taste, critique, proof expectations, and acceptance.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4,\"sources\":[\".opencode/skills/sk-design/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-5-challenge\",\"text\":\"The live endpoint returns a 401 Bearer challenge pointing to its protected-resource metadata; this proves reachability before authorization.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://api.mobbin.com/mcp\",\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-5-oauth-metadata\",\"text\":\"Live metadata confirms the Mobbin resource, openid scope, authorization server, DCR endpoint, and PKCE S256 support.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://api.mobbin.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp\",\"https://ujasntkfphywizsdaapi.supabase.co/auth/v1/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-5-public-completeness\",\"text\":\"At the evidence date the complete public documented baseline is one read tool, search_screens; authenticated tools/list completeness and exact JSON Schema remain validation-time UNKNOWNs.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"https://api.github.com/repos/mobbin/skills/contents/skills\",\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mobbin/skills/main/skills/mobbin-search/SKILL.md\"]},\n    {\"id\":\"finding-5-acceptance\",\"text\":\"Deployment acceptance requires a paid-account browser OAuth round-trip, Code Mode list/search/tool_info discovery, a minimal read, and explicit read-only/sk-design/hub graph proof.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/SKILL.md\",\".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/002-skill-authoring/spec.md\",\".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/003-hub-integration/spec.md\"]}\n  ],\n  \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-static-api-key\",\"text\":\"Static MOBBIN_API_KEY as the official MCP credential\",\"reason\":\"Official MCP docs specify browser OAuth and no manual key setup.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-local-package\",\"text\":\"An npm-installed local Mobbin server as the official transport\",\"reason\":\"Official manifests declare a hosted Streamable HTTP remote.\",\"addedAtIteration\":1},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-invented-tools\",\"text\":\"Invented app/flow/element/detail tool names\",\"reason\":\"Current public official repositories name only search_screens.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-board-write\",\"text\":\"HTML evidence-board creation inside the transport packet\",\"reason\":\"The requested transport is read-only; optional artifact authoring belongs to a separate authorized workflow.\",\"addedAtIteration\":2},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-rest-key\",\"text\":\"REST API key reused for MCP\",\"reason\":\"Official overview separates API-key REST from OAuth MCP.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-free-mcp\",\"text\":\"Free described as a limited MCP tier\",\"reason\":\"Official MCP eligibility begins at Pro; website browsing limits are a separate surface.\",\"addedAtIteration\":3},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-direct-http\",\"text\":\"An unproven direct HTTP Code Mode manual\",\"reason\":\"Current repository manuals and the hosted-OAuth precedent adapt remote servers through mcp-remote stdio.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-mcp-env-secret\",\"text\":\"A Mobbin API key or OAuth token in the manual environment\",\"reason\":\"Mobbin MCP uses browser OAuth and mcp-remote manages local OAuth state.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-transport-judgment\",\"text\":\"Transport-owned design judgment or local evidence-board writes\",\"reason\":\"The packet is non-mutating evidence retrieval and sk-design owns acceptance.\",\"addedAtIteration\":4},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-public-live-equivalence\",\"text\":\"Public skill catalog represented as authenticated live tools/list\",\"reason\":\"The protected endpoint prevents unauthenticated enumeration and no public live schema export exists.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5},\n    {\"id\":\"ruled-out-bridge-proven\",\"text\":\"mcp-remote integration declared operational from static compatibility alone\",\"reason\":\"A clean paid-account Code Mode OAuth/discovery run is still required.\",\"addedAtIteration\":5}\n  ],\n  \"coverageBySources\": {\"github.com\":10,\"docs.mobbin.com\":12,\"mobbin.com\":4,\"local\":10},\n  \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n  \"graphConvergenceScore\": 1.0,\n  \"graphDecision\": \"STOP\",\n  \"graphBlockers\": [],\n  \"divergence\": {\"completed\":[],\"failures\":[],\"overrides\":[],\"saturatedDirections\":[]},\n  \"metrics\": {\"iterationsCompleted\":5,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":5,\"keyFindings\":20,\"convergenceScore\":1.0,\"coverageBySources\":{\"github.com\":10,\"docs.mobbin.com\":12,\"mobbin.com\":4,\"local\":10}},\n  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-07-16T11:17:52Z\"\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":53,"totalLines":53,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/mcp-tooling/010-mcp-mobbin/001-r