nt/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@\n+---\n+title: Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\n+description: Detached ten-iteration audit strategy for framework dead code, residue, placement, architecture, and over-engineering.\n+---\n+\n+# Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\n+\n+## 1. Overview\n+\n+This detached lineage runs exactly ten evidence iterations. Convergence is telemetry only before the hard cap. Each pass pivots to an uncovered repository surface or failure mode.\n+\n+## 2. Topic\n+\n+Audit `.opencode/`, repository-root configuration, and `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, and `.devin/` mirrors for CAT-1 through CAT-6 findings. Exclude `.opencode/specs/` from findings.\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n+## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n+\n+- [ ] Which `bin/` launchers, daemon bridges, flags, and helper modules are unreachable, duplicated, or disproportionate?\n+- [ ] Which MCP-server modules, generated outputs, and compatibility layers are dead, superseded, or misplaced?\n+- [ ] Which deep-loop runtime layers duplicate responsibility, violate boundaries, or cost more than current usage justifies?\n+- [ ] Which skill-hub metadata, mode registries, routers, and generated compiled-routing artifacts drift or duplicate policy?\n+- [ ] Which commands and agents are stale, dynamically unreachable, mirrored incorrectly, or contractually inconsistent?\n+- [ ] Which repository-root configs and dotfiles are obsolete, duplicated, or misplaced?\n+- [ ] Which runtime mirror files drift from canonical `.opencode/` sources or contain redundant standalone logic?\n+- [ ] Which backup, scratch, dated snapshot, generated output, or nested dependency residue exists outside excluded specs?\n+- [ ] Which candidate files remain unreferenced after literal searches across code, docs, YAML, and JSON?\n+- [ ] Which high-value simplifications survive adversarial cross-surface verification?\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n+\n+## 4. Non-Goals\n+\n+- Do not delete, move, rename, refactor, or repair audited files.\n+- Do not report findings under `.opencode/specs/`.\n+- Do not treat third-party dependency contents as findings unless a stray dependency tree is committed in a source surface.\n+- Do not infer deadness from import graphs alone; dynamic string and documentation contracts count as reachability.\n+\n+## 5. Stop Conditions\n+\n+- Complete all ten iterations unless state corruption prevents valid lineage artifacts.\n+- Stop at iteration ten with `maxIterationsReached`.\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n+## 6. Answered Questions\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n+\n+<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n+<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n+## 7. What Worked\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n+## 8. What Failed\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n+## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n+## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n+## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n+\n+- Completed pivots: 0\n+- Saturated: none yet\n+- Remaining frontier: all named surfaces\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n+## 11A. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n+## 11. Next Focus\n+\n+Iteration 1: `bin/`, launchers, daemon clients, and compiled-routing serving surface.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n+<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n+\n+## 12. Known Context\n+\n+- The code graph is empty, so structural deadness must be established with exact literal searches and direct source inspection.\n+- The audit excludes `.opencode/specs/` from findings and writes only to this lineage.\n+- The caller requires every finding to name an existing path, `file:line` evidence, and an exact reproducible command.\n+\n+## 13. Research Boundaries\n+\n+- Max iterations: 10\n+- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n+- Stop policy: max-iterations\n+- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n+- Progressive synthesis: false\n+- Executor provenance: `cli-opencode`, model `openai/gpt-5.6-sol`\n+- Session: `fanout-sol-1785133613018-3fbdzo`\n+- Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol`\n\nIndex: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-se