gh CAT-6 findings. Exclude `.opencode/specs/` from findings.\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n+## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n+\n+- [ ] Which `bin/` launchers, daemon bridges, flags, and helper modules are unreachable, duplicated, or disproportionate?\n+- [ ] Which MCP-server modules, generated outputs, and compatibility layers are dead, superseded, or misplaced?\n+- [ ] Which deep-loop runtime layers duplicate responsibility, violate boundaries, or cost more than current usage justifies?\n+- [ ] Which skill-hub metadata, mode registries, routers, and generated compiled-routing artifacts drift or duplicate policy?\n+- [ ] Which commands and agents are stale, dynamically unreachable, mirrored incorrectly, or contractually inconsistent?\n+- [ ] Which repository-root configs and dotfiles are obsolete, duplicated, or misplaced?\n+- [ ] Which runtime mirror files drift from canonical `.opencode/` sources or contain redundant standalone logic?\n+- [ ] Which backup, scratch, dated snapshot, generated output, or nested dependency residue exists outside excluded specs?\n+- [ ] Which candidate files remain unreferenced after literal searches across code, docs, YAML, and JSON?\n+- [ ] Which high-value simplifications survive adversarial cross-surface verification?\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n+\n+## 4. Non-Goals\n+\n+- Do not delete, move, rename, refactor, or repair audited files.\n+- Do not report findings under `.opencode/specs/`.\n+- Do not treat third-party dependency contents as findings unless a stray dependency tree is committed in a source surface.\n+- Do not infer deadness from import graphs alone; dynamic string and documentation contracts count as reachability.\n+\n+## 5. Stop Conditions\n+\n+- Complete all ten iterations unless state corruption prevents valid lineage artifacts.\n+- Stop at iteration ten with `maxIterationsReached`.\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n+## 6. Answered Questions\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n+\n+<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n+<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n+## 7. What Worked\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n+## 8. What Failed\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n+## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n+## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n+## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n+\n+- Completed pivots: 0\n+- Saturated: none yet\n+- Remaining frontier: all named surfaces\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n+## 11A. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n+\n+None yet.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n+## 11. Next Focus\n+\n+Iteration 1: `bin/`, launchers, daemon clients, and compiled-routing serving surface.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n+<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n+\n+## 12. Known Context\n+\n+- The code graph is empty, so structural deadness must be established with exact literal searches and direct source inspection.\n+- The audit excludes `.opencode/specs/` from findings and writes only to this lineage.\n+- The caller requires every finding to name an existing path, `file:line` evidence, and an exact reproducible command.\n+\n+## 13. Research Boundaries\n+\n+- Max iterations: 10\n+- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n+- Stop policy: max-iterations\n+- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n+- Progressive synthesis: false\n+- Executor provenance: `cli-opencode`, model `openai/gpt-5.6-sol`\n+- Session: `fanout-sol-1785133613018-3fbdzo`\n+- Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol`\n","additions":110,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","relativePath":".opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","type":"add","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+{\n+  \"openQuestions\": [],\n+  \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n+  \"keyFindings\": [],\n+  \"ruledOutDirections\": [],\n+  \"coverageBySources\": {},\n+  \"blockedStopHistory\": [],\n+  \"graphConvergenceScore\": 0,\n+  \"graphDecision\": \"CONTINUE\",\n+  \"graphBlockers\": [\"questionCoverage\", \"evidenceDepth\"],\n+  \"divergence\": { \"completed\": [], \"failures\": [], \"overrides\": [], \"saturatedDirections\": [] },\n+  \"metrics\": {\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 0,\n+    \"openQuestions\": 10,\n+    \"resolvedQuestions\": 0,\n+    \"keyFindings\": 0,\n+    \"convergenceScore\": 0,\n+    \"coverageBySources\": {}\n+  },\n+  \"lastUpdated\": \"2026-07-27T06:29:51Z\"\n+}\n","additions":21,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA .opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json\nA .opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl\nA .opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\nA .opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","time":{"start":1785133863155,"end":1785133863167}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0df418f9abcfb3c3016a66faf166f88191b16eb8fcad9a7504"}},"id":"prt_fa2443fb2001SjfRt23ldVHiY5","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa244121600193BRb7hFKrGSeJ"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1785133864463,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"id":"prt_fa245160c0014hNGcCtNYuTMAv","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fa244121600193BRb7hFKrGSeJ","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":225095,"input":1393,"output":2990,"reasoning":40,"cache":{"write":0,"read":220672}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785133876547,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"id":"prt_fa2454541001OPnG01O4wF31tA","messageID":"msg_fa2451ace001RiLa50jjImprPx","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133889144,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_3vdm3IosjuDFo6M7rpEJJnzH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"bin: MCP Launchers, Daemon CLIs, Compiled Routing and Repo Tooling\"\n3: description: \"Executable entrypoints for the OpenCode runtime: three MCP launchers and their daemon-backed CLI shims, the local embedding server, the compiled-routing serving and publication tools, and the git, worktree and hook helpers.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"mcp launcher\"\n6:   - \"hf model server\"\n7:   - \"mk-spec-memory launcher\"\n8:   - \"spec-memory cli\"\n9:   - \"code-index cli\"\n10:   - \"skill-advisor cli\"\n11:   - \"compiled route cli\"\n12:   - \"compiled routing runtime\"\n13: ---\n14: \n15: # bin: MCP Launchers, Daemon CLIs, Compiled Routing and Repo Tooling\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `bin/` holds the executable entrypoints that the OpenCode runtime spawns to start each MCP server, plus the daemon-backed CLI shims that reach the same servers from a shell. Three launchers wrap the spec-kit, skill-advisor and code-graph MCP servers. three CLI shims (`spec-memory.cjs`, `code-index.cjs`, `skill-advisor.cjs`) front the same daemons over the IPC socket. one process is the local HuggingFace embedding server that serves `hf-local` vector requests over a Unix domain socket or TCP loopback.\n20: \n21: Current state:\n22: \n23: - Each launcher loads project-local `.env.local` / `.env`, ensures the server's `dist/` artifacts are built and current, serializes concurrent starts with a filesystem bootstrap lock, then spawns the MCP child and bridges stdio to the running daemon.\n24: - The three CLI shims run the built daemon-backed CLIs (`spec-memory` 41 tools, `code-index` 8 tools, `skill-advisor` 9 tools) against the **same unchanged daemons** the MCP registrations use, a dual-stack surface, not a replacement. Each shim enforces a dist-freshness guard (exit `69` on missing/stale dist, with a per-CLI `*_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), defaults `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to the short `/tmp/<service>` directory, and refuses a socket path over the Darwin `sun_path` limit.\n25: - The freshness check itself is a shared module, not per-shim logic: all three shims call `checkPackageFreshness()` from [`system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/dist-freshness.cjs`](../skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/dist-freshness.cjs), which also backs `validate.sh`'s hard staleness backstop, the `sk-code` PostToolUse hook, and the `mk-dist-freshness-guard` OpenCode plugin, one source of truth for \"is this package's dist current\" across all four call sites. See §6 \"Dist freshness\" for the full package table and consumer list.\n26: - `hf-model-server.cjs` loads a transformers model and answers `/api/health` and `/api/embed` requests. It refuses any non-loopback bind unless the operator sets `HF_EMBED_ALLOW_REMOTE_BIND=1` and supplies `HF_EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN`, and it asserts ownership of the socket directory before listening.\n27: - Shared launcher behavior (model-server supervision, stdio-to-socket bridging, sidecar env allowlist) lives in `lib/`. The CLI shims' dist entrypoints reuse `lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs` for socket-path resolution and warm-daemon probes.\n28: - A second family serves and publishes **compiled routing**. `compiled-route.cjs` is the runtime front door a hub calls to ask whether the compiled router is authoritative for it, falling back to legacy routing when it is not. `compiled-route-status.cjs` reports per-hub serving state with a cause code that separates expected drift from breakage. `compiled-route-guard.cjs` is the gate: it fails when a hub's activation manifest no longer matches what its routing inputs compile to, or when the promoted runtime and its authored source disagree. `compiled-route-sync.cjs` publishes a new closure by tracing, staging, verifying, swapping and then finalizing or reverting. `compiled-route-manifest.cjs` is a thin CLI over the activation-manifest library in `lib/`.\n29: - `check-no-spec-imports.cjs` proves the durable invariant behind that family: nothing under `bin/` reaches into `.opencode/specs/` at runtime, so the serving path cannot break when the authored tree moves.\n30: - The remaining files are repository tooling. `worktree-*.sh` launch, prune, guard and report on per-session git worktrees. `git-sync.sh` and `git-live-follow.sh` back the continuous-integration workflow. `check-git-hooks.sh` warns at session start when git hooks are missing or drifted, and `install-codex-hooks.mjs` merges the versioned Codex hook set into the user-global config.\n31: - Launcher reliability knobs, persistent log, lease-probe reap hardening, the mk-code-index reconnecting proxy, the Stop-hook orphan-sweep fallback, and default-on daemon re-election for mk-spec-memory, are operator-tunable via `SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_LOG`, `SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRIES`, `SPECKIT_STOP_HOOK_ORPHAN_SWEEP`, and `SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION`. see the MCP server's [`ENV-REFERENCE.md`](../skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/ENV-REFERENCE.md).\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n36: \n37: ```text\n38: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n39: │                              bin/                                 │\n40: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n41: \n42: ┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────┐     ┌────────────────┐\n43: │ OpenCode     │ ──▶ │ mk-*-launcher.cjs    │ ──▶ │ MCP server     │\n44: │ runtime      │     │ env + build + lock   │     │ dist child     │\n45: └──────────────┘     └──────────┬───────────┘     └────────────────┘\n46:                                 │\n47:                                 ▼\n48:                      ┌──────────────────────┐\n49:                      │ lib/                 │\n50:                      │ supervision + bridge │\n51:                      └──────────┬───────────┘\n52:                                 │ (spec-memory + advisor only)\n53:                                 ▼\n54:                      ┌──────────────────────┐     ┌────────────────┐\n55:                      │ hf-model-server.cjs  │ ──▶ │ transformers   │\n56:                      │ /api/embed + health  │     │ embedding model│\n57:                      └──────────────────────┘     └────────────────┘\n58: \n59: Dependency direction: launchers ───▶ lib/ ───▶ hf-model-server.cjs\n60: ```\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 3. DIRECTORY TREE\n65: \n66: ```text\n67: bin/\n68: +-- mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs    # Launches mk-spec-memory MCP, owns shared hf-model-server lease\n69: +-- mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs  # Launches mk-skill-advisor MCP, optional model-server supervision\n70: +-- mk-code-index-launcher.cjs     # Launches mk-code-index MCP, maintainer-mode INDEX_* override\n71: +-- spec-memory.cjs                # Daemon-backed CLI shim for mk-spec-memory (41 tools)\n72: +-- code-index.cjs                 # Daemon-backed CLI shim for mk-code-index (8 tools)\n73: +-- skill-advisor.cjs              # Daemon-backed CLI shim for mk-skill-advisor (9 tools)\n74: +-- cli-offline-smoke.cjs          # Daemon-free smoke: list-tools counts (41/8/9), cwd-independent\n75: +-- cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke.cjs    # Daemon-free smoke: CLI failure contract (exit 64/69/75, parseable envelopes)\n76: +-- cli-offline-smoke.test.cjs     # Test runner asserting cli-offline-smoke.cjs passes\n77: +-- hf-model-server.cjs            # Local HTTP/UDS HuggingFace embedding server\n78: +-- worktree-session.sh            # Launch an AI session in an isolated git worktree + branch + DBs\n79: +-- worktree-reaper.sh             # Prune merged/clean per-session worktrees + stale socket dirs\n80: +-- worktree-guard.sh              # SessionStart detect-and-warn when a top-level session is on shared main\n81: +-- worktree-status.sh             # Reports worktree, branch and sync state\n82: +-- git-sync.sh                    # Autosync helper for the git continuous-integration workflow\n83: +-- git-live-follow.sh             # Live-follow watcher for the same workflow\n84: +-- check-git-hooks.sh             # SessionStart guard warning on missing or drifted git hooks\n85: +-- install-codex-hooks.mjs        # Merges the versioned Codex hook set into the user-global config\n86: +-- speckit-completion.cjs         # Completion-state CLI over the runtime-neutral core\n87: +-- compiled-route.cjs             # Runtime front door: is the compiled router authoritative for a hub\n88: +-- compiled-route-status.cjs      # Per-hub serving status with a cause code separating drift from breakage\n89: +-- compiled-route-guard.cjs       # Freshness gate: serving matches inputs, runtime matches source\n90: +-- compiled-route-manifest.cjs    # CLI over the activation-manifest library in lib/\n91: +-- compiled-route-sync.cjs        # Publication tool: trace, stage, verify, swap, finalize or revert\n92: +-- check-no-spec-imports.cjs      # Proves nothing here reaches into the spec tree at runtime\n93: +-- compiled-routing-*.vitest.ts   # Routing foundation and flag-propagation suites\n94: +-- mk-code-index-launcher-*.vitest.ts  # Launcher lease, registry and WAL coverage\n95: +-- tests/                         # node:test suite for the publication lifecycle\n96: +-- lib/                           # Shared supervision, IPC bridge, env allowlist, routing library\n97: `-- README.md\n98: ```\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: ## 4. KEY FILES\n103: \n104: | File | Responsibility |\n105: |---|---|\n106: | `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-spec-memory MCP child. Manages the shared hf-model-server lease, respawn locks, and reaping a dead lease child before respawn. |\n107: | `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-skill-advisor MCP child. Loads model-server supervision when enabled, enforces a strict single-writer lease, and rebuilds `dist/` from `handlers`, `lib`, `schemas`, `tools` when stale. |\n108: | `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-code-index MCP child. Applies the maintainer-mode `INDEX_*` override, migrates the code-graph database back to the skill-local path, and sets `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR` for the child. |\n109: | `spec-memory.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-spec-memory. Checks dist freshness and exits `69` when stale, with `SPECKIT_SPEC_MEMORY_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` as the override, ensures the socket dir, then runs `mcp-server/dist/spec-memory-cli.js` with inherited stdio. |\n110: | `code-index.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-code-index. Same guard pattern (`SPECKIT_CODE_INDEX_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/code-index-cli.js`. Blocked-read payloads render as actionable answers (exit `0`). `detect_changes` `parse_error` exits `64`. |\n111: | `skill-advisor.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-skill-advisor. Same guard pattern (`MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/mcp-server/skill-advisor-cli.js`. Mutation tools require `--trusted` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`. calls are sent untrusted by default. |\n112: | `hf-model-server.cjs` | Loads a transformers embedding model and serves `/api/health` and `/api/embed`. Enforces the loopback bind perimeter guard, socket-dir ownership, request size limits and inference timeouts. |\n113: \n114: Lifecycle parity note: `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` is the hardened reference for persistent launcher logging, detached daemon re-election/adoption, and owner-release-on-shutdown. `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` and `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` currently stop with their child and rely on fresh-session reload plus bridge/respawn paths instead.\n115: \n116: ---\n117: \n118: ## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n119: \n120: | Boundary | Rule |\n121: |---|---|\n122: | Imports | Launchers require `./lib/model-server-supervision.cjs` and `./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs`. The model server requires only Node core plus `@huggingface/transformers` loaded at runtime. |\n123: | Exports | Launchers run as CLI processes. `hf-model-server.cjs` exports `createHfModelServer`, `loadHfModel`, `resolveListenTarget`, `assertLoopbackBindAllowed`, `assertSocketDirOwnership` and `probeSocketResident` for tests and direct callers. |\n124: | Ownership | This folder owns process bootstrap, lease arbitration and the embedding HTTP surface. MCP request handling, schemas and tools live in each server's own skill directory under `.opencode/skills/`. |\n125: \n126: Main flow:\n127: \n128: ```text\n129: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n130: │ OpenCode runtime spawns mk-*-launcher    │\n131: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n132:                   │\n133:                   ▼\n134: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n135: │ load .env.local / .env, refresh paths    │\n136: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n137:                   │\n138:                   ▼\n139: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n140: │ build dist if artifacts stale            │\n141: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n142:                   │\n143:                   ▼\n144: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n145: │ acquire bootstrap + respawn lease        │\n146: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n147:                   │\n148:                   ▼\n149: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n150: │ spawn MCP child, bridge stdio to socket  │\n151: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n152:                   │\n153:                   ▼\n154: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n155: │ runtime talks to the live daemon         │\n156: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n157: ```\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: ## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n162: \n163: | Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n164: |---|---|---|\n165: | `node .opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the mk-spec-memory MCP server. |\n166: | `node .opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the mk-skill-advisor MCP server. |\n167: | `node .opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the mk-code-index MCP server. |\n168: | `node .opencode/bin/spec-memory.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 41 mk-spec-memory tools from a shell (`list-tools` enumerates them offline). |\n169: | `node .opencode/bin/code-index.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 8 mk-code-index tools from a shell. |\n170: | `node .opencode/bin/skill-advisor.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 9 mk-skill-advisor tools from a shell. pass `--trusted` for maintainer mutations. |\n171: | `node .opencode/bin/hf-model-server.cjs` | CLI | Start the local embedding server (via `main`). |\n172: | `createHfModelServer` | Function | Build an embedding server instance with `listen`, `close`, `dispose` and `inject` for tests. |\n173: | `assertLoopbackBindAllowed` | Function | Refuse non-loopback binds unless remote bind plus auth token are set. |\n174: | `bash .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh <runtime> [args]` | CLI | Launch an AI session in its own git worktree + branch + isolated MCP databases. Top-level sessions isolate. orchestrated children (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` or already inside a linked worktree) exec in place. `--dry-run` prints the plan. |\n175: | `bash .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh [--dry-run] [--reap-daemons]` | CLI | Prune merged + clean per-session worktrees and stale socket dirs. report orphan daemons (kill only with `--reap-daemons`). Auto-reap is restricted to proven-inactive exact `work/<runtime>/<slug>` pairs (the whole marker file must match a PID grammar, a malformed marker is treated as ambiguous and the worktree is kept. the branch's runtime/slug must equal the directory basename). `--reap-daemons` signals only when the referenced worktree/DB path is absent and the PID identity still matches. |\n176: | `bash .opencode/bin/worktree-guard.sh` | CLI / SessionStart hook | Detect-and-warn: prints a one-line stderr warning when a top-level session is on shared `main`/`master` instead of an isolated worktree. Non-fatal (always exits 0). silent for children, inside worktrees, non-git dirs, or with `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_GUARD=off`. |\n177: | `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <id> --prompt \"<task>\"` | CLI | Ask whether the compiled router is authoritative for a hub. Returns a legacy sentinel when it is not. |\n178: | `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --all` | CLI | Report per-hub serving authority and a cause code separating expected drift from breakage. |\n179: | `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs [--warn-only] [--json]` | CLI | Fail when a hub's serving manifest no longer matches its inputs, or when the runtime and its authored source disagree. |\n180: | `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs [--check] [--verify] [--finalize <path>] [--revert <path>]` | CLI | Trace the authored closure, publish it atomically, and finalize or revert the retained rollback. |\n181: | `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs <command>` | CLI | Mint, refresh or inspect a hub activation manifest through the library in `lib/`. |\n182: | `node .opencode/bin/check-no-spec-imports.cjs` | CLI | Prove no file here reaches into the spec tree at runtime. |\n183: | `node .opencode/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs` | CLI | Merge the repo's versioned Codex hook set (lifecycle + tool-level guards) into user-global `~/.codex/hooks.json`. Backs up to `.bak-<ts>` first, preserves Superset/user entries, substitutes the repo path, and is idempotent (re-runs add nothing). |\n184: \n185: ### Daemon-backed CLI shims\n186: \n187: The three CLI shims are the dual-stack front door shipped by the MCP-to-CLI transition: the MCP registrations stay unchanged, and the CLI is an additive surface over the same daemons for hooks, cron, CI and transport-down recovery. Usage is uniform across all three: `<shim> <tool_name> [--json '{...}' | --param value] [--format json|text|jsonl] [--timeout-ms N]`, with `list-tools` answering offline (no daemon contact). Flag values are coerced against each tool's input schema, so `--limit 3` arrives as a number, not a string.\n188: \n189: **Exit taxonomy (shared).** `0` success, `1` runtime error, `64` usage/schema error, `69` protocol mismatch or missing/stale dist, `75` retryable daemon error. A `spawnSync` failure in the shim itself also exits `75`.\n190: \n191: **Warm-only and prompt time.** `--warm-only` (or the per-CLI `*_CLI_WARM_ONLY` / `*_CLI_PROMPT_TIME` envs, plus the shared `SPECKIT_CLI_PROMPT_TIME`, `OPENCODE_PROMPT_TIME`, `CODEX_PROMPT_TIME`, `CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_TIME`) makes the CLI probe the daemon and exit `75` instead of cold-spawning it, the contract prompt-time hooks rely on. Without warm-only, a cold daemon is auto-spawned through the matching `mk-*-launcher.cjs`, so non-prompt contexts (scripts, CI) work from a cold start.\n192: \n193: **Dist freshness.** Each shim calls the shared `checkPackageFreshness()` (`system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) to compare its package's watched source files against the built dist entrypoint, exiting `69` with a rebuild instruction when stale. Dev overrides: `SPECKIT_SPEC_MEMORY_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`, `SPECKIT_CODE_INDEX_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`.\n194: \n195: The same shared module tracks 7 dist-producing packages total (the 3 CLI shims' own `mcp_server`s plus `system-spec-kit/{shared,scripts}`, `mcp-code-mode/mcp-server`, and `sk-design/design-md-generator/backend`) and backs three other consumers: `validate.sh`'s `run_node_orchestrator()` fails closed (exit `3`, no auto-rebuild) when the compiled spec-validation orchestrator it depends on is stale. the `sk-code` `claude-posttooluse.sh` PostToolUse hook prints a non-blocking `STALE DIST WARNING` banner when an edit lands in a watched source tree. and the `mk-dist-freshness-guard` OpenCode plugin (`.opencode/plugins/`) surfaces stale packages to the agent via bounded system-context injection (`experimental.chat.system.transform`) plus an append-only `.opencode/logs/dist-freshness-guard.log`, never stdout/stderr, which the TUI would paint over the chat input, refreshed before a Bash call matching `opencode run`/`validate.sh` and once per session on `session.created`. Root cause and full design: `system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/002-spec-data-quality/050-validate-sh-dist-freshness-and-repo-remediation/001-dist-freshness-enforcement` spec folder.\n196: \n197: **Trust (skill-advisor only).** `advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan` and apply-mode `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` require `--trusted` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`. everything else is sent untrusted by default. The daemon-side gate fails closed when transport `_meta` is absent, see the skill-advisor server docs.\n198: \n199: Full env-var detail lives in the MCP server's [`ENV-REFERENCE.md`](../skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/ENV-REFERENCE.md).\n200: \n201: ### Worktree session isolation\n202: \n203: `worktree-session.sh` ends the cross-session contention where every runtime shared one working tree on `main` plus one set of MCP databases. A top-level session gets `.worktrees/<runtime>-<slug>` on `work/<runtime>/<slug>`, with `SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR` + `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR` pointed at per-worktree databases and `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` pointed at a short `~/.spk-wt-sock/<slug>` dir (the daemon's unix socket path would otherwise exceed the platform `sun_path` limit from inside a deep worktree). Shared `node_modules`/`dist` are symlinked from the main checkout, so there is no per-worktree reinstall or rebuild. Adversarial inputs are rejected before they can act: a runtime identity that cannot form a legal Git ref is refused before `worktree add`, and any `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_SHARED_PATHS` entry with `..`/absolute components is rejected, source and destination are canonicalized and containment-checked so a shared-path copy can never delete or symlink outside the worktree.\n204: \n205: **Child suppression.** Orchestrated children must NOT create their own worktree. Two signals make the wrapper exec in place: the env var `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (which the wrapper exports for its own descendants, and which cli-* dispatch recipes should set when spawning a child runtime), and a structural backstop (`git --git-dir` differs from `--git-common-dir`, i.e. already inside a linked worktree). An unknown signal defaults to top-level (isolate), the safe failure mode.\n206: \n207: **Spec-gate enforce neutralization.** Every `exec_in_place` path (both child signals above) also exports `MK_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0` before handing off to the runtime, so a child cannot inherit an enforced spec-mutation gate from its parent shell. This is belt-and-suspenders: the spec-gate core independently treats `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` as a complete no-op in both classify and enforce, so a leaked enforce env is harmless even without this wrapper. See the [spec-gate core reference](../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec-gate/README.md) for the shared contract.\n208: \n209: To make a runtime isolate by default, alias its launch through the wrapper, e.g. `alias claude='bash /abs/path/.opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh claude'`. See [`sk-git`](../skills/sk-git/SKILL.md) §3 for how this relates to the in-session worktree ask-first rule.\n210: \n211: **Backstop warning.** For sessions that still start directly (no alias), add `worktree-guard.sh` as a SessionStart hook step so the operator is warned when a top-level session lands on shared `main`. It is detect-and-warn only, it never relocates or blocks the session.\n212: \n213: ---\n214: \n215: ## 7. VALIDATION\n216: \n217: Run from the repository root.\n218: \n219: ```bash\n220: node -e \"require('./.opencode/bin/hf-model-server.cjs')\"\n221: node -e \"require('./.opencode/bin/lib/model-server-supervision.cjs')\"\n222: node .opencode/bin/spec-memory.cjs list-tools --format text | head -3\n223: node .opencode/bin/code-index.cjs list-tools --format text | head -3\n224: node .opencode/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format text | head -3\n225: node .opencode/bin/cli-offline-smoke.cjs --format text          # daemon-free: list-tools counts 41/8/9, cwd-independent\n226: node .opencode/bin/cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke.cjs --format text    # daemon-free: CLI failure contract (exit 64/69/75)\n227: bash -n .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh\n228: \n229: # Compiled routing\n230: node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs                     # every hub fresh, runtime matches source\n231: node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --all              # per-hub serving authority and cause code\n232: node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --check              # authored closure resolves every hub\n233: node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --verify             # promoted closure resolves with no spec reads\n234: node .opencode/bin/check-no-spec-imports.cjs                    # nothing here imports from the spec tree\n235: node .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs       # publication lifecycle suite\n236: \n237: # Vitest suites for this folder, run from .opencode\n238: npx vitest run --config vitest.config.bin.ts\n239: bash -n .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\n240: AI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh --dry-run claude   # must report exec-in-place, no worktree\n241: ```\n242: \n243: Expected result: each `.cjs` module loads without throwing. each CLI shim lists tool names offline and exits 0. both daemon-free smokes pass (offline tool counts + the failure-contract exit taxonomy). both shell scripts pass `bash -n`. the child dry-run reports it would exec in place without creating a worktree.\n244: \n245: ---\n246: \n247: ## 8. RELATED\n248: \n249: - [`lib/`](lib/README.md)\n250: - [`system-spec-kit MCP server`](../skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/)\n251: - [`system-skill-advisor MCP server`](../skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/)\n252: - [`system-code-graph skill`](../skills/system-code-graph/)\n\n(End of file - total 252 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"bin: MCP Launchers, Daemon CLIs, Compiled Routing and Repo Tooling\"\ndescription: \"Executable entrypoints for the OpenCode runtime: three MCP launchers and their daemon-backed CLI shims, the local embedding server, the compiled-routing serving and publication tools, and the git, worktree and hook helpers.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"mcp launcher\"\n  - \"hf model server\"\n  - \"mk-spec-memory launcher\"\n  - \"spec-memory cli\"\n  - \"code-index cli\"\n  - \"skill-advisor cli\"\n  - \"compiled route cli\"\n  - \"compiled routing runtime\"\n---\n\n# bin: MCP Launchers, Daemon CLIs, Compiled Routing and Repo Tooling\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`bin/` holds the executable entrypoints that the OpenCode runtime spawns to start each MCP server, plus the daemon-backed CLI shims that reach the same servers from a shell. Three launchers wrap the spec-kit, skill-advisor and code-graph MCP servers. three CLI shims (`spec-memory.cjs`, `code-index.cjs`, `skill-advisor.cjs`) front the same daemons over the IPC socket. one process is the local HuggingFace embedding server that serves `hf-local` vector requests over a Unix domain socket or TCP loopback.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"bin: MCP Launchers, Daemon CLIs, Compiled Routing and Repo Tooling\"\ndescription: \"Executable entrypoints for the OpenCode runtime: three MCP launchers and their daemon-backed CLI shims, the local embedding server, the compiled-routing serving and publication tools, and the git, worktree and hook helpers.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"mcp launcher\"\n  - \"hf model server\"\n  - \"mk-spec-memory launcher\"\n  - \"spec-memory cli\"\n  - \"code-index cli\"\n  - \"skill-advisor cli\"\n  - \"compiled route cli\"\n  - \"compiled routing runtime\"\n---\n\n# bin: MCP Launchers, Daemon CLIs, Compiled Routing and Repo Tooling\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`bin/` holds the executable entrypoints that the OpenCode runtime spawns to start each MCP server, plus the daemon-backed CLI shims that reach the same servers from a shell. Three launchers wrap the spec-kit, skill-advisor and code-graph MCP servers. three CLI shims (`spec-memory.cjs`, `code-index.cjs`, `skill-advisor.cjs`) front the same daemons over the IPC socket. one process is the local HuggingFace embedding server that serves `hf-local` vector requests over a Unix domain socket or TCP loopback.\n\nCurrent state:\n\n- Each launcher loads project-local `.env.local` / `.env`, ensures the server's `dist/` artifacts are built and current, serializes concurrent starts with a filesystem bootstrap lock, then spawns the MCP child and bridges stdio to the running daemon.\n- The three CLI shims run the built daemon-backed CLIs (`spec-memory` 41 tools, `code-index` 8 tools, `skill-advisor` 9 tools) against the **same unchanged daemons** the MCP registrations use, a dual-stack surface, not a replacement. Each shim enforces a dist-freshness guard (exit `69` on missing/stale dist, with a per-CLI `*_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), defaults `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to the short `/tmp/<service>` directory, and refuses a socket path over the Darwin `sun_path` limit.\n- The freshness check itself is a shared module, not per-shim logic: all three shims call `checkPackageFreshness()` from [`system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/dist-freshness.cjs`](../skills/system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/dist-freshness.cjs), which also backs `validate.sh`'s hard staleness backstop, the `sk-code` PostToolUse hook, and the `mk-dist-freshness-guard` OpenCode plugin, one source of truth for \"is this package's dist current\" across all four call sites. See §6 \"Dist freshness\" for the full package table and consumer list.\n- `hf-model-server.cjs` loads a transformers model and answers `/api/health` and `/api/embed` requests. It refuses any non-loopback bind unless the operator sets `HF_EMBED_ALLOW_REMOTE_BIND=1` and supplies `HF_EMBED_AUTH_TOKEN`, and it asserts ownership of the socket directory before listening.\n- Shared launcher behavior (model-server supervision, stdio-to-socket bridging, sidecar env allowlist) lives in `lib/`. The CLI shims' dist entrypoints reuse `lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs` for socket-path resolution and warm-daemon probes.\n- A second family serves and publishes **compiled routing**. `compiled-route.cjs` is the runtime front door a hub calls to ask whether the compiled router is authoritative for it, falling back to legacy routing when it is not. `compiled-route-status.cjs` reports per-hub serving state with a cause code that separates expected drift from breakage. `compiled-route-guard.cjs` is the gate: it fails when a hub's activation manifest no longer matches what its routing inputs compile to, or when the promoted runtime and its authored source disagree. `compiled-route-sync.cjs` publishes a new closure by tracing, staging, verifying, swapping and then finalizing or reverting. `compiled-route-manifest.cjs` is a thin CLI over the activation-manifest library in `lib/`.\n- `check-no-spec-imports.cjs` proves the durable invariant behind that family: nothing under `bin/` reaches into `.opencode/specs/` at runtime, so the serving path cannot break when the authored tree moves.\n- The remaining files are repository tooling. `worktree-*.sh` launch, prune, guard and report on per-session git worktrees. `git-sync.sh` and `git-live-follow.sh` back the continuous-integration workflow. `check-git-hooks.sh` warns at session start when git hooks are missing or drifted, and `install-codex-hooks.mjs` merges the versioned Codex hook set into the user-global config.\n- Launcher reliability knobs, persistent log, lease-probe reap hardening, the mk-code-index reconnecting proxy, the Stop-hook orphan-sweep fallback, and default-on daemon re-election for mk-spec-memory, are operator-tunable via `SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_LOG`, `SPECKIT_LEASE_PROBE_RETRIES`, `SPECKIT_STOP_HOOK_ORPHAN_SWEEP`, and `SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION`. see the MCP server's [`ENV-REFERENCE.md`](../skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/ENV-REFERENCE.md).\n\n---\n\n## 2. ARCHITECTURE\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│                              bin/                                 │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯\n\n┌──────────────┐     ┌──────────────────────┐     ┌────────────────┐\n│ OpenCode     │ ──▶ │ mk-*-launcher.cjs    │ ──▶ │ MCP server     │\n│ runtime      │     │ env + build + lock   │     │ dist child     │\n└──────────────┘     └──────────┬───────────┘     └────────────────┘\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                     ┌──────────────────────┐\n                     │ lib/                 │\n                     │ supervision + bridge │\n                     └──────────┬───────────┘\n                                │ (spec-memory + advisor only)\n                                ▼\n                     ┌──────────────────────┐     ┌────────────────┐\n                     │ hf-model-server.cjs  │ ──▶ │ transformers   │\n                     │ /api/embed + health  │     │ embedding model│\n                     └──────────────────────┘     └────────────────┘\n\nDependency direction: launchers ───▶ lib/ ───▶ hf-model-server.cjs\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nbin/\n+-- mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs    # Launches mk-spec-memory MCP, owns shared hf-model-server lease\n+-- mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs  # Launches mk-skill-advisor MCP, optional model-server supervision\n+-- mk-code-index-launcher.cjs     # Launches mk-code-index MCP, maintainer-mode INDEX_* override\n+-- spec-memory.cjs                # Daemon-backed CLI shim for mk-spec-memory (41 tools)\n+-- code-index.cjs                 # Daemon-backed CLI shim for mk-code-index (8 tools)\n+-- skill-advisor.cjs              # Daemon-backed CLI shim for mk-skill-advisor (9 tools)\n+-- cli-offline-smoke.cjs          # Daemon-free smoke: list-tools counts (41/8/9), cwd-independent\n+-- cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke.cjs    # Daemon-free smoke: CLI failure contract (exit 64/69/75, parseable envelopes)\n+-- cli-offline-smoke.test.cjs     # Test runner asserting cli-offline-smoke.cjs passes\n+-- hf-model-server.cjs            # Local HTTP/UDS HuggingFace embedding server\n+-- worktree-session.sh            # Launch an AI session in an isolated git worktree + branch + DBs\n+-- worktree-reaper.sh             # Prune merged/clean per-session worktrees + stale socket dirs\n+-- worktree-guard.sh              # SessionStart detect-and-warn when a top-level session is on shared main\n+-- worktree-status.sh             # Reports worktree, branch and sync state\n+-- git-sync.sh                    # Autosync helper for the git continuous-integration workflow\n+-- git-live-follow.sh             # Live-follow watcher for the same workflow\n+-- check-git-hooks.sh             # SessionStart guard warning on missing or drifted git hooks\n+-- install-codex-hooks.mjs        # Merges the versioned Codex hook set into the user-global config\n+-- speckit-completion.cjs         # Completion-state CLI over the runtime-neutral core\n+-- compiled-route.cjs             # Runtime front door: is the compiled router authoritative for a hub\n+-- compiled-route-status.cjs      # Per-hub serving status with a cause code separating drift from breakage\n+-- compiled-route-guard.cjs       # Freshness gate: serving matches inputs, runtime matches source\n+-- compiled-route-manifest.cjs    # CLI over the activation-manifest library in lib/\n+-- compiled-route-sync.cjs        # Publication tool: trace, stage, verify, swap, finalize or revert\n+-- check-no-spec-imports.cjs      # Proves nothing here reaches into the spec tree at runtime\n+-- compiled-routing-*.vitest.ts   # Routing foundation and flag-propagation suites\n+-- mk-code-index-launcher-*.vitest.ts  # Launcher lease, registry and WAL coverage\n+-- tests/                         # node:test suite for the publication lifecycle\n+-- lib/                           # Shared supervision, IPC bridge, env allowlist, routing library\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-spec-memory MCP child. Manages the shared hf-model-server lease, respawn locks, and reaping a dead lease child before respawn. |\n| `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-skill-advisor MCP child. Loads model-server supervision when enabled, enforces a strict single-writer lease, and rebuilds `dist/` from `handlers`, `lib`, `schemas`, `tools` when stale. |\n| `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-code-index MCP child. Applies the maintainer-mode `INDEX_*` override, migrates the code-graph database back to the skill-local path, and sets `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR` for the child. |\n| `spec-memory.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-spec-memory. Checks dist freshness and exits `69` when stale, with `SPECKIT_SPEC_MEMORY_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` as the override, ensures the socket dir, then runs `mcp-server/dist/spec-memory-cli.js` with inherited stdio. |\n| `code-index.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-code-index. Same guard pattern (`SPECKIT_CODE_INDEX_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/code-index-cli.js`. Blocked-read payloads render as actionable answers (exit `0`). `detect_changes` `parse_error` exits `64`. |\n| `skill-advisor.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-skill-advisor. Same guard pattern (`MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/mcp-server/skill-advisor-cli.js`. Mutation tools require `--trusted` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`. calls are sent untrusted by default. |\n| `hf-model-server.cjs` | Loads a transformers embedding model and serves `/api/health` and `/api/embed`. Enforces the loopback bind perimeter guard, socket-dir ownership, request size limits and inference timeouts. |\n\nLifecycle parity note: `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` is the hardened reference for persistent launcher logging, detached daemon re-election/adoption, and owner-release-on-shutdown. `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` and `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` currently stop with their child and rely on fresh-session reload plus bridge/respawn paths instead.\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n\n| Boundary | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Imports | Launchers require `./lib/model-server-supervision.cjs` and `./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs`. The model server requires only Node core plus `@huggingface/transformers` loaded at runtime. |\n| Exports | Launchers run as CLI processes. `hf-model-server.cjs` exports `createHfModelServer`, `loadHfModel`, `resolveListenTarget`, `assertLoopbackBindAllowed`, `assertSocketDirOwnership` and `probeSocketResident` for tests and direct callers. |\n| Ownership | This folder owns process bootstrap, lease arbitration and the embedding HTTP surface. MCP request handling, schemas and tools live in each server's own skill directory under `.opencode/skills/`. |\n\nMain flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ OpenCode runtime spawns mk-*-launcher    │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ load .env.local / .env, refresh paths    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ build dist if artifacts stale            │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ acquire bootstrap + respawn lease        │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ spawn MCP child, bridge stdio to socket  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ runtime talks to the live daemon         │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. ENTRYPOINTS\n\n| Entrypoint | Type | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| `node .opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the mk-spec-memory MCP server. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the mk-skill-advisor MCP server. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` | CLI | Start the mk-code-index MCP server. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/spec-memory.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 41 mk-spec-memory tools from a shell (`list-tools` enumerates them offline). |\n| `node .opencode/bin/code-index.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 8 mk-code-index tools from a shell. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/skill-advisor.cjs <tool> [flags]` | CLI | Call any of the 9 mk-skill-advisor tools from a shell. pass `--trusted` for maintainer mutations. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/hf-model-server.cjs` | CLI | Start the local embedding server (via `main`). |\n| `createHfModelServer` | Function | Build an embedding server instance with `listen`, `close`, `dispose` and `inject` for tests. |\n| `assertLoopbackBindAllowed` | Function | Refuse non-loopback binds unless remote bind plus auth token are set. |\n| `bash .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh <runtime> [args]` | CLI | Launch an AI session in its own git worktree + branch + isolated MCP databases. Top-level sessions isolate. orchestrated children (`AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` or already inside a linked worktree) exec in place. `--dry-run` prints the plan. |\n| `bash .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh [--dry-run] [--reap-daemons]` | CLI | Prune merged + clean per-session worktrees and stale socket dirs. report orphan daemons (kill only with `--reap-daemons`). Auto-reap is restricted to proven-inactive exact `work/<runtime>/<slug>` pairs (the whole marker file must match a PID grammar, a malformed marker is treated as ambiguous and the worktree is kept. the branch's runtime/slug must equal the directory basename). `--reap-daemons` signals only when the referenced worktree/DB path is absent and the PID identity still matches. |\n| `bash .opencode/bin/worktree-guard.sh` | CLI / SessionStart hook | Detect-and-warn: prints a one-line stderr warning when a top-level session is on shared `main`/`master` instead of an isolated worktree. Non-fatal (always exits 0). silent for children, inside worktrees, non-git dirs, or with `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_GUARD=off`. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <id> --prompt \"<task>\"` | CLI | Ask whether the compiled router is authoritative for a hub. Returns a legacy sentinel when it is not. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --all` | CLI | Report per-hub serving authority and a cause code separating expected drift from breakage. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs [--warn-only] [--json]` | CLI | Fail when a hub's serving manifest no longer matches its inputs, or when the runtime and its authored source disagree. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs [--check] [--verify] [--finalize <path>] [--revert <path>]` | CLI | Trace the authored closure, publish it atomically, and finalize or revert the retained rollback. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs <command>` | CLI | Mint, refresh or inspect a hub activation manifest through the library in `lib/`. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/check-no-spec-imports.cjs` | CLI | Prove no file here reaches into the spec tree at runtime. |\n| `node .opencode/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs` | CLI | Merge the repo's versioned Codex hook set (lifecycle + tool-level guards) into user-global `~/.codex/hooks.json`. Backs up to `.bak-<ts>` first, preserves Superset/user entries, substitutes the repo path, and is idempotent (re-runs add nothing). |\n\n### Daemon-backed CLI shims\n\nThe three CLI shims are the dual-stack front door shipped by the MCP-to-CLI transition: the MCP registrations stay unchanged, and the CLI is an additive surface over the same daemons for hooks, cron, CI and transport-down recovery. Usage is uniform across all three: `<shim> <tool_name> [--json '{...}' | --param value] [--format json|text|jsonl] [--timeout-ms N]`, with `list-tools` answering offline (no daemon contact). Flag values are coerced against each tool's input schema, so `--limit 3` arrives as a number, not a string.\n\n**Exit taxonomy (shared).** `0` success, `1` runtime error, `64` usage/schema error, `69` protocol mismatch or missing/stale dist, `75` retryable daemon error. A `spawnSync` failure in the shim itself also exits `75`.\n\n**Warm-only and prompt time.** `--warm-only` (or the per-CLI `*_CLI_WARM_ONLY` / `*_CLI_PROMPT_TIME` envs, plus the shared `SPECKIT_CLI_PROMPT_TIME`, `OPENCODE_PROMPT_TIME`, `CODEX_PROMPT_TIME`, `CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_TIME`) makes the CLI probe the daemon and exit `75` instead of cold-spawning it, the contract prompt-time hooks rely on. Without warm-only, a cold daemon is auto-spawned through the matching `mk-*-launcher.cjs`, so non-prompt contexts (scripts, CI) work from a cold start.\n\n**Dist freshness.** Each shim calls the shared `checkPackageFreshness()` (`system-spec-kit/scripts/lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) to compare its package's watched source files against the built dist entrypoint, exiting `69` with a rebuild instruction when stale. Dev overrides: `SPECKIT_SPEC_MEMORY_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`, `SPECKIT_CODE_INDEX_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`, `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1`.\n\nThe same shared module tracks 7 dist-producing packages total (the 3 CLI shims' own `mcp_server`s plus `system-spec-kit/{shared,scripts}`, `mcp-code-mode/mcp-server`, and `sk-design/design-md-generator/backend`) and backs three other consumers: `validate.sh`'s `run_node_orchestrator()` fails closed (exit `3`, no auto-rebuild) when the compiled spec-validation orchestrator it depends on is stale. the `sk-code` `claude-posttooluse.sh` PostToolUse hook prints a non-blocking `STALE DIST WARNING` banner when an edit lands in a watched source tree. and the `mk-dist-freshness-guard` OpenCode plugin (`.opencode/plugins/`) surfaces stale packages to the agent via bounded system-context injection (`experimental.chat.system.transform`) plus an append-only `.opencode/logs/dist-freshness-guard.log`, never stdout/stderr, which the TUI would paint over the chat input, refreshed before a Bash call matching `opencode run`/`validate.sh` and once per session on `session.created`. Root cause and full design: `system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/002-spec-data-quality/050-validate-sh-dist-freshness-and-repo-remediation/001-dist-freshness-enforcement` spec folder.\n\n**Trust (skill-advisor only).** `advisor_rebuild`, `skill_graph_scan` and apply-mode `skill_graph_propagate_enhances` require `--trusted` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`. everything else is sent untrusted by default. The daemon-side gate fails closed when transport `_meta` is absent, see the skill-advisor server docs.\n\nFull env-var detail lives in the MCP server's [`ENV-REFERENCE.md`](../skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/ENV-REFERENCE.md).\n\n### Worktree session isolation\n\n`worktree-session.sh` ends the cross-session contention where every runtime shared one working tree on `main` plus one set of MCP databases. A top-level session gets `.worktrees/<runtime>-<slug>` on `work/<runtime>/<slug>`, with `SPEC_KIT_DB_DIR` + `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR` pointed at per-worktree databases and `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` pointed at a short `~/.spk-wt-sock/<slug>` dir (the daemon's unix socket path would otherwise exceed the platform `sun_path` limit from inside a deep worktree). Shared `node_modules`/`dist` are symlinked from the main checkout, so there is no per-worktree reinstall or rebuild. Adversarial inputs are rejected before they can act: a runtime identity that cannot form a legal Git ref is refused before `worktree add`, and any `SPECKIT_WORKTREE_SHARED_PATHS` entry with `..`/absolute components is rejected, source and destination are canonicalized and containment-checked so a shared-path copy can never delete or symlink outside the worktree.\n\n**Child suppression.** Orchestrated children must NOT create their own worktree. Two signals make the wrapper exec in place: the env var `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` (which the wrapper exports for its own descendants, and which cli-* dispatch recipes should set when spawning a child runtime), and a structural backstop (`git --git-dir` differs from `--git-common-dir`, i.e. already inside a linked worktree). An unknown signal defaults to top-level (isolate), the safe failure mode.\n\n**Spec-gate enforce neutralization.** Every `exec_in_place` path (both child signals above) also exports `MK_SPEC_GATE_ENFORCE=0` before handing off to the runtime, so a child cannot inherit an enforced spec-mutation gate from its parent shell. This is belt-and-suspenders: the spec-gate core independently treats `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` as a complete no-op in both classify and enforce, so a leaked enforce env is harmless even without this wrapper. See the [spec-gate core reference](../skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/lib/spec-gate/README.md) for the shared contract.\n\nTo make a runtime isolate by default, alias its launch through the wrapper, e.g. `alias claude='bash /abs/path/.opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh claude'`. See [`sk-git`](../skills/sk-git/SKILL.md) §3 for how this relates to the in-session worktree ask-first rule.\n\n**Backstop warning.** For sessions that still start directly (no alias), add `worktree-guard.sh` as a SessionStart hook step so the operator is warned when a top-level session lands on shared `main`. It is detect-and-warn only, it never relocates or blocks the session.\n\n---\n\n## 7. VALIDATION\n\nRun from the repository root.\n\n```bash\nnode -e \"require('./.opencode/bin/hf-model-server.cjs')\"\nnode -e \"require('./.opencode/bin/lib/model-server-supervision.cjs')\"\nnode .opencode/bin/spec-memory.cjs list-tools --format text | head -3\nnode .opencode/bin/code-index.cjs list-tools --format text | head -3\nnode .opencode/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format text | head -3\nnode .opencode/bin/cli-offline-smoke.cjs --format text          # daemon-free: list-tools counts 41/8/9, cwd-independent\nnode .opencode/bin/cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke.cjs --format text    # daemon-free: CLI failure contract (exit 64/69/75)\nbash -n .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh\n\n# Compiled routing\nnode .opencode/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs                     # every hub fresh, runtime matches source\nnode .opencode/bin/compiled-route-status.cjs --all              # per-hub serving authority and cause code\nnode .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --check              # authored closure resolves every hub\nnode .opencode/bin/compiled-route-sync.cjs --verify             # promoted closure resolves with no spec reads\nnode .opencode/bin/check-no-spec-imports.cjs                    # nothing here imports from the spec tree\nnode .opencode/bin/tests/compiled-route-manifest.test.cjs       # publication lifecycle suite\n\n# Vitest suites for this folder, run from .opencode\nnpx vitest run --config vitest.config.bin.ts\nbash -n .opencode/bin/worktree-reaper.sh\nAI_SESSION_CHILD=1 bash .opencode/bin/worktree-session.sh --dry-run claude   # must report exec-in-place, no worktree\n```\n\nExpected result: each `.cjs` module loads without throwing. each CLI shim lists tool names offline and exits 0. both daemon-free smokes pass (offline tool counts + the failure-contract exit taxonomy). both shell scripts pass `bash -n`. the child dry-run reports it would exec in place without creating a worktree.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RELATED\n\n- [`lib/`](lib/README.md)\n- [`system-spec-kit MCP server`](../skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/)\n- [`system-skill-advisor MCP server`](../skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/)\n- [`system-code-graph skill`](../skills/system-code-graph/)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":252,"totalLines":252,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/bin/README.md","time":{"start":1785133889136,"end":1785133889142}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01ecde0a1a76a560016a66fb40f40481918496569838a7e520"}},"id":"prt_fa245763d0019SVFcos085V78r","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa2451ace001RiLa50jjImprPx"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133889156,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PSuOsspxTf7RwZwV6G81DqpE","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n3: // ║ CLI: CANONICAL COMPILED-ROUTE MANIFEST                                  ║\n4: // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8: // 1. IMPORTS\n9: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10: \n11: const {\n12:   checkCanonicalManifestFreshness,\n13:   mintCanonicalManifest,\n14:   refreshCanonicalManifest,\n15: } = require('./lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs');\n16: \n17: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n18: // 2. CONSTANTS\n19: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n20: \n21: const USAGE = 'usage: compiled-route-manifest.cjs <mint|refresh|freshness> '\n22:   + '--hub <hub-id> --skill-root <path> [--pretty]';\n23: \n24: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n25: // 3. HELPERS\n26: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n27: \n28: function parseArgs(argv) {\n29:   const verb = argv[0];\n30:   if (verb !== 'mint' && verb !== 'refresh' && verb !== 'freshness') return null;\n31:   const values = { verb, pretty: false };\n32:   const seen = new Set();\n33:   for (let index = 1; index < argv.length; index += 1) {\n34:     const arg = argv[index];\n35:     if (arg === '--pretty') {\n36:       if (seen.has(arg)) return null;\n37:       seen.add(arg);\n38:       values.pretty = true;\n39:       continue;\n40:     }\n41:     if (arg !== '--hub' && arg !== '--skill-root') return null;\n42:     if (seen.has(arg) || index + 1 >= argv.length || argv[index + 1].startsWith('--')) {\n43:       return null;\n44:     }\n45:     seen.add(arg);\n46:     values[arg === '--hub' ? 'hubId' : 'skillRoot'] = argv[index + 1];\n47:     index += 1;\n48:   }\n49:   if (!values.hubId || !values.skillRoot) return null;\n50:   return values;\n51: }\n52: \n53: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n54: // 4. CLI\n55: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56: \n57: /**\n58:  * Run one manifest operation and emit a single JSON record.\n59:  *\n60:  * @param {string[]} argv - CLI arguments after the executable path.\n61:  * @returns {number} Process exit code.\n62:  */\n63: function main(argv = process.argv.slice(2)) {\n64:   const parsed = parseArgs(argv);\n65:   if (!parsed) {\n66:     process.stderr.write(`${USAGE}\\n`);\n67:     return 2;\n68:   }\n69:   const input = { hubId: parsed.hubId, skillRoot: parsed.skillRoot };\n70:   const result = parsed.verb === 'mint'\n71:     ? mintCanonicalManifest(input)\n72:     : parsed.verb === 'refresh'\n73:       ? refreshCanonicalManifest(input)\n74:       : checkCanonicalManifestFreshness(input);\n75:   const output = parsed.pretty ? JSON.stringify(result, null, 2) : JSON.stringify(result);\n76:   process.stdout.write(`${output}\\n`);\n77:   return result.manifestValid && result.fresh ? 0 : 1;\n78: }\n79: \n80: if (require.main === module) {\n81:   try {\n82:     process.exitCode = main();\n83:   } catch {\n84:     process.stderr.write('[compiled-route-manifest] operation failed\\n');\n85:     process.exitCode = 1;\n86:   }\n87: }\n88: \n89: module.exports = { main, parseArgs, USAGE };\n\n(End of file - total 89 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ CLI: CANONICAL COMPILED-ROUTE MANIFEST                                  ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst {\n  checkCanonicalManifestFreshness,\n  mintCanonicalManifest,\n  refreshCanonicalManifest,\n} = require('./lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs","text":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ CLI: CANONICAL COMPILED-ROUTE MANIFEST                                  ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst {\n  checkCanonicalManifestFreshness,\n  mintCanonicalManifest,\n  refreshCanonicalManifest,\n} = require('./lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst USAGE = 'usage: compiled-route-manifest.cjs <mint|refresh|freshness> '\n  + '--hub <hub-id> --skill-root <path> [--pretty]';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction parseArgs(argv) {\n  const verb = argv[0];\n  if (verb !== 'mint' && verb !== 'refresh' && verb !== 'freshness') return null;\n  const values = { verb, pretty: false };\n  const seen = new Set();\n  for (let index = 1; index < argv.length; index += 1) {\n    const arg = argv[index];\n    if (arg === '--pretty') {\n      if (seen.has(arg)) return null;\n      seen.add(arg);\n      values.pretty = true;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (arg !== '--hub' && arg !== '--skill-root') return null;\n    if (seen.has(arg) || index + 1 >= argv.length || argv[index + 1].startsWith('--')) {\n      return null;\n    }\n    seen.add(arg);\n    values[arg === '--hub' ? 'hubId' : 'skillRoot'] = argv[index + 1];\n    index += 1;\n  }\n  if (!values.hubId || !values.skillRoot) return null;\n  return values;\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. CLI\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Run one manifest operation and emit a single JSON record.\n *\n * @param {string[]} argv - CLI arguments after the executable path.\n * @returns {number} Process exit code.\n */\nfunction main(argv = process.argv.slice(2)) {\n  const parsed = parseArgs(argv);\n  if (!parsed) {\n    process.stderr.write(`${USAGE}\\n`);\n    return 2;\n  }\n  const input = { hubId: parsed.hubId, skillRoot: parsed.skillRoot };\n  const result = parsed.verb === 'mint'\n    ? mintCanonicalManifest(input)\n    : parsed.verb === 'refresh'\n      ? refreshCanonicalManifest(input)\n      : checkCanonicalManifestFreshness(input);\n  const output = parsed.pretty ? JSON.stringify(result, null, 2) : JSON.stringify(result);\n  process.stdout.write(`${output}\\n`);\n  return result.manifestValid && result.fresh ? 0 : 1;\n}\n\nif (require.main === module) {\n  try {\n    process.exitCode = main();\n  } catch {\n    process.stderr.write('[compiled-route-manifest] operation failed\\n');\n    process.exitCode = 1;\n  }\n}\n\nmodule.exports = { main, parseArgs, USAGE };","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":89,"totalLines":89,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/bin/compiled-route-manifest.cjs","time":{"start":1785133889148,"end":1785133889154}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01ecde0a1a76a560016a66fb40f4148191b1a42cb23b9685fc"}},"id":"prt_fa2457671001Famj76NjMJrt8I","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa2451ace001RiLa50jjImprPx"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133889163,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_APACkwMdWpaAJ3MZ2pqyxptr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n2: // ║ LIBRARY: CANONICAL COMPILED-ROUTE MANIFEST                              ║\n3: // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n4: 'use strict';\n5: \n6: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n7: // 1. IMPORTS\n8: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9: \n10: const fs = require('node:fs');\n11: const path = require('node:path');\n12: const crypto = require('node:crypto');\n13: \n14: const layout = require('./compiled-route-layout.cjs');\n15: \n16: const RUNTIME_ROOT = path.join(__dirname, 'compiled-routing');\n17: \n18: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: // 2. CONSTANTS\n20: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: \n22: const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..');\n23: const PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH = layout.publicationLockPathFor(RUNTIME_ROOT);\n24: const HUB_ID_PATTERN = /^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/;\n25: const HASH_PATTERN = /^[a-f0-9]{64}$/;\n26: const MANIFEST_KEYS = ['schemaVersion', 'selectedPolicy', 'servingAuthority', 'shadowOnly'];\n27: const SELECTED_POLICY_KEYS = ['effectivePolicyHash', 'generation'];\n28: \n29: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n30: // 3. HELPERS\n31: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n32: \n33: function contractError(causeCode) {\n34:   const error = new Error(causeCode);\n35:   error.causeCode = causeCode;\n36:   return error;\n37: }\n38: \n39: let cachedRuntimeContext = null;\n40: \n41: function clearRuntimeRequireCache() {\n42:   const root = path.resolve(RUNTIME_ROOT);\n43:   for (const cachePath of Object.keys(require.cache)) {\n44:     const relative = path.relative(root, cachePath);\n45:     if (relative === '' || (relative && !relative.startsWith('..') && !path.isAbsolute(relative))) {\n46:       delete require.cache[cachePath];\n47:     }\n48:   }\n49: }\n50: \n51: function runtimePaths({ allowLegacyFallback = false } = {}) {\n52:   return layout.resolveRuntimePaths(RUNTIME_ROOT, { allowLegacyFallback });\n53: }\n54: \n55: function activationRoot() {\n56:   return runtimePaths({ allowLegacyFallback: true }).activationRoot;\n57: }\n58: \n59: function runtimeContext() {\n60:   const binding = runtimePaths();\n61:   if (!binding) throw contractError('compile-error');\n62:   if (!cachedRuntimeContext || cachedRuntimeContext.rootIdentity !== binding.rootIdentity) {\n63:     clearRuntimeRequireCache();\n64:     cachedRuntimeContext = {\n65:       ...binding,\n66:       compiler: require(binding.compilerPath),\n67:       engine: require(binding.enginePath),\n68:     };\n69:   }\n70:   return cachedRuntimeContext;\n71: }\n72: \n73: function sha256(bytes) {\n74:   return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(bytes).digest('hex');\n75: }\n76: \n77: function artifactBytes(value) {\n78:   return runtimeContext().compiler.artifactBytes(value);\n79: }\n80: \n81: // A writer lease whose holder died would otherwise block every future mint and\n82: // refresh forever, with no escape but deleting the file by hand. Reclaim only an\n83: // abandoned WRITER lease: an abandoned publication lease may sit over a runtime\n84: // that is still mid-swap, so that one stays for an operator to clear explicitly.\n85: function abandonedWriterLease() {\n86:   let lock;\n87:   try {\n88:     lock = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH, 'utf8'));\n89:   } catch {\n90:     return false;\n91:   }\n92:   if (!lock || lock.kind !== 'manifest-writer') return false;\n93:   if (!Number.isInteger(lock.pid) || lock.pid === process.pid) return false;\n94:   try {\n95:     process.kill(lock.pid, 0);\n96:     return false;\n97:   } catch (error) {\n98:     return Boolean(error) && error.code === 'ESRCH';\n99:   }\n100: }\n101: \n102: function acquireManifestWriterLease(operation) {\n103:   const token = `writer-${process.pid}-${Date.now()}-${crypto.randomBytes(8).toString('hex')}`;\n104:   const payload = {\n105:     schemaVersion: 'V1',\n106:     kind: 'manifest-writer',\n107:     token,\n108:     operation,\n109:     pid: process.pid,\n110:     createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n111:   };\n112:   const write = () => fs.writeFileSync(\n113:     PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH,\n114:     `${JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2)}\\n`,\n115:     { flag: 'wx', mode: 0o600 },\n116:   );\n117:   try {\n118:     write();\n119:   } catch (error) {\n120:     if (!error || error.code !== 'EEXIST') throw error;\n121:     if (!abandonedWriterLease()) return null;\n122:     try {\n123:       fs.rmSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH);\n124:       write();\n125:     } catch (retryError) {\n126:       if (retryError && retryError.code === 'EEXIST') return null;\n127:       throw retryError;\n128:     }\n129:   }\n130:   return token;\n131: }\n132: \n133: function releaseManifestWriterLease(token) {\n134:   const stats = fs.lstatSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH);\n135:   if (stats.isSymbolicLink() || !stats.isFile()) {\n136:     throw new Error('manifest writer lock is not a real file');\n137:   }\n138:   let lock;\n139:   try {\n140:     lock = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH, 'utf8'));\n141:   } catch {\n142:     throw new Error('manifest writer lock is invalid');\n143:   }\n144:   if (lock.kind !== 'manifest-writer' || lock.token !== token) {\n145:     throw new Error('manifest writer lock ownership changed');\n146:   }\n147:   fs.rmSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH);\n148: }\n149: \n150: function isPlainObject(value) {\n151:   return Boolean(value) && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n152: }\n153: \n154: function hasExactKeys(value, expected) {\n155:   if (!isPlainObject(value)) return false;\n156:   const actual = Object.keys(value).sort();\n157:   return actual.length === expected.length\n158:     && actual.every((key, index) => key === expected[index]);\n159: }\n160: \n161: /**\n162:  * Check whether a hub identifier is safe for canonical activation storage.\n163:  *\n164:  * @param {unknown} hubId - Candidate hub identifier.\n165:  * @returns {boolean} Whether the identifier is canonical hyphen-case.\n166:  */\n167: function isCanonicalHubId(hubId) {\n168:   return typeof hubId === 'string' && HUB_ID_PATTERN.test(hubId);\n169: }\n170: \n171: function isContained(root, candidate) {\n172:   const relative = path.relative(root, candidate);\n173:   return relative === '' || (!relative.startsWith('..') && !path.isAbsolute(relative));\n174: }\n175: \n176: function relativeManifestPath(absolutePath) {\n177:   return path.relative(REPO_ROOT, absolutePath).split(path.sep).join('/');\n178: }\n179: \n180: function selectedPolicyFrom(manifest) {\n181:   if (!manifest || !isPlainObject(manifest.selectedPolicy)) {\n182:     return { effectivePolicyHash: null, generation: null };\n183:   }\n184:   return {\n185:     effectivePolicyHash: manifest.selectedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash ?? null,\n186:     generation: manifest.selectedPolicy.generation ?? null,\n187:   };\n188: }\n189: \n190: function resultRecord({\n191:   hubId,\n192:   causeCode,\n193:   manifestValid = false,\n194:   fresh = false,\n195:   manifest = null,\n196:   manifestFingerprint = null,\n197:   currentPolicyHash = null,\n198:   manifestPath = null,\n199:   created,\n200:   refreshed,\n201: }) {\n202:   const result = {\n203:     hubId: typeof hubId === 'string' ? hubId : null,\n204:     manifestPath,\n205:     manifestValid,\n206:     fresh,\n207:     causeCode,\n208:     selectedPolicy: selectedPolicyFrom(manifest),\n209:     currentPolicyHash,\n210:     manifestFingerprint,\n211:   };\n212:   if (typeof created === 'boolean') result.created = created;\n213:   if (typeof refreshed === 'boolean') result.refreshed = refreshed;\n214:   return result;\n215: }\n216: \n217: function failureRecord(hubId, causeCode, options = {}) {\n218:   let manifestPath = null;\n219:   try {\n220:     manifestPath = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId }).manifestPath;\n221:   } catch {\n222:     // Unsafe identities do not receive a synthesized path.\n223:   }\n224:   return resultRecord({ hubId, causeCode, manifestPath, ...options });\n225: }\n226: \n227: function normalizeCurrentPolicy(currentPolicy) {\n228:   if (!isPlainObject(currentPolicy)) return null;\n229:   const generation = currentPolicy.activationGeneration ?? currentPolicy.generation;\n230:   if (!Number.isSafeInteger(generation) || generation < 1) return null;\n231:   if (!HASH_PATTERN.test(currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash || '')) return null;\n232:   return { effectivePolicyHash: currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash, generation };\n233: }\n234: \n235: function safeManifestLocationExists(absolutePath) {\n236:   const currentActivationRoot = activationRoot();\n237:   let activationStats;\n238:   try {\n239:     activationStats = fs.lstatSync(currentActivationRoot);\n240:   } catch (error) {\n241:     if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;\n242:     throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n243:   }\n244:   if (activationStats.isSymbolicLink() || !activationStats.isDirectory()) {\n245:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n246:   }\n247:   const realActivationRoot = fs.realpathSync(currentActivationRoot);\n248:   const directoryPath = path.dirname(absolutePath);\n249:   let directoryStats;\n250:   try {\n251:     directoryStats = fs.lstatSync(directoryPath);\n252:   } catch (error) {\n253:     if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;\n254:     throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n255:   }\n256:   if (directoryStats.isSymbolicLink() || !directoryStats.isDirectory()) {\n257:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n258:   }\n259:   if (!isContained(realActivationRoot, fs.realpathSync(directoryPath))) {\n260:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n261:   }\n262:   let manifestStats;\n263:   try {\n264:     manifestStats = fs.lstatSync(absolutePath);\n265:   } catch (error) {\n266:     if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;\n267:     throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n268:   }\n269:   if (manifestStats.isSymbolicLink() || !manifestStats.isFile()) {\n270:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n271:   }\n272:   if (!isContained(realActivationRoot, fs.realpathSync(absolutePath))) {\n273:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n274:   }\n275:   return true;\n276: }\n277: \n278: function readManifestBytes(absolutePath) {\n279:   try {\n280:     if (!safeManifestLocationExists(absolutePath)) return null;\n281:     return fs.readFileSync(absolutePath);\n282:   } catch (error) {\n283:     if (error && error.causeCode) throw error;\n284:     if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return null;\n285:     throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n286:   }\n287: }\n288: \n289: /**\n290:  * Validate canonical manifest structure without evaluating policy freshness.\n291:  *\n292:  * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and candidate bytes.\n293:  * @returns {Object} Structural validity, parsed manifest, and fingerprint.\n294:  */\n295: function validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes }) {\n296:   if (!isCanonicalHubId(hubId) || !Buffer.isBuffer(manifestBytes)) {\n297:     return { manifestValid: false, manifest: null, manifestFingerprint: null };\n298:   }\n299:   const manifestFingerprint = sha256(manifestBytes);\n300:   let manifest;\n301:   try {\n302:     manifest = JSON.parse(manifestBytes.toString('utf8'));\n303:   } catch {\n304:     return { manifestValid: false, manifest: null, manifestFingerprint };\n305:   }\n306:   const selectedPolicy = manifest && manifest.selectedPolicy;\n307:   const manifestValid = hasExactKeys(manifest, MANIFEST_KEYS)\n308:     && manifest.schemaVersion === 'V1'\n309:     && (manifest.servingAuthority === 'legacy' || manifest.servingAuthority === 'compiled')\n310:     && typeof manifest.shadowOnly === 'boolean'\n311:     && hasExactKeys(selectedPolicy, SELECTED_POLICY_KEYS)\n312:     && Number.isSafeInteger(selectedPolicy.generation)\n313:     && selectedPolicy.generation >= 1\n314:     && HASH_PATTERN.test(selectedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash || '');\n315:   return { manifestValid, manifest: manifestValid ? manifest : null, manifestFingerprint };\n316: }\n317: \n318: function ensureSafeSkillRoot(hubId, skillRoot) {\n319:   if (typeof skillRoot !== 'string' || !skillRoot.trim()) {\n320:     throw contractError('invalid-input');\n321:   }\n322:   if (skillRoot.includes('\\0') || skillRoot.split(/[\\\\/]+/).includes('..')) {\n323:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n324:   }\n325:   const resolvedRoot = path.resolve(skillRoot);\n326:   let realRoot;\n327:   let rootStats;\n328:   try {\n329:     rootStats = fs.lstatSync(resolvedRoot);\n330:     realRoot = fs.realpathSync(resolvedRoot);\n331:   } catch {\n332:     throw contractError('invalid-input');\n333:   }\n334:   if (rootStats.isSymbolicLink()) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n335:   if (!rootStats.isDirectory()) throw contractError('invalid-input');\n336:   if (path.basename(resolvedRoot) !== hubId || path.basename(realRoot) !== hubId) {\n337:     throw contractError('hub-mismatch');\n338:   }\n339:   return realRoot;\n340: }\n341: \n342: function readOwnedFile(realRoot, fileName) {\n343:   const candidate = path.join(realRoot, fileName);\n344:   if (!isContained(realRoot, candidate)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n345:   let stats;\n346:   try {\n347:     stats = fs.lstatSync(candidate);\n348:   } catch {\n349:     throw contractError('invalid-input');\n350:   }\n351:   if (stats.isSymbolicLink() || !stats.isFile()) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n352:   const realFile = fs.realpathSync(candidate);\n353:   if (!isContained(realRoot, realFile)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n354:   return fs.readFileSync(realFile);\n355: }\n356: \n357: function ensureActivationDirectory(directoryPath) {\n358:   const currentActivationRoot = activationRoot();\n359:   fs.mkdirSync(currentActivationRoot, { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });\n360:   const activationStats = fs.lstatSync(currentActivationRoot);\n361:   if (activationStats.isSymbolicLink() || !activationStats.isDirectory()) {\n362:     throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n363:   }\n364:   const realActivationRoot = fs.realpathSync(currentActivationRoot);\n365:   if (fs.existsSync(directoryPath)) {\n366:     const directoryStats = fs.lstatSync(directoryPath);\n367:     if (directoryStats.isSymbolicLink() || !directoryStats.isDirectory()) {\n368:       throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n369:     }\n370:   }\n371:   fs.mkdirSync(directoryPath, { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });\n372:   const realDirectory = fs.realpathSync(directoryPath);\n373:   if (!isContained(realActivationRoot, realDirectory)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n374: }\n375: \n376: function causeFrom(error, fallback = 'invalid-input') {\n377:   return error && typeof error.causeCode === 'string' ? error.causeCode : fallback;\n378: }\n379: \n380: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n381: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n382: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n383: \n384: /**\n385:  * Resolve the only writable activation-manifest path for a hub.\n386:  *\n387:  * @param {Object} input - Hub identity.\n388:  * @param {string} input.hubId - Hyphen-case hub identifier.\n389:  * @returns {{absolutePath: string, manifestPath: string}} Canonical paths.\n390:  */\n391: function canonicalManifestPath({ hubId }) {\n392:   if (!isCanonicalHubId(hubId)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n393:   const currentActivationRoot = activationRoot();\n394:   const directoryPath = path.resolve(currentActivationRoot, hubId);\n395:   const absolutePath = path.join(directoryPath, 'manifest.json');\n396:   if (!isContained(currentActivationRoot, absolutePath)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n397:   return { absolutePath, manifestPath: relativeManifestPath(absolutePath) };\n398: }\n399: \n400: function loadCanonicalRouterInputs({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n401:   if (!isCanonicalHubId(hubId)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n402:   const realRoot = ensureSafeSkillRoot(hubId, skillRoot);\n403:   const sourceBytes = {\n404:     'SKILL.md': readOwnedFile(realRoot, 'SKILL.md'),\n405:     'hub-router.json': readOwnedFile(realRoot, 'hub-router.json'),\n406:     'mode-registry.json': readOwnedFile(realRoot, 'mode-registry.json'),\n407:   };\n408:   let registry;\n409:   let hubRouter;\n410:   try {\n411:     registry = JSON.parse(sourceBytes['mode-registry.json'].toString('utf8'));\n412:     hubRouter = JSON.parse(sourceBytes['hub-router.json'].toString('utf8'));\n413:   } catch {\n414:     throw contractError('invalid-input');\n415:   }\n416:   if (registry.skill !== hubId || hubRouter.skill !== hubId) {\n417:     throw contractError('hub-mismatch');\n418:   }\n419:   return {\n420:     hubRouter,\n421:     registry,\n422:     skillMarkdown: sourceBytes['SKILL.md'].toString('utf8'),\n423:     sourceBytes,\n424:   };\n425: }\n426: \n427: function compileCanonicalParent({ hubId, skillRoot, generation }) {\n428:   const inputs = loadCanonicalRouterInputs({ hubId, skillRoot });\n429:   try {\n430:     return runtimeContext().compiler.compileRegistry({ activationGeneration: generation, ...inputs }).policy;\n431:   } catch (error) {\n432:     if (error && error.causeCode) throw error;\n433:     throw contractError('compile-error');\n434:   }\n435: }\n436: \n437: // Every graduated hub in HUB_CHILD owns a bespoke\n438: // shadow-child registry-compiler.cjs with its own packetKind vocabulary,\n439: // vocabulary-ownership rules, and bundle-rule generation -- structurally\n440: // different from the generic 001-sk-code compiler compileCanonicalParent\n441: // falls back to below. Recompiling a graduated hub's inputs through that\n442: // generic compiler either throws (PACKET_KIND_UNSUPPORTED on packetKinds\n443: // the generic PACKET_AUTHORITY map never learned, e.g. mcp-tooling's/\n444: // cli-external-orchestration's 'transport') or silently yields a different\n445: // basePolicyHash (different vocabulary/composition-rule construction), so\n446: // the freshness check can never agree with compiled-route-status.cjs's\n447: // loadHubEngine-sourced verdict for those hubs. This reuses the identical\n448: // cached snapshot the runtime engine and Lane C parity already compute, so\n449: // the two views read the same policy and cannot diverge.\n450: \n451: /**\n452:  * Prefer a graduated hub's own compiled shadow-child snapshot over the\n453:  * generic canonical compiler for a freshness comparison. Returns undefined\n454:  * (never throws for a routing reason) when hubId has no registered shadow\n455:  * child, or when skillRoot resolves somewhere other than that hub's\n456:  * canonical skill folder, so scaffolding and fixture-driven callers keep\n457:  * today's generic-compiler behavior unchanged.\n458:  *\n459:  * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and authored source root.\n460:  * @param {string} input.hubId - Hyphen-case hub identifier.\n461:  * @param {string} input.skillRoot - Candidate authored source root.\n462:  * @returns {Object|undefined} The shadow-child's compiled policy, or undefined.\n463:  */\n464: function shadowChildPolicyFor({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n465:   const { engine } = runtimeContext();\n466:   if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(engine.HUB_CHILD, hubId)) return undefined;\n467:   let realSkillRoot;\n468:   let realCanonicalRoot;\n469:   try {\n470:     realSkillRoot = fs.realpathSync(path.resolve(skillRoot));\n471:     realCanonicalRoot = fs.realpathSync(path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'skills', hubId));\n472:   } catch {\n473:     return undefined;\n474:   }\n475:   if (realSkillRoot !== realCanonicalRoot) return undefined;\n476:   try {\n477:     return engine.loadHubEngine(hubId).snapshot.policy;\n478:   } catch {\n479:     throw contractError('compile-error');\n480:   }\n481: }\n482: \n483: /**\n484:  * Compare a structurally valid manifest with an already compiled policy.\n485:  *\n486:  * @param {Object} input - Manifest identity and current policy.\n487:  * @param {string} input.hubId - Hub identifier.\n488:  * @param {Object} input.currentPolicy - Current compiled policy snapshot.\n489:  * @returns {Object} Stable manifest validity and freshness record.\n490:  */\n491: function evaluateManifestFreshness({ hubId, currentPolicy, manifestBytes: suppliedBytes }) {\n492:   let paths;\n493:   try {\n494:     paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n495:   } catch (error) {\n496:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'));\n497:   }\n498:   let manifestBytes = suppliedBytes;\n499:   try {\n500:     if (manifestBytes === undefined) manifestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n501:   } catch (error) {\n502:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'));\n503:   }\n504:   if (manifestBytes === null) return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest');\n505:   const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes });\n506:   if (!inspected.manifestValid) {\n507:     return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', inspected);\n508:   }\n509:   const normalizedPolicy = normalizeCurrentPolicy(currentPolicy);\n510:   if (!normalizedPolicy) {\n511:     return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-input', {\n512:       ...inspected,\n513:       manifestValid: true,\n514:       manifest: inspected.manifest,\n515:     });\n516:   }\n517:   const selectedPolicy = inspected.manifest.selectedPolicy;\n518:   const fresh = selectedPolicy.generation === normalizedPolicy.generation\n519:     && selectedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash === normalizedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash;\n520:   return resultRecord({\n521:     hubId,\n522:     manifestPath: paths.manifestPath,\n523:     manifestValid: true,\n524:     fresh,\n525:     causeCode: fresh ? 'fresh' : 'stale-manifest',\n526:     manifest: inspected.manifest,\n527:     currentPolicyHash: normalizedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash,\n528:     manifestFingerprint: inspected.manifestFingerprint,\n529:   });\n530: }\n531: \n532: /**\n533:  * Recompile current hub inputs at the selected generation and check freshness.\n534:  *\n535:  * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and authored source root.\n536:  * @returns {Object} Stable manifest validity and freshness record.\n537:  */\n538: function checkCanonicalManifestFreshness({ hubId, skillRoot, manifestBytes: suppliedBytes }) {\n539:   let paths;\n540:   try {\n541:     paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n542:   } catch (error) {\n543:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'));\n544:   }\n545:   let manifestBytes = suppliedBytes;\n546:   try {\n547:     if (manifestBytes === undefined) manifestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n548:   } catch (error) {\n549:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'));\n550:   }\n551:   if (manifestBytes === null) return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest');\n552:   const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes });\n553:   if (!inspected.manifestValid) {\n554:     return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', inspected);\n555:   }\n556:   let currentPolicy;\n557:   try {\n558:     currentPolicy = shadowChildPolicyFor({ hubId, skillRoot }) ?? compileCanonicalParent({\n559:       hubId,\n560:       skillRoot,\n561:       generation: inspected.manifest.selectedPolicy.generation,\n562:     });\n563:   } catch (error) {\n564:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), {\n565:       ...inspected,\n566:       manifestValid: true,\n567:       manifest: inspected.manifest,\n568:     });\n569:   }\n570:   return evaluateManifestFreshness({ hubId, currentPolicy, manifestBytes });\n571: }\n572: \n573: /**\n574:  * Atomically create an inert generation-one manifest and verify it immediately.\n575:  *\n576:  * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and final authored source root.\n577:  * @returns {Object} Stable mint result with a created flag.\n578:  */\n579: function mintCanonicalManifestUnlocked({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n580:   let paths;\n581:   try {\n582:     paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n583:   } catch (error) {\n584:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'), { created: false });\n585:   }\n586:   if (fs.existsSync(paths.absolutePath)) {\n587:     try {\n588:       const manifestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n589:       const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes });\n590:       return failureRecord(hubId, 'already-exists', {\n591:         ...inspected,\n592:         manifestValid: inspected.manifestValid,\n593:         manifest: inspected.manifest,\n594:         created: false,\n595:       });\n596:     } catch (error) {\n597:       return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { created: false });\n598:     }\n599:   }\n600:   let currentPolicy;\n601:   try {\n602:     currentPolicy = compileCanonicalParent({ hubId, skillRoot, generation: 1 });\n603:   } catch (error) {\n604:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { created: false });\n605:   }\n606:   const manifest = {\n607:     schemaVersion: 'V1',\n608:     selectedPolicy: {\n609:       effectivePolicyHash: currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash,\n610:       generation: 1,\n611:     },\n612:     servingAuthority: 'legacy',\n613:     shadowOnly: true,\n614:   };\n615:   const manifestBytes = artifactBytes(manifest);\n616:   let created = false;\n617:   try {\n618:     ensureActivationDirectory(path.dirname(paths.absolutePath));\n619:     fs.writeFileSync(paths.absolutePath, manifestBytes, { flag: 'wx', mode: 0o600 });\n620:     created = true;\n621:   } catch (error) {\n622:     if (error && error.code === 'EEXIST') {\n623:       const existingBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n624:       const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes: existingBytes });\n625:       return failureRecord(hubId, 'already-exists', {\n626:         ...inspected,\n627:         manifestValid: inspected.manifestValid,\n628:         manifest: inspected.manifest,\n629:         created: false,\n630:       });\n631:     }\n632:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { created });\n633:   }\n634:   return {\n635:     ...checkCanonicalManifestFreshness({ hubId, skillRoot }),\n636:     created: true,\n637:   };\n638: }\n639: \n640: function mintCanonicalManifest(input) {\n641:   const lease = acquireManifestWriterLease('mint');\n642:   if (!lease) return failureRecord(input && input.hubId, 'publication-locked', { created: false });\n643:   try {\n644:     return mintCanonicalManifestUnlocked(input);\n645:   } finally {\n646:     releaseManifestWriterLease(lease);\n647:   }\n648: }\n649: \n650: /**\n651:  * Recompile current hub inputs one generation ahead and overwrite an existing\n652:  * manifest in place, preserving servingAuthority and shadowOnly untouched.\n653:  * Refuses a missing manifest outright — use mintCanonicalManifest for that.\n654:  *\n655:  * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and current authored source root.\n656:  * @returns {Object} Stable freshness record with a refreshed flag.\n657:  */\n658: function refreshCanonicalManifestUnlocked({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n659:   let paths;\n660:   try {\n661:     paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n662:   } catch (error) {\n663:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'), { refreshed: false });\n664:   }\n665:   let existingBytes;\n666:   try {\n667:     existingBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n668:   } catch (error) {\n669:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'), { refreshed: false });\n670:   }\n671:   if (existingBytes === null) {\n672:     return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest', { refreshed: false });\n673:   }\n674:   const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes: existingBytes });\n675:   if (!inspected.manifestValid) {\n676:     return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', { ...inspected, refreshed: false });\n677:   }\n678:   const existingManifest = inspected.manifest;\n679:   const newGeneration = existingManifest.selectedPolicy.generation + 1;\n680:   let currentPolicy;\n681:   try {\n682:     // Prefer a graduated hub's own shadow-child snapshot, exactly as the freshness\n683:     // check does. The generic canonical compiler throws on those hubs' packet kinds\n684:     // (or yields a different hash), so refreshing through it can never produce a\n685:     // manifest the resolver's serve-time identity binding will accept.\n686:     currentPolicy = shadowChildPolicyFor({ hubId, skillRoot })\n687:       ?? compileCanonicalParent({ hubId, skillRoot, generation: newGeneration });\n688:   } catch (error) {\n689:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), {\n690:       ...inspected,\n691:       manifestValid: true,\n692:       manifest: inspected.manifest,\n693:       refreshed: false,\n694:     });\n695:   }\n696:   // Re-read the manifest's serving state as late as possible. A concurrent flip of\n697:   // servingAuthority/shadowOnly during the (slow) compile above must survive this\n698:   // refresh, so carry forward the CURRENT on-disk values rather than the snapshot\n699:   // taken before the compile. A vanished or corrupt manifest here means another\n700:   // writer is mid-operation — fail closed instead of clobbering it.\n701:   let latest;\n702:   try {\n703:     const latestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n704:     if (latestBytes === null) {\n705:       return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest', { refreshed: false });\n706:     }\n707:     latest = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes: latestBytes });\n708:   } catch (error) {\n709:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'), { refreshed: false });\n710:   }\n711:   if (!latest.manifestValid) {\n712:     return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', { ...latest, refreshed: false });\n713:   }\n714:   const manifest = {\n715:     schemaVersion: 'V1',\n716:     selectedPolicy: {\n717:       effectivePolicyHash: currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash,\n718:       // Select the generation the compiled policy actually carries, normalizing\n719:       // because a snapshot names it `activationGeneration`. Selecting any other\n720:       // value leaves the identity binding mismatched and the hub silently on legacy.\n721:       generation: normalizeCurrentPolicy(currentPolicy)?.generation ?? newGeneration,\n722:     },\n723:     servingAuthority: latest.manifest.servingAuthority,\n724:     shadowOnly: latest.manifest.shadowOnly,\n725:   };\n726:   const manifestBytes = artifactBytes(manifest);\n727:   let tempPath = null;\n728:   try {\n729:     ensureActivationDirectory(path.dirname(paths.absolutePath));\n730:     // Publish atomically: write a unique temp sibling then rename over the target so\n731:     // a concurrent reader never observes a half-written manifest and two publishers\n732:     // cannot interleave a partial file.\n733:     tempPath = `${paths.absolutePath}.tmp-${process.pid}-${newGeneration}`;\n734:     fs.writeFileSync(tempPath, manifestBytes, { flag: 'wx', mode: 0o600 });\n735:     fs.renameSync(tempPath, paths.absolutePath);\n736:   } catch (error) {\n737:     if (tempPath) fs.rmSync(tempPath, { force: true });\n738:     return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { refreshed: false });\n739:   }\n740:   return {\n741:     ...checkCanonicalManifestFreshness({ hubId, skillRoot }),\n742:     refreshed: true,\n743:   };\n744: }\n745: \n746: function refreshCanonicalManifest(input) {\n747:   const lease = acquireManifestWriterLease('refresh');\n748:   if (!lease) return failureRecord(input && input.hubId, 'publication-locked', { refreshed: false });\n749:   try {\n750:     return refreshCanonicalManifestUnlocked(input);\n751:   } finally {\n752:     releaseManifestWriterLease(lease);\n753:   }\n754: }\n755: \n756: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n757: // 5. EXPORTS\n758: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n759: \n760: module.exports = {\n761:   get ACTIVATION_ROOT() { return activationRoot(); },\n762:   PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH,\n763:   canonicalManifestPath,\n764:   checkCanonicalManifestFreshness,\n765:   evaluateManifestFreshness,\n766:   isCanonicalHubId,\n767:   mintCanonicalManifest,\n768:   refreshCanonicalManifest,\n769:   validateCanonicalManifestBytes,\n770: };\n\n(End of file - total 770 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ LIBRARY: CANONICAL COMPILED-ROUTE MANIFEST                              ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst fs = require('node:fs');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst crypto = require('node:crypto');\n\nconst layout = require('./compiled-route-layout.cjs');\n\nconst RUNTIME_ROOT = path.join(__dirname, 'compiled-routing');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs","text":"// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n// ║ LIBRARY: CANONICAL COMPILED-ROUTE MANIFEST                              ║\n// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n'use strict';\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst fs = require('node:fs');\nconst path = require('node:path');\nconst crypto = require('node:crypto');\n\nconst layout = require('./compiled-route-layout.cjs');\n\nconst RUNTIME_ROOT = path.join(__dirname, 'compiled-routing');\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..');\nconst PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH = layout.publicationLockPathFor(RUNTIME_ROOT);\nconst HUB_ID_PATTERN = /^[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/;\nconst HASH_PATTERN = /^[a-f0-9]{64}$/;\nconst MANIFEST_KEYS = ['schemaVersion', 'selectedPolicy', 'servingAuthority', 'shadowOnly'];\nconst SELECTED_POLICY_KEYS = ['effectivePolicyHash', 'generation'];\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 3. HELPERS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nfunction contractError(causeCode) {\n  const error = new Error(causeCode);\n  error.causeCode = causeCode;\n  return error;\n}\n\nlet cachedRuntimeContext = null;\n\nfunction clearRuntimeRequireCache() {\n  const root = path.resolve(RUNTIME_ROOT);\n  for (const cachePath of Object.keys(require.cache)) {\n    const relative = path.relative(root, cachePath);\n    if (relative === '' || (relative && !relative.startsWith('..') && !path.isAbsolute(relative))) {\n      delete require.cache[cachePath];\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nfunction runtimePaths({ allowLegacyFallback = false } = {}) {\n  return layout.resolveRuntimePaths(RUNTIME_ROOT, { allowLegacyFallback });\n}\n\nfunction activationRoot() {\n  return runtimePaths({ allowLegacyFallback: true }).activationRoot;\n}\n\nfunction runtimeContext() {\n  const binding = runtimePaths();\n  if (!binding) throw contractError('compile-error');\n  if (!cachedRuntimeContext || cachedRuntimeContext.rootIdentity !== binding.rootIdentity) {\n    clearRuntimeRequireCache();\n    cachedRuntimeContext = {\n      ...binding,\n      compiler: require(binding.compilerPath),\n      engine: require(binding.enginePath),\n    };\n  }\n  return cachedRuntimeContext;\n}\n\nfunction sha256(bytes) {\n  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(bytes).digest('hex');\n}\n\nfunction artifactBytes(value) {\n  return runtimeContext().compiler.artifactBytes(value);\n}\n\n// A writer lease whose holder died would otherwise block every future mint and\n// refresh forever, with no escape but deleting the file by hand. Reclaim only an\n// abandoned WRITER lease: an abandoned publication lease may sit over a runtime\n// that is still mid-swap, so that one stays for an operator to clear explicitly.\nfunction abandonedWriterLease() {\n  let lock;\n  try {\n    lock = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH, 'utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    return false;\n  }\n  if (!lock || lock.kind !== 'manifest-writer') return false;\n  if (!Number.isInteger(lock.pid) || lock.pid === process.pid) return false;\n  try {\n    process.kill(lock.pid, 0);\n    return false;\n  } catch (error) {\n    return Boolean(error) && error.code === 'ESRCH';\n  }\n}\n\nfunction acquireManifestWriterLease(operation) {\n  const token = `writer-${process.pid}-${Date.now()}-${crypto.randomBytes(8).toString('hex')}`;\n  const payload = {\n    schemaVersion: 'V1',\n    kind: 'manifest-writer',\n    token,\n    operation,\n    pid: process.pid,\n    createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n  };\n  const write = () => fs.writeFileSync(\n    PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH,\n    `${JSON.stringify(payload, null, 2)}\\n`,\n    { flag: 'wx', mode: 0o600 },\n  );\n  try {\n    write();\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (!error || error.code !== 'EEXIST') throw error;\n    if (!abandonedWriterLease()) return null;\n    try {\n      fs.rmSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH);\n      write();\n    } catch (retryError) {\n      if (retryError && retryError.code === 'EEXIST') return null;\n      throw retryError;\n    }\n  }\n  return token;\n}\n\nfunction releaseManifestWriterLease(token) {\n  const stats = fs.lstatSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH);\n  if (stats.isSymbolicLink() || !stats.isFile()) {\n    throw new Error('manifest writer lock is not a real file');\n  }\n  let lock;\n  try {\n    lock = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH, 'utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    throw new Error('manifest writer lock is invalid');\n  }\n  if (lock.kind !== 'manifest-writer' || lock.token !== token) {\n    throw new Error('manifest writer lock ownership changed');\n  }\n  fs.rmSync(PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH);\n}\n\nfunction isPlainObject(value) {\n  return Boolean(value) && typeof value === 'object' && !Array.isArray(value);\n}\n\nfunction hasExactKeys(value, expected) {\n  if (!isPlainObject(value)) return false;\n  const actual = Object.keys(value).sort();\n  return actual.length === expected.length\n    && actual.every((key, index) => key === expected[index]);\n}\n\n/**\n * Check whether a hub identifier is safe for canonical activation storage.\n *\n * @param {unknown} hubId - Candidate hub identifier.\n * @returns {boolean} Whether the identifier is canonical hyphen-case.\n */\nfunction isCanonicalHubId(hubId) {\n  return typeof hubId === 'string' && HUB_ID_PATTERN.test(hubId);\n}\n\nfunction isContained(root, candidate) {\n  const relative = path.relative(root, candidate);\n  return relative === '' || (!relative.startsWith('..') && !path.isAbsolute(relative));\n}\n\nfunction relativeManifestPath(absolutePath) {\n  return path.relative(REPO_ROOT, absolutePath).split(path.sep).join('/');\n}\n\nfunction selectedPolicyFrom(manifest) {\n  if (!manifest || !isPlainObject(manifest.selectedPolicy)) {\n    return { effectivePolicyHash: null, generation: null };\n  }\n  return {\n    effectivePolicyHash: manifest.selectedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash ?? null,\n    generation: manifest.selectedPolicy.generation ?? null,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction resultRecord({\n  hubId,\n  causeCode,\n  manifestValid = false,\n  fresh = false,\n  manifest = null,\n  manifestFingerprint = null,\n  currentPolicyHash = null,\n  manifestPath = null,\n  created,\n  refreshed,\n}) {\n  const result = {\n    hubId: typeof hubId === 'string' ? hubId : null,\n    manifestPath,\n    manifestValid,\n    fresh,\n    causeCode,\n    selectedPolicy: selectedPolicyFrom(manifest),\n    currentPolicyHash,\n    manifestFingerprint,\n  };\n  if (typeof created === 'boolean') result.created = created;\n  if (typeof refreshed === 'boolean') result.refreshed = refreshed;\n  return result;\n}\n\nfunction failureRecord(hubId, causeCode, options = {}) {\n  let manifestPath = null;\n  try {\n    manifestPath = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId }).manifestPath;\n  } catch {\n    // Unsafe identities do not receive a synthesized path.\n  }\n  return resultRecord({ hubId, causeCode, manifestPath, ...options });\n}\n\nfunction normalizeCurrentPolicy(currentPolicy) {\n  if (!isPlainObject(currentPolicy)) return null;\n  const generation = currentPolicy.activationGeneration ?? currentPolicy.generation;\n  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(generation) || generation < 1) return null;\n  if (!HASH_PATTERN.test(currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash || '')) return null;\n  return { effectivePolicyHash: currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash, generation };\n}\n\nfunction safeManifestLocationExists(absolutePath) {\n  const currentActivationRoot = activationRoot();\n  let activationStats;\n  try {\n    activationStats = fs.lstatSync(currentActivationRoot);\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;\n    throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n  }\n  if (activationStats.isSymbolicLink() || !activationStats.isDirectory()) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  const realActivationRoot = fs.realpathSync(currentActivationRoot);\n  const directoryPath = path.dirname(absolutePath);\n  let directoryStats;\n  try {\n    directoryStats = fs.lstatSync(directoryPath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;\n    throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n  }\n  if (directoryStats.isSymbolicLink() || !directoryStats.isDirectory()) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  if (!isContained(realActivationRoot, fs.realpathSync(directoryPath))) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  let manifestStats;\n  try {\n    manifestStats = fs.lstatSync(absolutePath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return false;\n    throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n  }\n  if (manifestStats.isSymbolicLink() || !manifestStats.isFile()) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  if (!isContained(realActivationRoot, fs.realpathSync(absolutePath))) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  return true;\n}\n\nfunction readManifestBytes(absolutePath) {\n  try {\n    if (!safeManifestLocationExists(absolutePath)) return null;\n    return fs.readFileSync(absolutePath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error && error.causeCode) throw error;\n    if (error && error.code === 'ENOENT') return null;\n    throw contractError('invalid-manifest');\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Validate canonical manifest structure without evaluating policy freshness.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and candidate bytes.\n * @returns {Object} Structural validity, parsed manifest, and fingerprint.\n */\nfunction validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes }) {\n  if (!isCanonicalHubId(hubId) || !Buffer.isBuffer(manifestBytes)) {\n    return { manifestValid: false, manifest: null, manifestFingerprint: null };\n  }\n  const manifestFingerprint = sha256(manifestBytes);\n  let manifest;\n  try {\n    manifest = JSON.parse(manifestBytes.toString('utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    return { manifestValid: false, manifest: null, manifestFingerprint };\n  }\n  const selectedPolicy = manifest && manifest.selectedPolicy;\n  const manifestValid = hasExactKeys(manifest, MANIFEST_KEYS)\n    && manifest.schemaVersion === 'V1'\n    && (manifest.servingAuthority === 'legacy' || manifest.servingAuthority === 'compiled')\n    && typeof manifest.shadowOnly === 'boolean'\n    && hasExactKeys(selectedPolicy, SELECTED_POLICY_KEYS)\n    && Number.isSafeInteger(selectedPolicy.generation)\n    && selectedPolicy.generation >= 1\n    && HASH_PATTERN.test(selectedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash || '');\n  return { manifestValid, manifest: manifestValid ? manifest : null, manifestFingerprint };\n}\n\nfunction ensureSafeSkillRoot(hubId, skillRoot) {\n  if (typeof skillRoot !== 'string' || !skillRoot.trim()) {\n    throw contractError('invalid-input');\n  }\n  if (skillRoot.includes('\\0') || skillRoot.split(/[\\\\/]+/).includes('..')) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  const resolvedRoot = path.resolve(skillRoot);\n  let realRoot;\n  let rootStats;\n  try {\n    rootStats = fs.lstatSync(resolvedRoot);\n    realRoot = fs.realpathSync(resolvedRoot);\n  } catch {\n    throw contractError('invalid-input');\n  }\n  if (rootStats.isSymbolicLink()) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  if (!rootStats.isDirectory()) throw contractError('invalid-input');\n  if (path.basename(resolvedRoot) !== hubId || path.basename(realRoot) !== hubId) {\n    throw contractError('hub-mismatch');\n  }\n  return realRoot;\n}\n\nfunction readOwnedFile(realRoot, fileName) {\n  const candidate = path.join(realRoot, fileName);\n  if (!isContained(realRoot, candidate)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  let stats;\n  try {\n    stats = fs.lstatSync(candidate);\n  } catch {\n    throw contractError('invalid-input');\n  }\n  if (stats.isSymbolicLink() || !stats.isFile()) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  const realFile = fs.realpathSync(candidate);\n  if (!isContained(realRoot, realFile)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  return fs.readFileSync(realFile);\n}\n\nfunction ensureActivationDirectory(directoryPath) {\n  const currentActivationRoot = activationRoot();\n  fs.mkdirSync(currentActivationRoot, { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });\n  const activationStats = fs.lstatSync(currentActivationRoot);\n  if (activationStats.isSymbolicLink() || !activationStats.isDirectory()) {\n    throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  }\n  const realActivationRoot = fs.realpathSync(currentActivationRoot);\n  if (fs.existsSync(directoryPath)) {\n    const directoryStats = fs.lstatSync(directoryPath);\n    if (directoryStats.isSymbolicLink() || !directoryStats.isDirectory()) {\n      throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n    }\n  }\n  fs.mkdirSync(directoryPath, { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });\n  const realDirectory = fs.realpathSync(directoryPath);\n  if (!isContained(realActivationRoot, realDirectory)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n}\n\nfunction causeFrom(error, fallback = 'invalid-input') {\n  return error && typeof error.causeCode === 'string' ? error.causeCode : fallback;\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 4. CORE LOGIC\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n/**\n * Resolve the only writable activation-manifest path for a hub.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Hub identity.\n * @param {string} input.hubId - Hyphen-case hub identifier.\n * @returns {{absolutePath: string, manifestPath: string}} Canonical paths.\n */\nfunction canonicalManifestPath({ hubId }) {\n  if (!isCanonicalHubId(hubId)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  const currentActivationRoot = activationRoot();\n  const directoryPath = path.resolve(currentActivationRoot, hubId);\n  const absolutePath = path.join(directoryPath, 'manifest.json');\n  if (!isContained(currentActivationRoot, absolutePath)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  return { absolutePath, manifestPath: relativeManifestPath(absolutePath) };\n}\n\nfunction loadCanonicalRouterInputs({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n  if (!isCanonicalHubId(hubId)) throw contractError('unsafe-path');\n  const realRoot = ensureSafeSkillRoot(hubId, skillRoot);\n  const sourceBytes = {\n    'SKILL.md': readOwnedFile(realRoot, 'SKILL.md'),\n    'hub-router.json': readOwnedFile(realRoot, 'hub-router.json'),\n    'mode-registry.json': readOwnedFile(realRoot, 'mode-registry.json'),\n  };\n  let registry;\n  let hubRouter;\n  try {\n    registry = JSON.parse(sourceBytes['mode-registry.json'].toString('utf8'));\n    hubRouter = JSON.parse(sourceBytes['hub-router.json'].toString('utf8'));\n  } catch {\n    throw contractError('invalid-input');\n  }\n  if (registry.skill !== hubId || hubRouter.skill !== hubId) {\n    throw contractError('hub-mismatch');\n  }\n  return {\n    hubRouter,\n    registry,\n    skillMarkdown: sourceBytes['SKILL.md'].toString('utf8'),\n    sourceBytes,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction compileCanonicalParent({ hubId, skillRoot, generation }) {\n  const inputs = loadCanonicalRouterInputs({ hubId, skillRoot });\n  try {\n    return runtimeContext().compiler.compileRegistry({ activationGeneration: generation, ...inputs }).policy;\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error && error.causeCode) throw error;\n    throw contractError('compile-error');\n  }\n}\n\n// Every graduated hub in HUB_CHILD owns a bespoke\n// shadow-child registry-compiler.cjs with its own packetKind vocabulary,\n// vocabulary-ownership rules, and bundle-rule generation -- structurally\n// different from the generic 001-sk-code compiler compileCanonicalParent\n// falls back to below. Recompiling a graduated hub's inputs through that\n// generic compiler either throws (PACKET_KIND_UNSUPPORTED on packetKinds\n// the generic PACKET_AUTHORITY map never learned, e.g. mcp-tooling's/\n// cli-external-orchestration's 'transport') or silently yields a different\n// basePolicyHash (different vocabulary/composition-rule construction), so\n// the freshness check can never agree with compiled-route-status.cjs's\n// loadHubEngine-sourced verdict for those hubs. This reuses the identical\n// cached snapshot the runtime engine and Lane C parity already compute, so\n// the two views read the same policy and cannot diverge.\n\n/**\n * Prefer a graduated hub's own compiled shadow-child snapshot over the\n * generic canonical compiler for a freshness comparison. Returns undefined\n * (never throws for a routing reason) when hubId has no registered shadow\n * child, or when skillRoot resolves somewhere other than that hub's\n * canonical skill folder, so scaffolding and fixture-driven callers keep\n * today's generic-compiler behavior unchanged.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and authored source root.\n * @param {string} input.hubId - Hyphen-case hub identifier.\n * @param {string} input.skillRoot - Candidate authored source root.\n * @returns {Object|undefined} The shadow-child's compiled policy, or undefined.\n */\nfunction shadowChildPolicyFor({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n  const { engine } = runtimeContext();\n  if (!Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(engine.HUB_CHILD, hubId)) return undefined;\n  let realSkillRoot;\n  let realCanonicalRoot;\n  try {\n    realSkillRoot = fs.realpathSync(path.resolve(skillRoot));\n    realCanonicalRoot = fs.realpathSync(path.join(REPO_ROOT, '.opencode', 'skills', hubId));\n  } catch {\n    return undefined;\n  }\n  if (realSkillRoot !== realCanonicalRoot) return undefined;\n  try {\n    return engine.loadHubEngine(hubId).snapshot.policy;\n  } catch {\n    throw contractError('compile-error');\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Compare a structurally valid manifest with an already compiled policy.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Manifest identity and current policy.\n * @param {string} input.hubId - Hub identifier.\n * @param {Object} input.currentPolicy - Current compiled policy snapshot.\n * @returns {Object} Stable manifest validity and freshness record.\n */\nfunction evaluateManifestFreshness({ hubId, currentPolicy, manifestBytes: suppliedBytes }) {\n  let paths;\n  try {\n    paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'));\n  }\n  let manifestBytes = suppliedBytes;\n  try {\n    if (manifestBytes === undefined) manifestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'));\n  }\n  if (manifestBytes === null) return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest');\n  const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes });\n  if (!inspected.manifestValid) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', inspected);\n  }\n  const normalizedPolicy = normalizeCurrentPolicy(currentPolicy);\n  if (!normalizedPolicy) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-input', {\n      ...inspected,\n      manifestValid: true,\n      manifest: inspected.manifest,\n    });\n  }\n  const selectedPolicy = inspected.manifest.selectedPolicy;\n  const fresh = selectedPolicy.generation === normalizedPolicy.generation\n    && selectedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash === normalizedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash;\n  return resultRecord({\n    hubId,\n    manifestPath: paths.manifestPath,\n    manifestValid: true,\n    fresh,\n    causeCode: fresh ? 'fresh' : 'stale-manifest',\n    manifest: inspected.manifest,\n    currentPolicyHash: normalizedPolicy.effectivePolicyHash,\n    manifestFingerprint: inspected.manifestFingerprint,\n  });\n}\n\n/**\n * Recompile current hub inputs at the selected generation and check freshness.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and authored source root.\n * @returns {Object} Stable manifest validity and freshness record.\n */\nfunction checkCanonicalManifestFreshness({ hubId, skillRoot, manifestBytes: suppliedBytes }) {\n  let paths;\n  try {\n    paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'));\n  }\n  let manifestBytes = suppliedBytes;\n  try {\n    if (manifestBytes === undefined) manifestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'));\n  }\n  if (manifestBytes === null) return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest');\n  const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes });\n  if (!inspected.manifestValid) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', inspected);\n  }\n  let currentPolicy;\n  try {\n    currentPolicy = shadowChildPolicyFor({ hubId, skillRoot }) ?? compileCanonicalParent({\n      hubId,\n      skillRoot,\n      generation: inspected.manifest.selectedPolicy.generation,\n    });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), {\n      ...inspected,\n      manifestValid: true,\n      manifest: inspected.manifest,\n    });\n  }\n  return evaluateManifestFreshness({ hubId, currentPolicy, manifestBytes });\n}\n\n/**\n * Atomically create an inert generation-one manifest and verify it immediately.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and final authored source root.\n * @returns {Object} Stable mint result with a created flag.\n */\nfunction mintCanonicalManifestUnlocked({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n  let paths;\n  try {\n    paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'), { created: false });\n  }\n  if (fs.existsSync(paths.absolutePath)) {\n    try {\n      const manifestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n      const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes });\n      return failureRecord(hubId, 'already-exists', {\n        ...inspected,\n        manifestValid: inspected.manifestValid,\n        manifest: inspected.manifest,\n        created: false,\n      });\n    } catch (error) {\n      return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { created: false });\n    }\n  }\n  let currentPolicy;\n  try {\n    currentPolicy = compileCanonicalParent({ hubId, skillRoot, generation: 1 });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { created: false });\n  }\n  const manifest = {\n    schemaVersion: 'V1',\n    selectedPolicy: {\n      effectivePolicyHash: currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash,\n      generation: 1,\n    },\n    servingAuthority: 'legacy',\n    shadowOnly: true,\n  };\n  const manifestBytes = artifactBytes(manifest);\n  let created = false;\n  try {\n    ensureActivationDirectory(path.dirname(paths.absolutePath));\n    fs.writeFileSync(paths.absolutePath, manifestBytes, { flag: 'wx', mode: 0o600 });\n    created = true;\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (error && error.code === 'EEXIST') {\n      const existingBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n      const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes: existingBytes });\n      return failureRecord(hubId, 'already-exists', {\n        ...inspected,\n        manifestValid: inspected.manifestValid,\n        manifest: inspected.manifest,\n        created: false,\n      });\n    }\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { created });\n  }\n  return {\n    ...checkCanonicalManifestFreshness({ hubId, skillRoot }),\n    created: true,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction mintCanonicalManifest(input) {\n  const lease = acquireManifestWriterLease('mint');\n  if (!lease) return failureRecord(input && input.hubId, 'publication-locked', { created: false });\n  try {\n    return mintCanonicalManifestUnlocked(input);\n  } finally {\n    releaseManifestWriterLease(lease);\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Recompile current hub inputs one generation ahead and overwrite an existing\n * manifest in place, preserving servingAuthority and shadowOnly untouched.\n * Refuses a missing manifest outright — use mintCanonicalManifest for that.\n *\n * @param {Object} input - Hub identity and current authored source root.\n * @returns {Object} Stable freshness record with a refreshed flag.\n */\nfunction refreshCanonicalManifestUnlocked({ hubId, skillRoot }) {\n  let paths;\n  try {\n    paths = canonicalManifestPath({ hubId });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'unsafe-path'), { refreshed: false });\n  }\n  let existingBytes;\n  try {\n    existingBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'), { refreshed: false });\n  }\n  if (existingBytes === null) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest', { refreshed: false });\n  }\n  const inspected = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes: existingBytes });\n  if (!inspected.manifestValid) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', { ...inspected, refreshed: false });\n  }\n  const existingManifest = inspected.manifest;\n  const newGeneration = existingManifest.selectedPolicy.generation + 1;\n  let currentPolicy;\n  try {\n    // Prefer a graduated hub's own shadow-child snapshot, exactly as the freshness\n    // check does. The generic canonical compiler throws on those hubs' packet kinds\n    // (or yields a different hash), so refreshing through it can never produce a\n    // manifest the resolver's serve-time identity binding will accept.\n    currentPolicy = shadowChildPolicyFor({ hubId, skillRoot })\n      ?? compileCanonicalParent({ hubId, skillRoot, generation: newGeneration });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), {\n      ...inspected,\n      manifestValid: true,\n      manifest: inspected.manifest,\n      refreshed: false,\n    });\n  }\n  // Re-read the manifest's serving state as late as possible. A concurrent flip of\n  // servingAuthority/shadowOnly during the (slow) compile above must survive this\n  // refresh, so carry forward the CURRENT on-disk values rather than the snapshot\n  // taken before the compile. A vanished or corrupt manifest here means another\n  // writer is mid-operation — fail closed instead of clobbering it.\n  let latest;\n  try {\n    const latestBytes = readManifestBytes(paths.absolutePath);\n    if (latestBytes === null) {\n      return failureRecord(hubId, 'missing-manifest', { refreshed: false });\n    }\n    latest = validateCanonicalManifestBytes({ hubId, manifestBytes: latestBytes });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error, 'invalid-manifest'), { refreshed: false });\n  }\n  if (!latest.manifestValid) {\n    return failureRecord(hubId, 'invalid-manifest', { ...latest, refreshed: false });\n  }\n  const manifest = {\n    schemaVersion: 'V1',\n    selectedPolicy: {\n      effectivePolicyHash: currentPolicy.effectivePolicyHash,\n      // Select the generation the compiled policy actually carries, normalizing\n      // because a snapshot names it `activationGeneration`. Selecting any other\n      // value leaves the identity binding mismatched and the hub silently on legacy.\n      generation: normalizeCurrentPolicy(currentPolicy)?.generation ?? newGeneration,\n    },\n    servingAuthority: latest.manifest.servingAuthority,\n    shadowOnly: latest.manifest.shadowOnly,\n  };\n  const manifestBytes = artifactBytes(manifest);\n  let tempPath = null;\n  try {\n    ensureActivationDirectory(path.dirname(paths.absolutePath));\n    // Publish atomically: write a unique temp sibling then rename over the target so\n    // a concurrent reader never observes a half-written manifest and two publishers\n    // cannot interleave a partial file.\n    tempPath = `${paths.absolutePath}.tmp-${process.pid}-${newGeneration}`;\n    fs.writeFileSync(tempPath, manifestBytes, { flag: 'wx', mode: 0o600 });\n    fs.renameSync(tempPath, paths.absolutePath);\n  } catch (error) {\n    if (tempPath) fs.rmSync(tempPath, { force: true });\n    return failureRecord(hubId, causeFrom(error), { refreshed: false });\n  }\n  return {\n    ...checkCanonicalManifestFreshness({ hubId, skillRoot }),\n    refreshed: true,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction refreshCanonicalManifest(input) {\n  const lease = acquireManifestWriterLease('refresh');\n  if (!lease) return failureRecord(input && input.hubId, 'publication-locked', { refreshed: false });\n  try {\n    return refreshCanonicalManifestUnlocked(input);\n  } finally {\n    releaseManifestWriterLease(lease);\n  }\n}\n\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 5. EXPORTS\n// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nmodule.exports = {\n  get ACTIVATION_ROOT() { return activationRoot(); },\n  PUBLICATION_LOCK_PATH,\n  canonicalManifestPath,\n  checkCanonicalManifestFreshness,\n  evaluateManifestFreshness,\n  isCanonicalHubId,\n  mintCanonicalManifest,\n  refreshCanonicalManifest,\n  validateCanonicalManifestBytes,\n};","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":770,"totalLines":770,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-route-manifest.cjs","time":{"start":1785133889150,"end":1785133889162}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01ecde0a1a76a560016a66fb40f41c8191941308ad25f64e98"}},"id":"prt_fa245767d001CYqAhZTCiRfxB7","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa2451ace001RiLa50jjImprPx"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133889301,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_VJW2vEmJlWrf2nPp4HEgdiN8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"compiled-route-manifest|cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke|git-live-follow|hf-model-server|compiled-route-guard","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public","include":"*.{ts,js,cjs,mjs,md,yaml,yml,json,sh}"},"output":"Found 100 matches (more matches available)\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/sk-git/SKILL.md:\n  Line 328: 16. **Let launch-wrapper sessions autosync; never hand-roll the publish** - Under the continuous-integration model, a launch-wrapper session publishes each commit to the live branch automatically via the `post-commit` hook calling `git-sync.sh` (gated on the wrapper-injected `SPECKIT_AUTOSYNC=1` + `SPECKIT_LIVE_BRANCH`). Do NOT manually `git push origin HEAD:<live>` or manually rebase onto the live branch to \"make work visible\" — `git-sync.sh` already fast-forwards-or-rebases and never force-pushes; a hand-rolled push risks the exact non-force / abort-on-conflict invariants it protects. If autosync is blocked (a printed conflict), resolve per its message; do not force it. The primary checkout follows via `git-live-follow.sh` (fast-forward-only) and is never worked in. Full contract: [continuous-integration.md](references/continuous-integration.md).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.github/workflows/routing-registry-drift.yml:\n  Line 76:           node .opencode/bin/compiled-route-guard.cjs\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/hf-model-server.cjs:\n  Line 91:       `[hf-model-server] Unknown HF_EMBEDDINGS_DTYPE=\"${raw}\"; falling back to ${DEFAULT_DTYPE}. Allowed: ${ALLOWED_HF_LOCAL_DTYPES.join(', ')}`,\n\n  Line 179:     `[hf-model-server] Refusing to bind non-loopback host \"$