ST HARNESS: hf-model-server shutdown-signal subprocess                   ║\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/embedders/__fixtures__/hf-model-server-shutdown-harness.cjs:5:// ║ Spawned as a real child process by hf-model-server-shutdown.vitest.ts so   ║\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/embedders/__fixtures__/hf-model-server-shutdown-harness.cjs:17:const serverModule = require(path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', 'bin', 'hf-model-server.cjs'));\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/embedders/__fixtures__/README.md:18:| `hf-model-server-shutdown-harness.cjs` | Spawned as a real child process by `hf-model-server-shutdown.vitest.ts`. Calls the production `createHfModelServer()` and `installShutdownHandlers()` from `bin/hf-model-server.cjs` with a fake `loadModel` (env-controlled load/embed delay via `TEST_HF_FAKE_LOAD_DELAY_MS` / `TEST_HF_FAKE_EMBED_DELAY_MS`), so the busy-shutdown regression test can send a real OS signal and observe real process exit behavior. |\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/embedders/__fixtures__/README.md:22:- `../hf-model-server-shutdown.vitest.ts`\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/scripts/bench-dtype-q8-fp16.cjs:3:// BENCH: hf-model-server dtype comparison (q8 vs fp16)\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/scripts/bench-dtype-q8-fp16.cjs:5:// Spawns the REAL hf-model-server twice (HF_EMBEDDINGS_DTYPE=q8 then fp16) against a cached\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/scripts/bench-dtype-q8-fp16.cjs:28:const SERVER = join(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', 'bin', 'hf-model-server.cjs');\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/changelog/v3.4.2.0.md:60:Three documentation findings landed first. The 005 file-change matrix was attributing idle-eviction to the wrong file; it lives in `model-server-supervision.cjs`, not `hf-model-server.cjs`. ENV_REFERENCE was missing four embedding knobs (`EMBEDDER_REINDEX_BATCH_SIZE`, `EMBEDDING_DIM`, `HF_EMBEDDINGS_PREFIX_QUERY`/`DOC`). The four daemon-reliability packet ledgers (009/010/012/013) had verification tables left open while their summaries claimed \"implemented\"; all four strict-validate cleanly now, so the open items are marked done with real evidence.\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/model-server-respawn-lock-atomic.vitest.ts:2:// MODULE: hf-model-server Respawn-Lock Atomic Reclaim Tests\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp-server/tests/model-server-respawn-lock-atomic.vitest.ts:47:  return join(dir, 'hf-model-server.respawn.lock');\n./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/feature-catalog/pipeline-architecture/mcp-launcher-front-proxy.md:33:`recycleDaemonInPlace(graceMs)` in `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` is invoked on a sustained RSS ceiling breach (`onRssBreach`). It sends `SIGTERM` to the running `context-server` child (and the `hf-model-server` child first when present), escalates to `SIGKILL` after the grace window, then re-spawns the backend in place. The re-spawned backend runs with `SPECKIT_BACKEND_ONLY: '1'` so it serves the IPC socket without binding its own stdio transport.\n","exit":0,"truncated":true,"outputPath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_fa2457743001VqrhG0nEM2SuVo"},"title":"rg -n --glob '!**/.opencode/specs/**' --glob '*.{ts,js,cjs,mjs,md,yaml,yml,json,sh}' 'compiled-route-manifest|cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke|git-live-follow|hf-model-server|compiled-route-guard' .","time":{"start":1785133889493,"end":1785133889666}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01ecde0a1a76a560016a66fb40f5908191aea0d7524d11b117"}},"id":"prt_fa24576ac001Sv9fBICb4okp07","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa2451ace001RiLa50jjImprPx"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785133890309,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_BnrrOmi4phVefC0NArBdV34c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout|compiled-routing/008-calibration|compiled-routing/005-decision-evaluator","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public","include":"*.{ts,js,cjs,mjs,md,yaml,yml,json,sh}"},"output":"Found 17 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/handover.md:\n  Line 29: The compiled **shadow-child** router (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/00N-<hub>/lib/{router,canary-router}.cjs` + `registry-compiler.cjs`) must score/select like the frozen legacy replay `router-replay.cjs`: weighted keyword match over the hub's own `hub-router.json` vocabulary, ambiguity-delta near-tie retention, **always route** near-tied sets, correct bundle rules. sk-code was under-routing because its pipeline used a generic OR-set evaluator + a selective controller that force-`defer`ed bare-surface routes and abstained on ties (neither legacy nor sk-design does this). **Reference impls:** `006-sk-design/lib/router.cjs` (production, 37 match) and `001-sk-code/lib/*` (committed).\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/spec.md:\n  Line 21:       - \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/006-sk-design/lib/registry-compiler.cjs\"\n\n  Line 110: | `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/00N-<hub>/lib/registry-compiler.cjs` | Modify | Grow detectors per hub so compiled routes reach legacy parity |\n\n  Line 111: | `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/00N-<hub>/lib/router.cjs` or `canary-router.cjs` | Modify | Route the newly compiled destinations |\n\n  Line 112: | `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/00N-<hub>/fixtures/canary-cases.v1.json` | Modify | Extend canary coverage to the hub's full scenario set |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/plan.md:\n  Line 21:       - \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/006-sk-design/lib/registry-compiler.cjs\"\n\n  Line 131: - Same-class producers: `rg -n 'registry-compiler|canary-router' .opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout` - every hub's compiler/router pair, so the same over-detection class can be checked in each, not just the 2 known bugs.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/tasks.md:\n  Line 20:       - \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/006-sk-design/lib/registry-compiler.cjs\"\n\n  Line 54: - [ ] T001 Read sk-design's reference compiler (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/006-sk-design/lib/registry-compiler.cjs`)\n\n  Line 64: - [ ] T003 Grow sk-code's detectors to legacy parity (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/00N-sk-code/lib/registry-compiler.cjs`) {deps: T001}\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/013-compiled-coverage-buildout/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 91: Applying `refresh` to the two real stale hubs (`sk-doc` generation 5, `system-deep-loop` generation 3) at first surfaced a genuine defect outside this mechanism: `compileRegistry()` (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/001-sk-code/lib/registry-compiler.cjs`, `extractFallbackChecklist`) requires a literal `UNKNOWN_FALLBACK_CHECKLIST = [...]` array (>=3 items) in the hub's `SKILL.md`, matched by regex. Neither `sk-doc/SKILL.md` nor `system-deep-loop/SKILL.md` contained that literal array at the time — both only had prose mentioning \"UNKNOWN_FALLBACK\" — so `compileRegistry` threw `FALLBACK_CHECKLIST_MISSING`. Both refresh attempts correctly returned `causeCode: 'compile-error'`, `refreshed: false`, and left both manifests byte-identical to their pre-attempt state — fail-closed, exactly as designed.\n\n  Line 107: The compiled shadow-child router (`.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/00N-<hub>/lib/{router,canary-router}.cjs` + `registry-compiler.cjs`) had to be brought up to the same scoring/selection behavior as the frozen legacy replay (`router-replay.cjs`): weighted keyword match over the hub's own `hub-router.json` vocabulary, ambiguity-delta near-tie retention, always-route on near-tied sets, correct bundle rules. `sk-design` (`006-sk-design/lib/router.cjs`) was the reference implementation this was patterned on. `sk-design`, `system-deep-loop`, and `mcp-tooling` were brought to `compiled-serving` in `f9f639674b`; `sk-doc` moved from 27/5 to 31/1 in `b03b1dd882`. A fourth harness refinement (SD-015, `6ba5f2957f`) — exempting matched non-route decisions from the gold requirement — closed the remaining drift fleet-wide.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/012-p3-canonical-minter-foundation/spec.md:\n  Line 99: | The registry compiler accepts authored registry, router, skill Markdown, source bytes, and generation without hardcoding a hub ID. | `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/001-sk-code/lib/registry-compiler.cjs:230` | Its `compileRegistry()` function can compile a newly generated registry-driven parent hub. |\n\n  Line 100: | The current build harness hardcodes the `sk-code` skill root and rollout child. | `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/001-sk-code/harness/build-artifacts.cjs:31` | The harness itself is not a canonical new-hub minter. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/016-review-remediation/spec.md:\n  Line 23:       - \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/015-router-unification-program/019-routing-coverage-activation-verification/016-review-remediation/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 20:       - \".opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/router.cjs\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/composer/iterations/iteration-001.md:\n  Line 28: - **Path:** `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/005-decision-evaluator/`, `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/008-calibration/`, `.opencode/bin/lib/compiled-routing/serving-closure.manifest.json`\n","metadata":{"matches":17,"truncated":false},"title":"compiled-routing/009-parent-hub-rollout|compiled-routing/008-calibration|compiled-routing/005-decision-evaluator","time":{"start":1785133889194,"end":1785133890307}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_01ecde0a1a76a560016a66fb40f5848191afd9dbe5b7c95cb2"}},"id":"prt_fa24576a4001NFHJMAC7cIH8fC","sessionID":"ses_05