{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134046805,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_yzC3VlwWdiEuAsr86nqY5Tbx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/README.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Legacy Deep Command Bodies\"\n3: description: \"Developer reference for fallback deep-command bodies used by command injection and render tooling.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"legacy deep command bodies\"\n6:   - \"deep command fallback\"\n7:   - \"deep router bodies\"\n8: importance_tier: \"important\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Legacy Deep Command Bodies\n12: \n13: > Fallback router bodies retained for deep-command injection modes that do not use a compiled contract.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/` stores fallback command bodies for four deep-loop commands.\n20: \n21: Each body acts as a thin router. It resolves command setup and selects workflow YAML while leaving iteration dispatch, artifact writes and convergence handling to the selected workflow.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n26: \n27: ```text\n28: legacy/\n29: +-- deep-ai-council.body.md\n30: +-- deep-alignment.body.md\n31: +-- deep-research.body.md\n32: +-- deep-review.body.md\n33: `-- README.md\n34: ```\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. KEY FILES\n39: \n40: | File | Responsibility |\n41: |---|---|\n42: | `deep-research.body.md` | Fallback router for the deep-research loop. |\n43: | `deep-review.body.md` | Fallback router for the deep-review loop. |\n44: | `deep-ai-council.body.md` | Fallback router for bounded AI Council sessions. |\n45: | `deep-alignment.body.md` | Fallback router for structured alignment audits. |\n46: \n47: ---\n48: \n49: ## 4. ROUTER RESPONSIBILITIES\n50: \n51: The legacy bodies own:\n52: \n53: - Dispatch-context checks\n54: - Setup input resolution\n55: - Execution-mode selection\n56: - Workflow YAML selection\n57: - Presentation boundary references where applicable\n58: \n59: The workflow YAML assets own:\n60: \n61: - Iteration or round dispatch\n62: - Artifact writes\n63: - State reduction\n64: - Convergence checks\n65: - Final synthesis\n66: - Continuity updates\n67: \n68: Do not move workflow execution into these router bodies.\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 5. MODE ROUTING\n73: \n74: Each body recognizes attached command modes:\n75: \n76: | Suffix | Behavior |\n77: |---|---|\n78: | `:auto` | Resolve supported inputs non-interactively and load the auto workflow. |\n79: | `:confirm` | Ask the consolidated setup question and load the confirm workflow. |\n80: | No suffix | Ask for execution mode through the command's setup flow. |\n81: \n82: Inputs such as target paths, iteration limits, convergence settings and executor choices remain workflow inputs rather than execution modes.\n83: \n84: ---\n85: \n86: ## 6. INJECTION BOUNDARY\n87: \n88: Render tooling can return a legacy body directly when a command uses fallback injection.\n89: \n90: Compiled contracts live in the sibling `compiled/` folder. Their maintained sources remain authoritative, and generated contract files must not replace the workflow YAML as the owner of runtime execution.\n91: \n92: `deep-alignment.body.md` remains especially important because alignment has no generated compiler contract.\n93: \n94: ---\n95: \n96: ## 7. VALIDATION\n97: \n98: Confirm the expected files exist from the repository root:\n99: \n100: ```bash\n101: test -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-ai-council.body.md\n102: test -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-alignment.body.md\n103: test -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-research.body.md\n104: test -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-review.body.md\n105: ```\n106: \n107: Expected result: every command exits with status `0`.\n108: \n109: Validate command references with the shared checker:\n110: \n111: ```bash\n112: node .opencode/commands/scripts/validate-command-references.cjs\n113: ```\n114: \n115: Expected result: the checker reports that command references resolve cleanly.\n116: \n117: ---\n118: \n119: ## 8. RELATED\n120: \n121: - [Compiled deep command contracts](../compiled/)\n122: - [Deep command assets](../)\n123: - [Deep command router files](../../)\n124: - [Deep-loop skill](../../../../skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md)\n\n(End of file - total 124 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Legacy Deep Command Bodies\"\ndescription: \"Developer reference for fallback deep-command bodies used by command injection and render tooling.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"legacy deep command bodies\"\n  - \"deep command fallback\"\n  - \"deep router bodies\"\nimportance_tier: \"important\"\n---\n\n# Legacy Deep Command Bodies\n\n> Fallback router bodies retained for deep-command injection modes that do not use a compiled contract.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/` stores fallback command bodies for four deep-loop commands.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Legacy Deep Command Bodies\"\ndescription: \"Developer reference for fallback deep-command bodies used by command injection and render tooling.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"legacy deep command bodies\"\n  - \"deep command fallback\"\n  - \"deep router bodies\"\nimportance_tier: \"important\"\n---\n\n# Legacy Deep Command Bodies\n\n> Fallback router bodies retained for deep-command injection modes that do not use a compiled contract.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/` stores fallback command bodies for four deep-loop commands.\n\nEach body acts as a thin router. It resolves command setup and selects workflow YAML while leaving iteration dispatch, artifact writes and convergence handling to the selected workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\nlegacy/\n+-- deep-ai-council.body.md\n+-- deep-alignment.body.md\n+-- deep-research.body.md\n+-- deep-review.body.md\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `deep-research.body.md` | Fallback router for the deep-research loop. |\n| `deep-review.body.md` | Fallback router for the deep-review loop. |\n| `deep-ai-council.body.md` | Fallback router for bounded AI Council sessions. |\n| `deep-alignment.body.md` | Fallback router for structured alignment audits. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. ROUTER RESPONSIBILITIES\n\nThe legacy bodies own:\n\n- Dispatch-context checks\n- Setup input resolution\n- Execution-mode selection\n- Workflow YAML selection\n- Presentation boundary references where applicable\n\nThe workflow YAML assets own:\n\n- Iteration or round dispatch\n- Artifact writes\n- State reduction\n- Convergence checks\n- Final synthesis\n- Continuity updates\n\nDo not move workflow execution into these router bodies.\n\n---\n\n## 5. MODE ROUTING\n\nEach body recognizes attached command modes:\n\n| Suffix | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `:auto` | Resolve supported inputs non-interactively and load the auto workflow. |\n| `:confirm` | Ask the consolidated setup question and load the confirm workflow. |\n| No suffix | Ask for execution mode through the command's setup flow. |\n\nInputs such as target paths, iteration limits, convergence settings and executor choices remain workflow inputs rather than execution modes.\n\n---\n\n## 6. INJECTION BOUNDARY\n\nRender tooling can return a legacy body directly when a command uses fallback injection.\n\nCompiled contracts live in the sibling `compiled/` folder. Their maintained sources remain authoritative, and generated contract files must not replace the workflow YAML as the owner of runtime execution.\n\n`deep-alignment.body.md` remains especially important because alignment has no generated compiler contract.\n\n---\n\n## 7. VALIDATION\n\nConfirm the expected files exist from the repository root:\n\n```bash\ntest -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-ai-council.body.md\ntest -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-alignment.body.md\ntest -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-research.body.md\ntest -f .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-review.body.md\n```\n\nExpected result: every command exits with status `0`.\n\nValidate command references with the shared checker:\n\n```bash\nnode .opencode/commands/scripts/validate-command-references.cjs\n```\n\nExpected result: the checker reports that command references resolve cleanly.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RELATED\n\n- [Compiled deep command contracts](../compiled/)\n- [Deep command assets](../)\n- [Deep command router files](../../)\n- [Deep-loop skill](../../../../skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":124,"totalLines":124,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/README.md","time":{"start":1785134046794,"end":1785134046802}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_007eeec20c27d4b4016a66fbde93588191bf150574ab34997a"}},"id":"prt_fa247de04001Fvp39wjffkt7Fc","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa247a6350010Z9N8vaX3cs7Rg"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134046820,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_AwGVIWQSOpQh8OMSsTXJe3ZC","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/README.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Compiled Deep Command Contracts\"\n3: description: \"Developer reference for generated deep-command contracts, rollout metadata and the alignment placeholder contract.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"compiled deep contracts\"\n6:   - \"deep command contract manifest\"\n7:   - \"command injection contracts\"\n8: importance_tier: \"important\"\n9: ---\n10: \n11: # Compiled Deep Command Contracts\n12: \n13: > Generated executor contracts and rollout metadata derived from maintained deep-command authorities.\n14: \n15: ---\n16: \n17: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n18: \n19: `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/` stores flattened command contracts used by deep-command injection tooling.\n20: \n21: The generated contracts combine maintained command, workflow, skill, reference and agent sources into grep-checkable executor instructions. Maintained source files remain authoritative.\n22: \n23: ---\n24: \n25: ## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n26: \n27: ```text\n28: compiled/\n29: +-- deep-ai-council.contract.md\n30: +-- deep-alignment.contract.md\n31: +-- deep-research.contract.md\n32: +-- deep-review.contract.md\n33: +-- manifest.jsonl\n34: `-- README.md\n35: ```\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## 3. KEY FILES\n40: \n41: | File | Responsibility |\n42: |---|---|\n43: | `deep-research.contract.md` | Generated executor contract for `/deep:research`. |\n44: | `deep-review.contract.md` | Generated executor contract for `/deep:review`. |\n45: | `deep-ai-council.contract.md` | Generated executor contract for `/deep:ai-council`. |\n46: | `deep-alignment.contract.md` | Placeholder required by manifest hashing while alignment remains outside the compiler command map. |\n47: | `manifest.jsonl` | Append-only render records with command, mode and content digests. |\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 4. GENERATION MODEL\n52: \n53: Generated contracts record:\n54: \n55: - The command identifier and contract version\n56: - The compiler entrypoint\n57: - Source paths and source digests\n58: - The compiled body digest\n59: - Setup and execution rules\n60: - Write boundaries\n61: - Tool grants\n62: - Dispatch or council execution requirements\n63: \n64: The compiler named in generated headers is:\n65: \n66: ```text\n67: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/compile-command-contracts.cjs\n68: ```\n69: \n70: Regenerate a contract when any maintained source digest changes.\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 5. AUTHORITY BOUNDARY\n75: \n76: The generated contracts are derived artifacts. Do not edit their generated sections by hand.\n77: \n78: `deep-alignment.contract.md` is different. It documents that `/deep:alignment` is not registered in the compiler and that fallback injection uses the matching legacy body. It must not act as an execution authority.\n79: \n80: The maintained command files, workflow YAML assets, skill instructions and referenced runtime files remain the source of truth.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 6. MANIFEST\n85: \n86: Each `manifest.jsonl` row records:\n87: \n88: | Field | Meaning |\n89: |---|---|\n90: | `command` | Deep command identifier. |\n91: | `mode` | Injection or render mode. |\n92: | `argsSha256` | Digest of bound render arguments. |\n93: | `legacyBodySha256` | Digest of the legacy command body. |\n94: | `compiledContractSha256` | Digest of the compiled contract file. |\n95: | `renderedSha256` | Digest of the rendered command payload. |\n96: \n97: The manifest can contain multiple records for the same command because each render appends evidence for a specific mode and input set.\n98: \n99: ---\n100: \n101: ## 7. VALIDATION\n102: \n103: Check the JSONL structure from the repository root:\n104: \n105: ```bash\n106: node -e '\n107: const fs = require(\"fs\");\n108: const lines = fs.readFileSync(\".opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/manifest.jsonl\", \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\");\n109: for (const line of lines) JSON.parse(line);\n110: console.log(`OK ${lines.length} manifest rows`);\n111: '\n112: ```\n113: \n114: Expected result: every non-empty line parses as JSON and the command prints an `OK` count.\n115: \n116: Use the deep-loop compiler's validation path when verifying contract freshness. Do not infer freshness from file presence alone.\n117: \n118: ---\n119: \n120: ## 8. RELATED\n121: \n122: - [Legacy deep command bodies](../legacy/)\n123: - [Deep command assets](../)\n124: - [Deep command router files](../../)\n125: - [Deep-loop skill](../../../../skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md)\n\n(End of file - total 125 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: \"Compiled Deep Command Contracts\"\ndescription: \"Developer reference for generated deep-command contracts, rollout metadata and the alignment placeholder contract.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"compiled deep contracts\"\n  - \"deep command contract manifest\"\n  - \"command injection contracts\"\nimportance_tier: \"important\"\n---\n\n# Compiled Deep Command Contracts\n\n> Generated executor contracts and rollout metadata derived from maintained deep-command authorities.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/` stores flattened command contracts used by deep-command injection tooling.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/README.md","text":"---\ntitle: \"Compiled Deep Command Contracts\"\ndescription: \"Developer reference for generated deep-command contracts, rollout metadata and the alignment placeholder contract.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"compiled deep contracts\"\n  - \"deep command contract manifest\"\n  - \"command injection contracts\"\nimportance_tier: \"important\"\n---\n\n# Compiled Deep Command Contracts\n\n> Generated executor contracts and rollout metadata derived from maintained deep-command authorities.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n`.opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/` stores flattened command contracts used by deep-command injection tooling.\n\nThe generated contracts combine maintained command, workflow, skill, reference and agent sources into grep-checkable executor instructions. Maintained source files remain authoritative.\n\n---\n\n## 2. DIRECTORY TREE\n\n```text\ncompiled/\n+-- deep-ai-council.contract.md\n+-- deep-alignment.contract.md\n+-- deep-research.contract.md\n+-- deep-review.contract.md\n+-- manifest.jsonl\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `deep-research.contract.md` | Generated executor contract for `/deep:research`. |\n| `deep-review.contract.md` | Generated executor contract for `/deep:review`. |\n| `deep-ai-council.contract.md` | Generated executor contract for `/deep:ai-council`. |\n| `deep-alignment.contract.md` | Placeholder required by manifest hashing while alignment remains outside the compiler command map. |\n| `manifest.jsonl` | Append-only render records with command, mode and content digests. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. GENERATION MODEL\n\nGenerated contracts record:\n\n- The command identifier and contract version\n- The compiler entrypoint\n- Source paths and source digests\n- The compiled body digest\n- Setup and execution rules\n- Write boundaries\n- Tool grants\n- Dispatch or council execution requirements\n\nThe compiler named in generated headers is:\n\n```text\n.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/compile-command-contracts.cjs\n```\n\nRegenerate a contract when any maintained source digest changes.\n\n---\n\n## 5. AUTHORITY BOUNDARY\n\nThe generated contracts are derived artifacts. Do not edit their generated sections by hand.\n\n`deep-alignment.contract.md` is different. It documents that `/deep:alignment` is not registered in the compiler and that fallback injection uses the matching legacy body. It must not act as an execution authority.\n\nThe maintained command files, workflow YAML assets, skill instructions and referenced runtime files remain the source of truth.\n\n---\n\n## 6. MANIFEST\n\nEach `manifest.jsonl` row records:\n\n| Field | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `command` | Deep command identifier. |\n| `mode` | Injection or render mode. |\n| `argsSha256` | Digest of bound render arguments. |\n| `legacyBodySha256` | Digest of the legacy command body. |\n| `compiledContractSha256` | Digest of the compiled contract file. |\n| `renderedSha256` | Digest of the rendered command payload. |\n\nThe manifest can contain multiple records for the same command because each render appends evidence for a specific mode and input set.\n\n---\n\n## 7. VALIDATION\n\nCheck the JSONL structure from the repository root:\n\n```bash\nnode -e '\nconst fs = require(\"fs\");\nconst lines = fs.readFileSync(\".opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/manifest.jsonl\", \"utf8\").trim().split(\"\\n\");\nfor (const line of lines) JSON.parse(line);\nconsole.log(`OK ${lines.length} manifest rows`);\n'\n```\n\nExpected result: every non-empty line parses as JSON and the command prints an `OK` count.\n\nUse the deep-loop compiler's validation path when verifying contract freshness. Do not infer freshness from file presence alone.\n\n---\n\n## 8. RELATED\n\n- [Legacy deep command bodies](../legacy/)\n- [Deep command assets](../)\n- [Deep command router files](../../)\n- [Deep-loop skill](../../../../skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md)","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":125,"totalLines":125,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/README.md","time":{"start":1785134046808,"end":1785134046819}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_007eeec20c27d4b4016a66fbde938c819189ba06099cc826b5"}},"id":"prt_fa247de53001SixyROc0NcDJx2","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa247a6350010Z9N8vaX3cs7Rg"}}
