h `assets/legacy/deep_<name>.body.md` under the existing frontmatter + `# H1`, and REMOVE the `!node render-command-contract.cjs` bang line.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/012-deep-command-family-parity/004-pipeline-command-router-inline/plan.md:\n  Line 34: | **Storage** | `.opencode/commands/deep/*.md`, `assets/compiled/*`, `assets/legacy/*`, `shared/rollout/command-injection-rollout.json` |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/012-deep-command-family-parity/004-pipeline-command-router-inline/tasks.md:\n  Line 43: - [ ] T001 Read the 4 stubs + their legacy bodies + their compiled `autonomousExecutionDirective` blocks (`deep/{research,review,ai-council,alignment}.md`, `assets/legacy/*`, `assets/compiled/*`) [20m]\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/012-deep-command-family-parity/001-pipeline-command-parity/spec.md:\n  Line 74: | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md` | Modify | Owned-assets references presentation |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/012-deep-command-family-parity/001-pipeline-command-parity/implementation-summary.md:\n  Line 52: | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md` | Modified | §2 owned-assets references the presentation; fallback note replaced |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/012-deep-command-family-parity/001-pipeline-command-parity/graph-metadata.json:\n  Line 41:       \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md\",\n\n  Line 76:         \"path\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/012-deep-command-family-parity/graph-metadata.json:\n  Line 51:       \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md\",\n\n  Line 89:         \"path\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/009-deep-loop-parallel-fanout/008-deep-review/review/iterations/iteration-015.md:\n  Line 7574: .opencode/skills/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/07--command-flow-stress-tests/leaf-only-nested-dispatch-refusal.md:88:| CP-056 | LEAF_ONLY_REFUSAL | Prove @deep-review body rejects nested dispatch bait | `As a deep-review boundary tester, execute the nested-dispatch refusal scenario. Verify @deep-review refuses Task delegation. Return a grep-backed PASS/FAIL verdict.` | Run §3 exactly | Field counts all `1+` | Body transcript, state log, target/agent diffs, tripwire | PASS if nested dispatch is refused and no Task invocation appears | If Task appears, repair agent body LEAF hard block. If diffs are non-empty, repair write boundary. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/008-divergent-mode-dogfood/research/iterations/iteration-009.md:\n  Line 26: Executor timeout accepts any positive integer, and `--lineage-timeout-hours` can raise the four-hour ceiling to any positive value. Fan-out also permits `lagCeilingMs = 0`, `progressHeartbeatSeconds = 0`, and a raw `stallWatchdogMs = 0`; the watchdog only emits a warning and the synthetic heartbeat currently refreshes the timestamp it observes. A finite absolute process-tree lifetime, TERM-to-KILL reaping, and child-observed stall enforcement should be non-bypassable for autonomous runs. Operators may select shorter timeouts or request a longer timeout inside the absolute ceiling. Telemetry cadence may be disabled or tuned because it affects observability volume, but disabling telemetry must not disable or refresh the independent safety watchdog. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts:34-46,272-282] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:646-655,1059-1076,1131-1187,1385-1399] [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md:120-126]\n\n  Line 30: `maxIterations`, convergence threshold/mode, `stop-policy=max-iterations`, and council topic/round dimensions express desired evidence depth rather than containment by themselves. Making their defaults immutable would remove legitimate exhaustive-review and multi-topic use cases. They should remain operator controls, but values above the conservative default or policies that suppress early convergence should show the computed worst-case dispatch envelope and require an explicit opt-in. In `:confirm`, record operator identity/rationale and the resolved upper bound; in `:auto`, accept only a dedicated pre-bound override marker or flag and reject any value that crosses hard limits. [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep_research.contract.md:199-219,246-267] [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md:109-126] [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep_ai-council.contract.md:275-290,321-338]\n\n  Line 52: - Making every current default immutable is ruled out because evidence-depth controls legitimately vary by task; containment must instead be enforced on the computed aggregate envelope. [SOURCE: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md:120-126] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/references/convergence/depth_dispatch.md:33-37]\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/030-deep-loop-unification/008-divergent-mode-dogfood/research/research.md:\n  Line 148: | Make every current default immutable | Would remove legitimate exhaustive-review / multi-topic use cases; containment should target the computed aggregate envelope instead | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md:120-126` | 9 |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/001-deep-loop-market-research/research/iterations/iteration-034.md:\n  Line 262: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/001-deep-loop-market-research/research/iterations/iteration-032.md:\n  Line 288: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md\n\n  Line 289: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_ai-council.body.md\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/001-deep-loop-market-research/research/iterations/iteration-033.md:\n  Line 237: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/006-deep-skill-evolution/001-release-cleanup/007-deep-review-release-cleanup/research/iterations/iteration-007.md:\n  Line 41: - CP-056 tests: @deep-review body refuses nested agent dispatch requests instead of delegating <ref_file file=\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/deep-review/manual_testing_playbook/07--command-flow-stress-tests/leaf-only-nested-dispatch-refusal.md\" lines=\"14-18\" />\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/002-deep-loop-effectiveness-and-fanout/research/iterations-modes/iteration-030.md:\n  Line 284: .opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/036-deep-loop-innovation/003-baseline-taxonomy-and-state-census/pre-existing-kebab-renames.json:\n  Line 155:       \"from\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_ai-council.body.md\",\n\n  Line 156:       \"to\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-ai-council.body.md\"\n\n  Line 160:       \"from\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_alignment.body.md\",\n\n  Line 161:       \"to\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-alignment.body.md\"\n\n  Line 165:       \"from\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_research.body.md\",\n\n  Line 166:       \"to\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-research.body.md\"\n\n  Line 170:       \"from\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_review.body.md\",\n\n  Line 171:       \"to\": \".opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep-review.body.md\"\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/028-deprecate-deep-context-integrate-capabilities/002-public-redirect-and-replacement-contracts/spec.md:\n  Line 112: | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_context.body.md` | Modify if still authoritative | Replace executable setup flow with deprecation guidance or align it with restored command source. |\n\n  Line 254: - Should `.opencode/commands/deep/context.md` be restored as the maintained source, or should the command compiler be updated to use `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_context.body.md`?\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/028-deprecate-deep-context-integrate-capabilities/002-public-redirect-and-replacement-contracts/plan.md:\n  Line 115: | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_context.body.md` | Observed router body for legacy command source | Update or replace after source authority resolution | Read source, grep redirect text |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-deep-loop/z_archive/028-deprecate-deep-context-integrate-capabilities/002-public-redirect-and-replacement-contracts/checklist.md:\n  Line 67: - [x] CHK-012 [P0] Maintained command source contains fail-closed redirect logic. [EVIDENCE: `.opencode/commands/deep/context.md`; `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/legacy/deep_context.body.md`; `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep_context_presentation.txt`.]\n","metadata":{"matches":85,"truncated":false},"title":"assets/legacy|deep-research.body|deep-review.body|deep-ai-council.body|deep-alignment.body","time":{"start":1785134046932,"end":1785134047849}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_007eeec20c27d4b4016a66fbde93948191bce73109224695d7"}},"id":"prt_fa247de59001x9m5petIfQ0ir4","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa247a6350010Z9N8vaX3cs7Rg"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1785134048899,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"id":"prt_fa247e680001zzvtEl2xMdpUyg","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fa247a6350010Z9N8vaX3cs7Rg","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":312772,"input":549,"output":288,"reasoning":127,"cache":{"write":0,"read":311808}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785134054489,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"id":"prt_fa247fc4f001dzC5tscWxLRuuF","messageID":"msg_fa247ea84001ghGyIJKW01ed5D","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134062329,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UFES1CJ2xgDouuMO3VH8GDJO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/opencode.json"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/opencode.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n3:   \"permission\": {\n4:     \"edit\": \"allow\",\n5:     \"bash\": \"allow\",\n6:     \"webfetch\": \"allow\",\n7:     \"doom_loop\": \"allow\",\n8:     \"external_directory\": \"allow\"\n9:   },\n10:   \"mcp\": {\n11:     \"sequential_thinking\": {\n12:       \"type\": \"local\",\n13:       \"command\": [\n14:         \"npx\",\n15:         \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking@2025.12.18\"\n16:       ]\n17:     },\n18:     \"mk-spec-memory\": {\n19:       \"type\": \"local\",\n20:       \"command\": [\n21:         \"node\",\n22:         \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n23:       ],\n24:       \"environment\": {\n25:         \"EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"auto\",\n26:         \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n27:         \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-spec-memory\",\n28:         \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n29:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_BATCH_SIZE\": \"100\",\n30:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_INTERVAL_MS\": \"5000\",\n31:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_AGE_MS\": \"3153600000000\",\n32:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_PENDING\": \"300000\",\n33:         \"_NOTE_RECOMMENDED_SETUP\": \"New users: install Ollama (https://ollama.com) and run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. The cascade auto-detects Ollama and persists nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (768d) as the active embedder — no API keys, all-local.\",\n34:         \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Default DB (recommended): context-index__ollama__nomic-embed-text-v1.5__768.sqlite (auto-derived from provider+model+dim). Pull `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` for the local-first new-user setup; hf-local with nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 is the zero-install Node fallback (no Python).\",\n35:         \"_NOTE_PROVIDERS\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama (local) -> hf-local (pure-Node @huggingface/transformers HTTP model server, zero-install) -> OpenAI API -> Voyage API.\",\n36:         \"_NOTE_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama -> hf-local -> OpenAI -> Voyage. Set EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=<provider> (ollama|hf-local|openai|voyage) to force a specific tier.\",\n37:         \"_NOTE_CLOUD_PROVIDERS\": \"Cloud tiers are explicit opt-in: add VOYAGE_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY only when you want cloud embeddings; otherwise the cascade keeps everything local. Voyage is embeddings-only here; cloud rerankers (voyage/cohere) were removed in 022/013.\",\n38:         \"_NOTE_GET_VOYAGE_KEY\": \"Get Voyage key: https://dash.voyageai.com/api-keys\",\n39:         \"_NOTE_GET_OPENAI_KEY\": \"Get OpenAI key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\",\n40:         \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket. Pinned identically for mk-spec-memory AND mk_skill_advisor so both consume ONE resident nomic server (single-owner via the socket-keyed respawn lock). Short /tmp path stays under the macOS sun_path 104-char limit. Do not diverge the two services.\",\n41:         \"_NOTE_SOCKET\": \"macOS sun_path limit (104 chars): the default bridge socket path under database/daemon-ipc.sock exceeds the limit and the launcher fails with EINVAL. Pin to a short /tmp path so the multi-client bridge can bind.\",\n42:         \"_NOTE_FEATURE_FLAGS\": \"Opt-out flags (default ON): SPECKIT_ADAPTIVE_FUSION, SPECKIT_SESSION_BOOST, SPECKIT_CAUSAL_BOOST, SPECKIT_HYDE_ACTIVE, SPECKIT_ENTITY_LINKING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_CONCEPT_ROUTING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_REFRESH_MODE=write_local. Tier 3 LLM save routing is always on (fail-open to Tier 2 on timeout).\",\n43:         \"_NOTE_DAEMON_REELECTION\": \"Daemon re-election is on by default in the launcher code: on disposal the launcher releases the shared daemon for a live secondary to adopt instead of killing it, so concurrent sessions keep MCP transport. An unadopted released daemon is bounded by SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN. Set SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION=0 to restore kill-on-disposal. See ENV_REFERENCE.md.\",\n44:         \"_NOTE_RETRY_TUNING\": \"Bulk re-embed retry tuning: raised pending cap + max-age + faster batch/interval so a large embedding backlog drains instead of being parked as failed (defaults park excess/old pending: cap 1000, 24h age, 5-per-5min).\"\n45:       }\n46:     },\n47:     \"mk_skill_advisor\": {\n48:       \"type\": \"local\",\n49:       \"command\": [\n50:         \"node\",\n51:         \".opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\"\n52:       ],\n53:       \"environment\": {\n54:         \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n55:         \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database\",\n56:         \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\": \"0\",\n57:         \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"trusted\",\n58:         \"SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"true\",\n59:         \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-skill-advisor\",\n60:         \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n61:         \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives at .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite by default; MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR overrides, with SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR as a legacy fallback (both still recognized by the launcher + handlers).\",\n62:         \"_NOTE_MEMORY_DB_PATH\": \"createChildEnv() pins the advisor child's embedder-pointer resolution (which DB's active_embedder_* row gets read) to this package's own skill-graph.sqlite. An ambient MEMORY_DB_PATH — including one set for mk-spec-memory's own unrelated use of that same name — is never honored as an override, since that would silently misroute the advisor's embedder selection to spec-memory's database (the exact bug this pin fixed). Tests/CI only: MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_MEMORY_DB_PATH overrides the pin. See db_path_policy.md §4.\",\n63:         \"_NOTE_THRESHOLDS\": \"Advisor confidence/uncertainty thresholds are tunable: SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD (default 0.8), SPECKIT_ADVISOR_UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD (default 0.35). Lane weights tunable via SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON + SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON (partial-merge JSON, post-022/011/4b).\",\n64:         \"_NOTE_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"Opt-in doc-frontmatter harvest: skill_graph_scan ingests references/assets trigger_phrases into skill_docs and advisor_recommend returns matchedDocs pointers (dampened derived-lane signal). Default-off in code; enabled for this repo. Unset/false to roll back.\",\n65:         \"_NOTE_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"Daemon-owner trust grant for mutation tools (advisor_rebuild, skill_graph_scan, skill_graph_propagate_enhances). Callers whose _meta omits transport/trust markers default to UNTRUSTED unless this is 'trusted'. Native MCP clients (e.g. /doctor repair flows) send no _meta, so this grant keeps them working; remove it to fail-closed on every transport-absent caller. Explicit _meta trusted:false / callerAuthority:'untrusted' is always rejected.\",\n66:         \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket — identical to mk-spec-memory's so both services share ONE resident nomic server. (skill-advisor only spawns it when SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_MODEL_SERVER_ENABLED=1; otherwise it just connects to mk-spec-memory's.)\"\n67:       }\n68:     },\n69:     \"mk_code_index\": {\n70:       \"type\": \"local\",\n71:       \"command\": [\n72:         \"node\",\n73:         \".opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs\"\n74:       ],\n75:       \"environment\": {\n76:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_AGENTS\": \"true\",\n77:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_COMMANDS\": \"true\",\n78:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_PLUGINS\": \"true\",\n79:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SKILLS\": \"true\",\n80:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SPECS\": \"true\",\n81:         \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-code-index\",\n82:         \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n83:         \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives SKILL-LOCAL at .opencode/skills/system-code-graph/mcp-server/database/code-graph.sqlite by default (shared across runtimes via the .opencode/skills symlink); SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR overrides. Former shared location (.opencode/.spec-kit/code-graph/database/) is migrated back on first launcher startup.\",\n84:         \"_NOTE_INDEX_DEFAULTS\": \"INDEX_* committed defaults are false (end-user safe). Maintainer mode: set SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_MAINTAINER_MODE in .env.local (gitignored) to true (forces all 5 INDEX_* to true) or to a comma-separated subset such as skills,plugins (forces only those categories); the launcher applies the selection at startup. Per-call code_graph_scan args (includeSkills, includeAgents, includeCommands, includeSpecs, includePlugins) still override env for fine-grained control.\",\n85:         \"_NOTE_RESCAN_THRESHOLD\": \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_SELECTIVE_REINDEX_THRESHOLD (default 50) controls when the launcher switches from selective rescan to full scan. Raise to delay full-scans (faster session-boot, more drift tolerance); lower to keep the DB tighter. Post-commit hook (.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/post-commit) also invalidates the SQLite when commits exceed SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_POST_COMMIT_REBUILD_THRESHOLD (default 100).\"\n86:       }\n87:     },\n88:     \"code_mode\": {\n89:       \"type\": \"local\",\n90:       \"command\": [\n91:         \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v24.9.0/bin/node\",\n92:         \".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/mcp-server/dist/index.js\"\n93:       ],\n94:       \"environment\": {\n95:         \"UTCP_CONFIG_FILE\": \".utcp_config.json\"\n96:       }\n97:     }\n98:   },\n99:   \"experimental\": {\n100:     \"disable_paste_summary\": true\n101:   }\n102: }\n\n(End of file - total 102 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n  \"permission\": {\n    \"edit\": \"allow\",\n    \"bash\": \"allow\",\n    \"webfetch\": \"allow\",\n    \"doom_loop\": \"allow\",\n    \"external_directory\": \"allow\"\n  },\n  \"mcp\": {\n    \"sequential_thinking\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"npx\",\n        \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking@2025.12.18\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mk-spec-memory\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/opencode.json","text":"{\n  \"$schema\": \"https://opencode.ai/config.json\",\n  \"permission\": {\n    \"edit\": \"allow\",\n    \"bash\": \"allow\",\n    \"webfetch\": \"allow\",\n    \"doom_loop\": \"allow\",\n    \"external_directory\": \"allow\"\n  },\n  \"mcp\": {\n    \"sequential_thinking\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"npx\",\n        \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking@2025.12.18\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mk-spec-memory\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"node\",\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"environment\": {\n        \"EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"auto\",\n        \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-spec-memory\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_BATCH_SIZE\": \"100\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_INTERVAL_MS\": \"5000\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_AGE_MS\": \"3153600000000\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_PENDING\": \"300000\",\n        \"_NOTE_RECOMMENDED_SETUP\": \"New users: install Ollama (https://ollama.com) and run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. The cascade auto-detects Ollama and persists nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (768d) as the active embedder — no API keys, all-local.\",\n        \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Default DB (recommended): context-index__ollama__nomic-embed-text-v1.5__768.sqlite (auto-derived from provider+model+dim). Pull `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` for the local-first new-user setup; hf-local with nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 is the zero-install Node fallback (no Python).\",\n        \"_NOTE_PROVIDERS\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama (local) -> hf-local (pure-Node @huggingface/transformers HTTP model server, zero-install) -> OpenAI API -> Voyage API.\",\n        \"_NOTE_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama -> hf-local -> OpenAI -> Voyage. Set EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=<provider> (ollama|hf-local|openai|voyage) to force a specific tier.\",\n        \"_NOTE_CLOUD_PROVIDERS\": \"Cloud tiers are explicit opt-in: add VOYAGE_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY only when you want cloud embeddings; otherwise the cascade keeps everything local. Voyage is embeddings-only here; cloud rerankers (voyage/cohere) were removed in 022/013.\",\n        \"_NOTE_GET_VOYAGE_KEY\": \"Get Voyage key: https://dash.voyageai.com/api-keys\",\n        \"_NOTE_GET_OPENAI_KEY\": \"Get OpenAI key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\",\n        \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket. Pinned identically for mk-spec-memory AND mk_skill_advisor so both consume ONE resident nomic server (single-owner via the socket-keyed respawn lock). Short /tmp path stays under the macOS sun_path 104-char limit. Do not diverge the two services.\",\n        \"_NOTE_SOCKET\": \"macOS sun_path limit (104 chars): the default bridge socket path under database/daemon-ipc.sock exceeds the limit and the launcher fails with EINVAL. Pin to a short /tmp path so the multi-client bridge can bind.\",\n        \"_NOTE_FEATURE_FLAGS\": \"Opt-out flags (default ON): SPECKIT_ADAPTIVE_FUSION, SPECKIT_SESSION_BOOST, SPECKIT_CAUSAL_BOOST, SPECKIT_HYDE_ACTIVE, SPECKIT_ENTITY_LINKING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_CONCEPT_ROUTING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_REFRESH_MODE=write_local. Tier 3 LLM save routing is always on (fail-open to Tier 2 on timeout).\",\n        \"_NOTE_DAEMON_REELECTION\": \"Daemon re-election is on by default in the launcher code: on disposal the launcher releases the shared daemon for a live secondary to adopt instead of killing it, so concurrent sessions keep MCP transport. An unadopted released daemon is bounded by SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN. Set SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION=0 to restore kill-on-disposal. See ENV_REFERENCE.md.\",\n        \"_NOTE_RETRY_TUNING\": \"Bulk re-embed retry tuning: raised pending cap + max-age + faster batch/interval so a large embedding backlog drains instead of being parked as failed (defaults park excess/old pending: cap 1000, 24h age, 5-per-5min).\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"mk_skill_advisor\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"node\",\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"environment\": {\n        \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n        \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database\",\n        \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\": \"0\",\n        \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"trusted\",\n        \"SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-skill-advisor\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives at .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite by default; MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR overrides, with SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR as a legacy fallback (both still recognized by the launcher + handlers).\",\n        \"_NOTE_MEMORY_DB_PATH\": \"createChildEnv() pins the advisor child's embedder-pointer resolution (which DB's active_embedder_* row gets read) to this package's own skill-graph.sqlite. An ambient MEMORY_DB_PATH — including one set for mk-spec-memory's own unrelated use of that same name — is never honored as an override, since that would silently misroute the advisor's embedder selection to spec-memory's database (the exact bug this pin fixed). Tests/CI only: MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_MEMORY_DB_PATH overrides the pin. See db_path_policy.md §4.\",\n        \"_NOTE_THRESHOLDS\": \"Advisor confidence/uncertainty thresholds are tunable: SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD (default 0.8), SPECKIT_ADVISOR_UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD (default 0.35). Lane weights tunable via SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON + SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON (partial-merge JSON, post-022/011/4b).\",\n        \"_NOTE_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"Opt-in doc-frontmatter harvest: skill_graph_scan ingests references/assets trigger_phrases into skill_docs and advisor_recommend returns matchedDocs pointers (dampened derived-lane signal). Default-off in code; enabled for this repo. Unset/false to roll back.\",\n        \"_NOTE_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"Daemon-owner trust grant for mutation tools (advisor_rebuild, skill_graph_scan, skill_graph_propagate_enhances). Callers whose _meta omits transport/trust markers default to UNTRUSTED unless this is 'trusted'. Native MCP clients (e.g. /doctor repair flows) send no _meta, so this grant keeps them working; remove it to fail-closed on every transport-absent caller. Explicit _meta trusted:false / callerAuthority:'untrusted' is always rejected.\",\n        \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket — identical to mk-spec-memory's so both services share ONE resident nomic server. (skill-advisor only spawns it when SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_MODEL_SERVER_ENABLED=1; otherwise it just connects to mk-spec-memory's.)\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"mk_code_index\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"node\",\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"environment\": {\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_AGENTS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_COMMANDS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_PLUGINS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SKILLS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SPECS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-code-index\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives SKILL-LOCAL at .opencode/skills/system-code-graph/mcp-server/database/code-graph.sqlite by default (shared across runtimes via the .opencode/skills symlink); SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR overrides. Former shared location (.opencode/.spec-kit/code-graph/database/) is migrated back on first launcher startup.\",\n        \"_NOTE_INDEX_DEFAULTS\": \"INDEX_* committed defaults are false (end-user safe). Maintainer mode: set SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_MAINTAINER_MODE in .env.local (gitignored) to true (forces all 5 INDEX_* to true) or to a comma-separated subset such as skills,plugins (forces only those categories); the launcher applies the selection at startup. Per-call code_graph_scan args (includeSkills, includeAgents, includeCommands, includeSpecs, includePlugins) still override env for fine-grained control.\",\n        \"_NOTE_RESCAN_THRESHOLD\": \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_SELECTIVE_REINDEX_THRESHOLD (default 50) controls when the launcher switches from selective rescan to full scan. Raise to delay full-scans (faster session-boot, more drift tolerance); lower to keep the DB tighter. Post-commit hook (.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/post-commit) also invalidates the SQLite when commits exceed SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_POST_COMMIT_REBUILD_THRESHOLD (default 100).\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"code_mode\": {\n      \"type\": \"local\",\n      \"command\": [\n        \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v24.9.0/bin/node\",\n        \".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/mcp-server/dist/index.js\"\n      ],\n      \"environment\": {\n        \"UTCP_CONFIG_FILE\": \".utcp_config.json\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"experimental\": {\n    \"disable_paste_summary\": true\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":102,"totalLines":102,"truncated":false}},"title":"opencode.json","time":{"start":1785134062297,"end":1785134062322}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a4297b86da91746016a66fbee22848191b0858928139f2bfd"}},"id":"prt_fa2481ad50017VYDr51cendSW0","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa247ea84001ghGyIJKW01ed5D"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134062329,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_zsCJzw0dolEHfDZAInIVnOvx","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.mcp.json"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.mcp.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"mcpServers\": {\n3:     \"sequential_thinking\": {\n4:       \"command\": \"npx\",\n5:       \"args\": [\n6:         \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking@2025.12.18\"\n7:       ]\n8:     },\n9:     \"mk-spec-memory\": {\n10:       \"command\": \"node\",\n11:       \"args\": [\n12:         \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n13:       ],\n14:       \"env\": {\n15:         \"EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"auto\",\n16:         \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n17:         \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-spec-memory\",\n18:         \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n19:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_BATCH_SIZE\": \"100\",\n20:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_INTERVAL_MS\": \"5000\",\n21:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_AGE_MS\": \"3153600000000\",\n22:         \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_PENDING\": \"300000\",\n23:         \"_NOTE_RECOMMENDED_SETUP\": \"New users: install Ollama (https://ollama.com) and run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. The cascade auto-detects Ollama and persists nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (768d) as the active embedder — no API keys, all-local.\",\n24:         \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Default DB (recommended): context-index__ollama__nomic-embed-text-v1.5__768.sqlite (auto-derived from provider+model+dim). Pull `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` for the local-first new-user setup; hf-local with nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 is the zero-install Node fallback (no Python).\",\n25:         \"_NOTE_PROVIDERS\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama (local) -> hf-local (pure-Node @huggingface/transformers HTTP model server, zero-install) -> OpenAI API -> Voyage API.\",\n26:         \"_NOTE_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama -> hf-local -> OpenAI -> Voyage. Set EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=<provider> (ollama|hf-local|openai|voyage) to force a specific tier.\",\n27:         \"_NOTE_CLOUD_PROVIDERS\": \"Cloud tiers are explicit opt-in: add VOYAGE_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY only when you want cloud embeddings; otherwise the cascade keeps everything local. Voyage is embeddings-only here; cloud rerankers (voyage/cohere) were removed in 022/013.\",\n28:         \"_NOTE_GET_VOYAGE_KEY\": \"Get Voyage key: https://dash.voyageai.com/api-keys\",\n29:         \"_NOTE_GET_OPENAI_KEY\": \"Get OpenAI key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\",\n30:         \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket. Pinned identically for mk-spec-memory AND mk_skill_advisor so both consume ONE resident nomic server (single-owner via the socket-keyed respawn lock). Short /tmp path stays under the macOS sun_path 104-char limit. Do not diverge the two services.\",\n31:         \"_NOTE_SOCKET\": \"macOS sun_path limit (104 chars): the default bridge socket path under database/daemon-ipc.sock exceeds the limit and the launcher fails with EINVAL. Pin to a short /tmp path so the multi-client bridge can bind.\",\n32:         \"_NOTE_FEATURE_FLAGS\": \"Opt-out flags (default ON): SPECKIT_ADAPTIVE_FUSION, SPECKIT_SESSION_BOOST, SPECKIT_CAUSAL_BOOST, SPECKIT_HYDE_ACTIVE, SPECKIT_ENTITY_LINKING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_CONCEPT_ROUTING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_REFRESH_MODE=write_local. Tier 3 LLM save routing is always on (fail-open to Tier 2 on timeout).\",\n33:         \"_NOTE_DAEMON_REELECTION\": \"Daemon re-election is on by default in the launcher code: on disposal the launcher releases the shared daemon for a live secondary to adopt instead of killing it, so concurrent sessions keep MCP transport. An unadopted released daemon is bounded by SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN. Set SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION=0 to restore kill-on-disposal. See ENV_REFERENCE.md.\",\n34:         \"_NOTE_RETRY_TUNING\": \"Bulk re-embed retry tuning: raised pending cap + max-age + faster batch/interval so a large embedding backlog drains instead of being parked as failed (defaults park excess/old pending: cap 1000, 24h age, 5-per-5min).\"\n35:       }\n36:     },\n37:     \"mk_skill_advisor\": {\n38:       \"command\": \"node\",\n39:       \"args\": [\n40:         \".opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\"\n41:       ],\n42:       \"env\": {\n43:         \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n44:         \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database\",\n45:         \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\": \"0\",\n46:         \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"trusted\",\n47:         \"SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"true\",\n48:         \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-skill-advisor\",\n49:         \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n50:         \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives at .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite by default; MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR overrides, with SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR as a legacy fallback (both still recognized by the launcher + handlers).\",\n51:         \"_NOTE_MEMORY_DB_PATH\": \"createChildEnv() pins the advisor child's embedder-pointer resolution (which DB's active_embedder_* row gets read) to this package's own skill-graph.sqlite. An ambient MEMORY_DB_PATH — including one set for mk-spec-memory's own unrelated use of that same name — is never honored as an override, since that would silently misroute the advisor's embedder selection to spec-memory's database (the exact bug this pin fixed). Tests/CI only: MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_MEMORY_DB_PATH overrides the pin. See db_path_policy.md §4.\",\n52:         \"_NOTE_THRESHOLDS\": \"Advisor confidence/uncertainty thresholds are tunable: SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD (default 0.8), SPECKIT_ADVISOR_UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD (default 0.35). Lane weights tunable via SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON + SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON (partial-merge JSON, post-022/011/4b).\",\n53:         \"_NOTE_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"Opt-in doc-frontmatter harvest: skill_graph_scan ingests references/assets trigger_phrases into skill_docs and advisor_recommend returns matchedDocs pointers (dampened derived-lane signal). Default-off in code; enabled for this repo. Unset/false to roll back.\",\n54:         \"_NOTE_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"Daemon-owner trust grant for mutation tools (advisor_rebuild, skill_graph_scan, skill_graph_propagate_enhances). Callers whose _meta omits transport/trust markers default to UNTRUSTED unless this is 'trusted'. Native MCP clients (e.g. /doctor repair flows) send no _meta, so this grant keeps them working; remove it to fail-closed on every transport-absent caller. Explicit _meta trusted:false / callerAuthority:'untrusted' is always rejected.\",\n55:         \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket — identical to mk-spec-memory's so both services share ONE resident nomic server. (skill-advisor only spawns it when SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_MODEL_SERVER_ENABLED=1; otherwise it just connects to mk-spec-memory's.)\"\n56:       }\n57:     },\n58:     \"mk_code_index\": {\n59:       \"command\": \"node\",\n60:       \"args\": [\n61:         \".opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs\"\n62:       ],\n63:       \"env\": {\n64:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_AGENTS\": \"true\",\n65:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_COMMANDS\": \"true\",\n66:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_PLUGINS\": \"true\",\n67:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SKILLS\": \"true\",\n68:         \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SPECS\": \"true\",\n69:         \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-code-index\",\n70:         \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n71:         \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives SKILL-LOCAL at .opencode/skills/system-code-graph/mcp-server/database/code-graph.sqlite by default (shared across runtimes via the .opencode/skills symlink); SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR overrides. Former shared location (.opencode/.spec-kit/code-graph/database/) is migrated back on first launcher startup.\",\n72:         \"_NOTE_INDEX_DEFAULTS\": \"INDEX_* committed defaults are false (end-user safe). Maintainer mode: set SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_MAINTAINER_MODE in .env.local (gitignored) to true (forces all 5 INDEX_* to true) or to a comma-separated subset such as skills,plugins (forces only those categories); the launcher applies the selection at startup. Per-call code_graph_scan args (includeSkills, includeAgents, includeCommands, includeSpecs, includePlugins) still override env for fine-grained control.\",\n73:         \"_NOTE_RESCAN_THRESHOLD\": \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_SELECTIVE_REINDEX_THRESHOLD (default 50) controls when the launcher switches from selective rescan to full scan. Raise to delay full-scans (faster session-boot, more drift tolerance); lower to keep the DB tighter. Post-commit hook (.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/post-commit) also invalidates the SQLite when commits exceed SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_POST_COMMIT_REBUILD_THRESHOLD (default 100).\"\n74:       }\n75:     },\n76:     \"code_mode\": {\n77:       \"command\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v24.9.0/bin/node\",\n78:       \"args\": [\n79:         \".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/mcp-server/dist/index.js\"\n80:       ],\n81:       \"env\": {\n82:         \"UTCP_CONFIG_FILE\": \".utcp_config.json\"\n83:       }\n84:     }\n85:   }\n86: }\n\n(End of file - total 86 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"sequential_thinking\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking@2025.12.18\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mk-spec-memory\": {\n      \"command\": \"node\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"auto\",\n        \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-spec-memory\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_BATCH_SIZE\": \"100\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_INTERVAL_MS\": \"5000\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.mcp.json","text":"{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"sequential_thinking\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \"@modelcontextprotocol/server-sequential-thinking@2025.12.18\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"mk-spec-memory\": {\n      \"command\": \"node\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"auto\",\n        \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-spec-memory\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_BATCH_SIZE\": \"100\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_INTERVAL_MS\": \"5000\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_AGE_MS\": \"3153600000000\",\n        \"SPECKIT_RETRY_QUEUE_MAX_PENDING\": \"300000\",\n        \"_NOTE_RECOMMENDED_SETUP\": \"New users: install Ollama (https://ollama.com) and run `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5`. The cascade auto-detects Ollama and persists nomic-embed-text-v1.5 (768d) as the active embedder — no API keys, all-local.\",\n        \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Default DB (recommended): context-index__ollama__nomic-embed-text-v1.5__768.sqlite (auto-derived from provider+model+dim). Pull `ollama pull nomic-embed-text:v1.5` for the local-first new-user setup; hf-local with nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5 is the zero-install Node fallback (no Python).\",\n        \"_NOTE_PROVIDERS\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama (local) -> hf-local (pure-Node @huggingface/transformers HTTP model server, zero-install) -> OpenAI API -> Voyage API.\",\n        \"_NOTE_EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER\": \"Auto cascade (ADR-014, local-first): Ollama -> hf-local -> OpenAI -> Voyage. Set EMBEDDINGS_PROVIDER=<provider> (ollama|hf-local|openai|voyage) to force a specific tier.\",\n        \"_NOTE_CLOUD_PROVIDERS\": \"Cloud tiers are explicit opt-in: add VOYAGE_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY only when you want cloud embeddings; otherwise the cascade keeps everything local. Voyage is embeddings-only here; cloud rerankers (voyage/cohere) were removed in 022/013.\",\n        \"_NOTE_GET_VOYAGE_KEY\": \"Get Voyage key: https://dash.voyageai.com/api-keys\",\n        \"_NOTE_GET_OPENAI_KEY\": \"Get OpenAI key: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\",\n        \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket. Pinned identically for mk-spec-memory AND mk_skill_advisor so both consume ONE resident nomic server (single-owner via the socket-keyed respawn lock). Short /tmp path stays under the macOS sun_path 104-char limit. Do not diverge the two services.\",\n        \"_NOTE_SOCKET\": \"macOS sun_path limit (104 chars): the default bridge socket path under database/daemon-ipc.sock exceeds the limit and the launcher fails with EINVAL. Pin to a short /tmp path so the multi-client bridge can bind.\",\n        \"_NOTE_FEATURE_FLAGS\": \"Opt-out flags (default ON): SPECKIT_ADAPTIVE_FUSION, SPECKIT_SESSION_BOOST, SPECKIT_CAUSAL_BOOST, SPECKIT_HYDE_ACTIVE, SPECKIT_ENTITY_LINKING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_CONCEPT_ROUTING, SPECKIT_GRAPH_REFRESH_MODE=write_local. Tier 3 LLM save routing is always on (fail-open to Tier 2 on timeout).\",\n        \"_NOTE_DAEMON_REELECTION\": \"Daemon re-election is on by default in the launcher code: on disposal the launcher releases the shared daemon for a live secondary to adopt instead of killing it, so concurrent sessions keep MCP transport. An unadopted released daemon is bounded by SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN. Set SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION=0 to restore kill-on-disposal. See ENV_REFERENCE.md.\",\n        \"_NOTE_RETRY_TUNING\": \"Bulk re-embed retry tuning: raised pending cap + max-age + faster batch/interval so a large embedding backlog drains instead of being parked as failed (defaults park excess/old pending: cap 1000, 24h age, 5-per-5min).\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"mk_skill_advisor\": {\n      \"command\": \"node\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"HF_EMBED_SERVER_URL\": \"unix:///tmp/mk-hf-embed/hf-embed.sock\",\n        \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR\": \".opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database\",\n        \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_HOOK_DISABLED\": \"0\",\n        \"MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"trusted\",\n        \"SPECKIT_ADVISOR_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-skill-advisor\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives at .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/database/skill-graph.sqlite by default; MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR overrides, with SYSTEM_SKILL_ADVISOR_DB_DIR as a legacy fallback (both still recognized by the launcher + handlers).\",\n        \"_NOTE_MEMORY_DB_PATH\": \"createChildEnv() pins the advisor child's embedder-pointer resolution (which DB's active_embedder_* row gets read) to this package's own skill-graph.sqlite. An ambient MEMORY_DB_PATH — including one set for mk-spec-memory's own unrelated use of that same name — is never honored as an override, since that would silently misroute the advisor's embedder selection to spec-memory's database (the exact bug this pin fixed). Tests/CI only: MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_MEMORY_DB_PATH overrides the pin. See db_path_policy.md §4.\",\n        \"_NOTE_THRESHOLDS\": \"Advisor confidence/uncertainty thresholds are tunable: SPECKIT_ADVISOR_CONFIDENCE_THRESHOLD (default 0.8), SPECKIT_ADVISOR_UNCERTAINTY_THRESHOLD (default 0.35). Lane weights tunable via SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_WEIGHTS_JSON + SPECKIT_ADVISOR_LANE_SHADOW_WEIGHTS_JSON (partial-merge JSON, post-022/011/4b).\",\n        \"_NOTE_DOC_TRIGGERS\": \"Opt-in doc-frontmatter harvest: skill_graph_scan ingests references/assets trigger_phrases into skill_docs and advisor_recommend returns matchedDocs pointers (dampened derived-lane signal). Default-off in code; enabled for this repo. Unset/false to roll back.\",\n        \"_NOTE_TRUST_DEFAULT\": \"Daemon-owner trust grant for mutation tools (advisor_rebuild, skill_graph_scan, skill_graph_propagate_enhances). Callers whose _meta omits transport/trust markers default to UNTRUSTED unless this is 'trusted'. Native MCP clients (e.g. /doctor repair flows) send no _meta, so this grant keeps them working; remove it to fail-closed on every transport-absent caller. Explicit _meta trusted:false / callerAuthority:'untrusted' is always rejected.\",\n        \"_NOTE_HF_EMBED_SOCKET\": \"Shared hf-local model-server socket — identical to mk-spec-memory's so both services share ONE resident nomic server. (skill-advisor only spawns it when SPECKIT_SKILL_ADVISOR_MODEL_SERVER_ENABLED=1; otherwise it just connects to mk-spec-memory's.)\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"mk_code_index\": {\n      \"command\": \"node\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \".opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_AGENTS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_COMMANDS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_PLUGINS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SKILLS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_SPECS\": \"true\",\n        \"SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR\": \"/tmp/mk-code-index\",\n        \"SPECKIT_MAX_SECONDARY_CLIENTS\": \"64\",\n        \"_NOTE_DB\": \"Database lives SKILL-LOCAL at .opencode/skills/system-code-graph/mcp-server/database/code-graph.sqlite by default (shared across runtimes via the .opencode/skills symlink); SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR overrides. Former shared location (.opencode/.spec-kit/code-graph/database/) is migrated back on first launcher startup.\",\n        \"_NOTE_INDEX_DEFAULTS\": \"INDEX_* committed defaults are false (end-user safe). Maintainer mode: set SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_MAINTAINER_MODE in .env.local (gitignored) to true (forces all 5 INDEX_* to true) or to a comma-separated subset such as skills,plugins (forces only those categories); the launcher applies the selection at startup. Per-call code_graph_scan args (includeSkills, includeAgents, includeCommands, includeSpecs, includePlugins) still override env for fine-grained control.\",\n        \"_NOTE_RESCAN_THRESHOLD\": \"SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_SELECTIVE_REINDEX_THRESHOLD (default 50) controls when the launcher switches from selective rescan to full scan. Raise to delay full-scans (faster session-boot, more drift tolerance); lower to keep the DB tighter. Post-commit hook (.opencode/scripts/git-hooks/post-commit) also invalidates the SQLite when commits exceed SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_POST_COMMIT_REBUILD_THRESHOLD (default 100).\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"code_mode\": {\n      \"command\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.nvm/versions/node/v24.9.0/bin/node\",\n      \"args\": [\n        \".opencode/skills/mcp-code-mode/mcp-server/dist/index.js\"\n      ],\n      \"env\": {\n        \"UTCP_CONFIG_FILE\": \".utcp_config.json\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":86,"totalLines":86,"truncated":false}},"title":".mcp.json","time":{"start":1785134062302,"end":1785134062325}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0a4297b86da91746016a66fbee228c819189fb5d8426cc0450"}},"id":"prt_fa2481adb0014ZA1BABDN5cVcU","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa247ea84001ghGyIJKW01ed5D"}}
