{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134273324,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_98kKEinpnjUSdaCOYJqNORdc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: title: Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\n3: description: Detached ten-iteration audit strategy for framework dead code, residue, placement, architecture, and over-engineering.\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\n7: \n8: ## 1. Overview\n9: \n10: This detached lineage runs exactly ten evidence iterations. Convergence is telemetry only before the hard cap. Each pass pivots to an uncovered repository surface or failure mode.\n11: \n12: ## 2. Topic\n13: \n14: Audit `.opencode/`, repository-root configuration, and `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, and `.devin/` mirrors for CAT-1 through CAT-6 findings. Exclude `.opencode/specs/` from findings.\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n17: ## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n18: \n19: - [ ] Which `bin/` launchers, daemon bridges, flags, and helper modules are unreachable, duplicated, or disproportionate?\n20: - [ ] Which MCP-server modules, generated outputs, and compatibility layers are dead, superseded, or misplaced?\n21: - [ ] Which deep-loop runtime layers duplicate responsibility, violate boundaries, or cost more than current usage justifies?\n22: - [ ] Which skill-hub metadata, mode registries, routers, and generated compiled-routing artifacts drift or duplicate policy?\n23: - [ ] Which commands and agents are stale, dynamically unreachable, mirrored incorrectly, or contractually inconsistent?\n24: - [ ] Which repository-root configs and dotfiles are obsolete, duplicated, or misplaced?\n25: - [ ] Which runtime mirror files drift from canonical `.opencode/` sources or contain redundant standalone logic?\n26: - [ ] Which backup, scratch, dated snapshot, generated output, or nested dependency residue exists outside excluded specs?\n27: - [ ] Which candidate files remain unreferenced after literal searches across code, docs, YAML, and JSON?\n28: - [ ] Which high-value simplifications survive adversarial cross-surface verification?\n29: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n30: \n31: ## 4. Non-Goals\n32: \n33: - Do not delete, move, rename, refactor, or repair audited files.\n34: - Do not report findings under `.opencode/specs/`.\n35: - Do not treat third-party dependency contents as findings unless a stray dependency tree is committed in a source surface.\n36: - Do not infer deadness from import graphs alone; dynamic string and documentation contracts count as reachability.\n37: \n38: ## 5. Stop Conditions\n39: \n40: - Complete all ten iterations unless state corruption prevents valid lineage artifacts.\n41: - Stop at iteration ten with `maxIterationsReached`.\n42: \n43: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n44: ## 6. Answered Questions\n45: \n46: None yet.\n47: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n48: \n49: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n50: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n51: ## 7. What Worked\n52: \n53: None yet.\n54: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n55: \n56: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n57: ## 8. What Failed\n58: \n59: None yet.\n60: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n61: \n62: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n63: ## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n64: \n65: None yet.\n66: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n67: \n68: <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n69: ## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n70: \n71: None yet.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n73: \n74: <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n75: ## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n76: \n77: - Completed pivots: 0\n78: - Saturated: none yet\n79: - Remaining frontier: all named surfaces\n80: <!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n81: \n82: <!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n83: ## 11A. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n84: \n85: None yet.\n86: <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n87: \n88: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n89: ## 11. Next Focus\n90: \n91: Iteration 1: `bin/`, launchers, daemon clients, and compiled-routing serving surface.\n92: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n93: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n94: \n95: ## 12. Known Context\n96: \n97: - The code graph is empty, so structural deadness must be established with exact literal searches and direct source inspection.\n98: - The audit excludes `.opencode/specs/` from findings and writes only to this lineage.\n99: - The caller requires every finding to name an existing path, `file:line` evidence, and an exact reproducible command.\n100: \n101: ## 13. Research Boundaries\n102: \n103: - Max iterations: 10\n104: - Convergence threshold: 0.05\n105: - Stop policy: max-iterations\n106: - Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n107: - Progressive synthesis: false\n108: - Executor provenance: `cli-opencode`, model `openai/gpt-5.6-sol`\n109: - Session: `fanout-sol-1785133613018-3fbdzo`\n110: - Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol`\n\n(End of file - total 110 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\ndescription: Detached ten-iteration audit strategy for framework dead code, residue, placement, architecture, and over-engineering.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nThis detached lineage runs exactly ten evidence iterations. Convergence is telemetry only before the hard cap. Each pass pivots to an uncovered repository surface or failure mode.\n\n## 2. Topic\n\nAudit `.opencode/`, repository-root configuration, and `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, and `.devin/` mirrors for CAT-1 through CAT-6 findings. Exclude `.opencode/specs/` from findings.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Which `bin/` launchers, daemon bridges, flags, and helper modules are unreachable, duplicated, or disproportionate?\n- [ ] Which MCP-server modules, generated outputs, and compatibility layers are dead, superseded, or misplaced?","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","text":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\ndescription: Detached ten-iteration audit strategy for framework dead code, residue, placement, architecture, and over-engineering.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Dead Code and Architecture Audit Sol Lineage\n\n## 1. Overview\n\nThis detached lineage runs exactly ten evidence iterations. Convergence is telemetry only before the hard cap. Each pass pivots to an uncovered repository surface or failure mode.\n\n## 2. Topic\n\nAudit `.opencode/`, repository-root configuration, and `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, and `.devin/` mirrors for CAT-1 through CAT-6 findings. Exclude `.opencode/specs/` from findings.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. Key Questions (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Which `bin/` launchers, daemon bridges, flags, and helper modules are unreachable, duplicated, or disproportionate?\n- [ ] Which MCP-server modules, generated outputs, and compatibility layers are dead, superseded, or misplaced?\n- [ ] Which deep-loop runtime layers duplicate responsibility, violate boundaries, or cost more than current usage justifies?\n- [ ] Which skill-hub metadata, mode registries, routers, and generated compiled-routing artifacts drift or duplicate policy?\n- [ ] Which commands and agents are stale, dynamically unreachable, mirrored incorrectly, or contractually inconsistent?\n- [ ] Which repository-root configs and dotfiles are obsolete, duplicated, or misplaced?\n- [ ] Which runtime mirror files drift from canonical `.opencode/` sources or contain redundant standalone logic?\n- [ ] Which backup, scratch, dated snapshot, generated output, or nested dependency residue exists outside excluded specs?\n- [ ] Which candidate files remain unreferenced after literal searches across code, docs, YAML, and JSON?\n- [ ] Which high-value simplifications survive adversarial cross-surface verification?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n## 4. Non-Goals\n\n- Do not delete, move, rename, refactor, or repair audited files.\n- Do not report findings under `.opencode/specs/`.\n- Do not treat third-party dependency contents as findings unless a stray dependency tree is committed in a source surface.\n- Do not infer deadness from import graphs alone; dynamic string and documentation contracts count as reachability.\n\n## 5. Stop Conditions\n\n- Complete all ten iterations unless state corruption prevents valid lineage artifacts.\n- Stop at iteration ten with `maxIterationsReached`.\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. Answered Questions\n\nNone yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. What Worked\n\nNone yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. What Failed\n\nNone yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n\nNone yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n\nNone yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: all named surfaces\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. Carried-Forward Open Questions\n\nNone yet.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. Next Focus\n\nIteration 1: `bin/`, launchers, daemon clients, and compiled-routing serving surface.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n\n## 12. Known Context\n\n- The code graph is empty, so structural deadness must be established with exact literal searches and direct source inspection.\n- The audit excludes `.opencode/specs/` from findings and writes only to this lineage.\n- The caller requires every finding to name an existing path, `file:line` evidence, and an exact reproducible command.\n\n## 13. Research Boundaries\n\n- Max iterations: 10\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Stop policy: max-iterations\n- Per-iteration budget: 12 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: false\n- Executor provenance: `cli-opencode`, model `openai/gpt-5.6-sol`\n- Session: `fanout-sol-1785133613018-3fbdzo`\n- Allowed write root: `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":110,"totalLines":110,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/system-speckit/028-memory-search-intelligence/001-release-cleanup/016-dead-code-and-architecture-audit/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1785134273313,"end":1785134273322}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08c53ddf6f498d8b016a66fcc084b48191b46ac9ba6279ce59"}},"id":"prt_fa24b52d6001UCIOVzsKmqOo3g","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa24b16