outing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:84]\n12: 4. **No additional old-name drift found:** old parent and eight old child identities occur only in the scoped rename ledger. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:21]\n13: \n14: ## Ruled Out\n15: \n16: - Stale parent `spec.md` hash.\n17: - Incorrect direct-child names, counts, or A–F membership.\n18: - Broken companion link between the two routing references.\n19: - Treating intentional rename-history tokens as live defects.\n20: \n21: ## Sources Consulted\n22: \n23: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:6]\n24: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:182]\n25: - [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:171]\n26: \n27: ## Assessment\n28: \n29: - New information ratio: 0.12\n30: - Novelty: low by design; this pass mainly falsified false positives and confirmed severity boundaries.\n31: \n32: ## Reflection\n33: \n34: Convergence telemetry is low, but the max-iterations policy required this final adversarial pass before synthesis.\n35: \n36: ## Recommended Next Focus\n37: \n38: Synthesize concrete findings; do not modify audited sources.\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 010 — Adversarial residual verification\n\n## Focus\n\nTry to falsify, deduplicate, and severity-rank all prior parent-level findings.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Confirmed highest-impact cluster:** ghost `000` child, stale narrow description, and null active-child routing are independent metadata defects, not duplicate wording. Together they can misrank or misroute resume. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:6] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/description.json:4] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:123]\n2. **Confirmed reference split-brain:** current 7/7 statements coexist with stale 2/7 quick-reference rows in the same authoritative document; this is not historical framing because the stale rows are labeled LIVE. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:182] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-config-and-advisor-reference.md:199]\n3. **Confirmed broken pointers:** the parent `../spec.md` and two `smart_routing.md` paths do not resolve; their sibling/current equivalents are known. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/spec.md:171] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/routing-before-after.md:84]\n4. **No additional old-name drift found:** old parent and eight old child identities occur only in the scoped rename ledger. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/context-index.md:21]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Stale parent `spec.md` hash.\n- Incorrect direct-child names, counts, or A–F membership.\n- Broken companion link between the two routing references.\n- Treating intentional rename-history tokens as live defects.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/research/lineages/sol-parent-audit/iterations/iteration-010.md","text":"# Iteration 010 — Adversarial residual verification\n\n## Focus\n\nTry to falsify, deduplicate, and severity-rank all prior parent-level findings.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Confirmed highest-impact cluster:** ghost `000` child, stale narrow description, and null active-child routing are independent metadata defects, not duplicate wording. Together they can misrank or misroute resume. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/graph-metadata.json:6] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/description.json:4] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor