ive code-audit dimension pass, P0/P1/P2 findings, JSONL state |\n\n  Line 163: | @ai-council | `.opencode/agents/ai-council.md` | Planning-only multi-strategy architect (max 3 strategies). Post-dispatch responsibility: when @orchestrate dispatches at Depth 1, run `node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-ai-council/scripts/persist-artifacts.cjs <packet>` after the LEAF returns to persist `ai-council/` artifacts (see ai-council persistence protocol). If the LEAF's returned report shows `max_rounds` reached without a converged plan (check `current_round >= max_rounds` in `ai-council-config.json`), add `--not-converged` to that invocation — the helper cannot detect max-round exhaustion on its own and defaults to `convergence:true` otherwise. |\n\n  Line 164: | @review   | `.opencode/agents/review.md`   | Codebase-agnostic quality scoring                                                      |\n\n  Line 165: | @debug    | `.opencode/agents/debug.md`    | Isolated by design (no conversation context)                                           |\n\n  Line 166: | @code     | `.opencode/agents/code.md`     | Application-code LEAF; sk-code stack delegation; D3 convention-floor caller-restriction (`Depth: 1` marker required); fail-closed verify |\n\n  Line 187: ├─ Agent Definition: [.opencode/agents/<name>.md — MUST be read and included in prompt | \"built-in\" for @general]\n\n  Line 271: ├─ Agent Def: [loaded | built-in | prior-session] → [.opencode/agents/<name>.md]\n\n  Line 405: **Trigger:** Task creates or substantively writes `.opencode/skills/**`, `.opencode/agents/**`, or `.opencode/commands/**` component definitions, role files, command workflows, templates, metadata, or package docs.\n\n  Line 809: | Improvise custom agent instructions instead of loading the definition file | Every custom agent has a definition file in `.opencode/agents/` (canonical source; `.claude/agents/` is this runtime's mirror) with specialized templates, enforcement rules, and quality standards; \"you are @debug\" in a prompt loses the actual debugging workflow | §2 |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/review.md:\n  Line 27: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/markdown.md:\n  Line 26: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/code.md:\n  Line 26: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n  Line 30: > ⛔ **DISPATCH GATE (§0 caller-restriction, D3 convention-floor):** @code MUST be dispatched by @orchestrate. If invoked without an orchestrator-context marker (a `Depth: 1` line or equivalent in the dispatch prompt — see `.opencode/agents/orchestrate.md` §2 NDP), HALT and return:\n\n  Line 36: > ⛔ **COMPONENT-AUTHORING GATE:** @code MUST NOT author skill, agent, or command components as component scaffolding or documentation. If the dispatch objective is to create or substantively write `.opencode/skills/**`, `.opencode/agents/**`, or `.opencode/commands/**` component definitions, role files, command workflows, templates, metadata, or package docs, HALT and return:\n\n  Line 38: > \"SCOPE_CONFLICT: @code does not author skill/agent/command components. The orchestrator should dispatch this work to @markdown (see `.opencode/agents/markdown.md`) using the orchestrator's agent dispatch. @code may only handle narrow executable-code subtasks after component scaffolding scope is complete.\"\n\n  Line 376: - Author skill, agent, or command component scaffolds/docs under `.opencode/skills/**`, `.opencode/agents/**`, or `.opencode/commands/**`; return `SCOPE_CONFLICT` and tell the orchestrator to dispatch `@markdown` (see `.opencode/agents/markdown.md`) unless the task is a narrow executable-code subtask with exact files and verification\n\n  Line 508: | **Component-authoring route bleed** | The task asks to create or substantively write a skill, agent, command, template, metadata file, or package docs under `.opencode/skills/**`, `.opencode/agents/**`, or `.opencode/commands/**` | Treat component scaffolding as @code implementation because the files live under `.opencode/` | RETURN `SCOPE_CONFLICT` and tell the orchestrator to dispatch `@markdown` (see `.opencode/agents/markdown.md`). @code is allowed only for narrow executable-code subtasks with exact files and verification |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/debug.md:\n  Line 26: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/design.md:\n  Line 28: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/deep-research.md:\n  Line 28: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/ai-council.md:\n  Line 29: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference. Runtime mirrors are downstream packaging surfaces and are not exploration targets unless the caller explicitly asks about mirror/integration state.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/deep-review.md:\n  Line 28: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference.\n\n  Line 300: | `.claude/agents/deep-review.md` | Mirror of canonical agent | Read-only context if explicitly in review scope; never edit |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/context.md:\n  Line 34: **Path Convention**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference. Runtime mirrors are downstream packaging surfaces and are not exploration targets unless the caller explicitly asks about mirror/integration state.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/prompt-improver.md:\n  Line 30: **IMPORTANT**: Use only `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference. Runtime mirrors are downstream packaging surfaces.\n\n  Line 67: | `INT-RUNTIME-MIRRORS` | `.claude/agents` | Downstream packaging surface only; never use it as canonical prompt authority |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/agents/deep-improvement.md:\n  Line 28: **IMPORTANT**: Use `.opencode/agents/*.md` as the canonical runtime path reference. Runtime mirrors are downstream packaging concerns.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/skills/system-code-graph/INSTALL-GUIDE.md:\n  Line 226: | `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_INDEX_AGENTS` | `false` | Include `.opencode/agents/**`. |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/hooks/README.md:\n  Line 21: Today the only hook is `pre-commit`, which runs two independent gates. The **comment-hygiene gate** blocks any commit that adds ephemeral-artifact pointers (spec-folder paths, packet/phase numbers, ADR/REQ/CHK/task/finding ids) to **code comments**, enforcing the durable-WHY rule from the code style guide. The **agent-mirror-sync gate** fires only when the commit stages files under `.opencode/agents/` or `.claude/agents/`, and blocks a commit that would desync the two agent mirrors. Both gates fail open if their tooling is missing.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-manual-testing-playbook-auto.yaml:\n  Line 45:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 46:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml:\n  Line 48:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 49:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-agent-auto.yaml:\n  Line 45:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 46:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-readme-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 78:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 79:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-agent-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 46:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 47:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-skill-parent-auto.yaml:\n  Line 45:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 46:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/install-guides/README.md:\n  Line 1276: ls .opencode/agents/*.md 2>/dev/null && echo \"✅ PASS\" || echo \"❌ FAIL\"\n\n  Line 1557: | `.opencode/agents/`          | Base agent source definitions                 |\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-skill-parent-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 45:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 46:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-feature-catalog-confirm.yaml:\n  Line 45:   default: .opencode/agents\n\n  Line 46:   claude: .claude/agents\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/commands/create/assets/create-changelog-auto.yaml:\n  Line 44:   default: .opencode/agents\n