:\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public\"},\"output\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/hf-model-server.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/code-index.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/cli-offline-smoke.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/spec-memory.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/cli-exit-taxonomy-smoke.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/skill-advisor.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/cli-offline-smoke.test.cjs\",\"metadata\":{\"count\":10,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"\",\"time\":{\"start\":1781780769372,\"end\":1781780769497}},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"fc_0873788f9d199a20016a33d1212a78819099b431a7866fafed\"}},\"id\":\"prt_eda68ea58001sansim7idmBFfO\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_12598b860ffelzDQeIUKkQIE0B\",\"messageID\":\"msg_eda6867a0001hD56aK7eBQIfMT\"}}\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/027-xce-research-based-refinement/005-verification-and-remediation/007-release-alignment-review/001-readmes-vs-027/review/seats/A09.json:\n  Line 34: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1781780262331,\"sessionID\":\"ses_125a0d67fffemhYqxhh1zk565k\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_kqTHfZMX2w8sJkzU7CdyWYx1\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION|re[-_ ]?election|daemon.*election\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public\",\"include\":\"*.{ts,js,json,jsonc,md,cjs,mjs}\"},\"output\":\"Found 100 matches (more matches available)\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/opencode.json:\\n  Line 43:         \\\"_NOTE_DAEMON_REELECTION\\\": \\\"Daemon re-election is on by default in the launcher code: on disposal the launcher releases the shared daemon for a live secondary to adopt instead of killing it, so concurrent sessions keep MCP transport. An unadopted released daemon is bounded by SPECKIT_LAUNCHER_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MIN. Set SPECKIT_DAEMON_REELECTION=0 to restore kill-on-disposal. See ENV_REFERENCE.md.\\\",\\n\\n\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/README.md:\\n  Line 144: The native MCP servers (`mk-spec-memory`, `mk_skill_advisor`, `mk_code_index`) ship as committed launcher binaries under `.opencode/bin/`. They self-vendor their dependencies on first run and the checked-in runtime configs already point at them, so there is no separate build step. Launcher reliability (owner-disposal relaunch, lease-probe reap, mk-code-index reconnect, default-on daemon re-election and a single-writer database lock with `SPECKIT_DB_LOCK_DISABLE=1` as the kill switch) is operator-tunable and documented in [`ENV_REFERENCE.md`](.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/mcp_server/ENV_REFERENCE.md).\\n\\n\\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.claude/mcp.json:\\n  Line 33:         \\\"_NOTE_DAEMON_REELECTION\\\": \\\"Daemon re-election is on by default in the launcher code: on disposal the launcher releases the shared daemon for a live secondary to adopt instead of killing it, so concurrent sessions keep MCP trans...\n  Line 38: {\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1781780278907,\"sessionID\":\"ses_125a0d67fffemhYqxhh1zk565k\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_nrKbnznAr268lTDmrx3MZU4E\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md\",\"offset\":15,\"limit\":85},\"output\":\"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n15: ## 1. OVERVIEW\\n16: \\n17: `bin/` holds the executable entrypoints that the OpenCode runtime spawns to start each MCP server, plus the daemon-backed CLI shims that reach the same servers from a shell. Three launchers wrap the spec-kit, skill-advisor and code-graph MCP servers; three CLI shims (`spec-memory.cjs`, `code-index.cjs`, `skill-advisor.cjs`) front the same daemons over the IPC socket; one process is the local HuggingFace embedding server that serves `hf-local` vector requests over a Unix domain socket or TCP loopback.\\n18: \\n19: Current state:\\n20: \\n21: - Each launcher loads project-local `.env.local` / `.env`, ensures the server's `dist/` artifacts are built and current, serializes concurrent starts with a filesystem bootstrap lock, then spawns the MCP child and bridges stdio to the running daemon.\\n22: - The three CLI shims run the built daemon-backed CLIs (`spec-memory` 37 tools, `code-index` 8 tools, `skill-advisor` 9 tools) against the **same unchanged daemons** the MCP registrations use — a dual-stack surface, not a replacement. Each shim enforces a dist-freshness guard (exit `69` on missing/stale dist, with a per-CLI `*_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), defaults `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` to the short `/tmp/<service>` directory, and refuses a socket path over the Darwin `sun_path` limit.\\n23: - `hf-model-server.cjs` loads a transformers model and answers `/api/health` and `/api/embed` requests. It refuses any non-loopback bind unless the operator sets `HF_EMBED_ALLOW_REMOTE_BIND=1` an...\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/027-xce