{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134512312,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_vGlHY6A0UQfUfQ7SaQaYYXVk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"daemonReelectionEnabled|launcher-session-proxy|launcher-ipc-bridge|model-server-supervision","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin","include":"*.cjs"},"output":"Found 17 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs:\n  Line 18: const mss = require('./lib/model-server-supervision.cjs');\n\n  Line 19: const { createSessionProxy } = require('./lib/launcher-session-proxy.cjs');\n\n  Line 231: function daemonReelectionEnabled(env = process.env) {\n\n  Line 296:     return require('./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs');\n\n  Line 1520:   const reelectionEnabled = daemonReelectionEnabled();\n\n  Line 1665:   if (shouldReleaseDaemonForReelection({ enabled: daemonReelectionEnabled(), hasLiveDaemon: isChildRunning(childProcess) })) {\n\n  Line 1981:   daemonReelectionEnabled,\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/lib/launcher-session-proxy.cjs:\n  Line 17: } = require('./launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs');\n\n  Line 87:   process.stderr.write(`[launcher-session-proxy] ${message}\\n`);\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/lib/model-server-supervision.cjs:\n  Line 57:   process.stderr.write(`[model-server-supervision] ${message}\\n`);\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/mk-code-index-launcher.cjs:\n  Line 18: const { createSessionProxy, createClassifyFrame } = require('./lib/launcher-session-proxy.cjs');\n\n  Line 225:     return require('./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs');\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs:\n  Line 32:     return require('./lib/model-server-supervision.cjs');\n\n  Line 174:     return require('./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs');\n\n  Line 213:     sessionProxyModule = require('./lib/launcher-session-proxy.cjs');\n\n  Line 253:     throw new Error('launcher-session-proxy.cjs is unavailable');\n\n  Line 952:     throw new Error('model-server-supervision.cjs is unavailable');\n","metadata":{"matches":17,"truncated":false},"title":"daemonReelectionEnabled|launcher-session-proxy|launcher-ipc-bridge|model-server-supervision","time":{"start":1785134512290,"end":1785134512311}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03fe8c3abcaf7ab2016a66fdb0247c8191b4b8869c2da39222"}},"id":"prt_fa24ef89d001Zw1BcrkjCKE6vZ","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa24ec9dc001aS6yDJgiu1b8D3"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785134512319,"sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_qUzYbusgbpPmjLtAPEKargHk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md","offset":88,"limit":70},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n88: +-- compiled-route-status.cjs      # Per-hub serving status with a cause code separating drift from breakage\n89: +-- compiled-route-guard.cjs       # Freshness gate: serving matches inputs, runtime matches source\n90: +-- compiled-route-manifest.cjs    # CLI over the activation-manifest library in lib/\n91: +-- compiled-route-sync.cjs        # Publication tool: trace, stage, verify, swap, finalize or revert\n92: +-- check-no-spec-imports.cjs      # Proves nothing here reaches into the spec tree at runtime\n93: +-- compiled-routing-*.vitest.ts   # Routing foundation and flag-propagation suites\n94: +-- mk-code-index-launcher-*.vitest.ts  # Launcher lease, registry and WAL coverage\n95: +-- tests/                         # node:test suite for the publication lifecycle\n96: +-- lib/                           # Shared supervision, IPC bridge, env allowlist, routing library\n97: `-- README.md\n98: ```\n99: \n100: ---\n101: \n102: ## 4. KEY FILES\n103: \n104: | File | Responsibility |\n105: |---|---|\n106: | `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-spec-memory MCP child. Manages the shared hf-model-server lease, respawn locks, and reaping a dead lease child before respawn. |\n107: | `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-skill-advisor MCP child. Loads model-server supervision when enabled, enforces a strict single-writer lease, and rebuilds `dist/` from `handlers`, `lib`, `schemas`, `tools` when stale. |\n108: | `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-code-index MCP child. Applies the maintainer-mode `INDEX_*` override, migrates the code-graph database back to the skill-local path, and sets `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR` for the child. |\n109: | `spec-memory.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-spec-memory. Checks dist freshness and exits `69` when stale, with `SPECKIT_SPEC_MEMORY_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` as the override, ensures the socket dir, then runs `mcp-server/dist/spec-memory-cli.js` with inherited stdio. |\n110: | `code-index.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-code-index. Same guard pattern (`SPECKIT_CODE_INDEX_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/code-index-cli.js`. Blocked-read payloads render as actionable answers (exit `0`). `detect_changes` `parse_error` exits `64`. |\n111: | `skill-advisor.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-skill-advisor. Same guard pattern (`MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/mcp-server/skill-advisor-cli.js`. Mutation tools require `--trusted` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`. calls are sent untrusted by default. |\n112: | `hf-model-server.cjs` | Loads a transformers embedding model and serves `/api/health` and `/api/embed`. Enforces the loopback bind perimeter guard, socket-dir ownership, request size limits and inference timeouts. |\n113: \n114: Lifecycle parity note: `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` is the hardened reference for persistent launcher logging, detached daemon re-election/adoption, and owner-release-on-shutdown. `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` and `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` currently stop with their child and rely on fresh-session reload plus bridge/respawn paths instead.\n115: \n116: ---\n117: \n118: ## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n119: \n120: | Boundary | Rule |\n121: |---|---|\n122: | Imports | Launchers require `./lib/model-server-supervision.cjs` and `./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs`. The model server requires only Node core plus `@huggingface/transformers` loaded at runtime. |\n123: | Exports | Launchers run as CLI processes. `hf-model-server.cjs` exports `createHfModelServer`, `loadHfModel`, `resolveListenTarget`, `assertLoopbackBindAllowed`, `assertSocketDirOwnership` and `probeSocketResident` for tests and direct callers. |\n124: | Ownership | This folder owns process bootstrap, lease arbitration and the embedding HTTP surface. MCP request handling, schemas and tools live in each server's own skill directory under `.opencode/skills/`. |\n125: \n126: Main flow:\n127: \n128: ```text\n129: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n130: │ OpenCode runtime spawns mk-*-launcher    │\n131: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n132:                   │\n133:                   ▼\n134: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n135: │ load .env.local / .env, refresh paths    │\n136: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n137:                   │\n138:                   ▼\n139: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n140: │ build dist if artifacts stale            │\n141: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n142:                   │\n143:                   ▼\n144: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n145: │ acquire bootstrap + respawn lease        │\n146: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n147:                   │\n148:                   ▼\n149: ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n150: │ spawn MCP child, bridge stdio to socket  │\n151: └──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n152:                   │\n153:                   ▼\n154: ╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n155: │ runtime talks to the live daemon         │\n156: ╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n157: ```\n\n(Showing lines 88-157 of 252. Use offset=158 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"+-- compiled-route-status.cjs      # Per-hub serving status with a cause code separating drift from breakage\n+-- compiled-route-guard.cjs       # Freshness gate: serving matches inputs, runtime matches source\n+-- compiled-route-manifest.cjs    # CLI over the activation-manifest library in lib/\n+-- compiled-route-sync.cjs        # Publication tool: trace, stage, verify, swap, finalize or revert\n+-- check-no-spec-imports.cjs      # Proves nothing here reaches into the spec tree at runtime\n+-- compiled-routing-*.vitest.ts   # Routing foundation and flag-propagation suites\n+-- mk-code-index-launcher-*.vitest.ts  # Launcher lease, registry and WAL coverage\n+-- tests/                         # node:test suite for the publication lifecycle\n+-- lib/                           # Shared supervision, IPC bridge, env allowlist, routing library\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-spec-memory MCP child. Manages the shared hf-model-server lease, respawn locks, and reaping a dead lease child before respawn. |\n| `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-skill-advisor MCP child. Loads model-server supervision when enabled, enforces a strict single-writer lease, and rebuilds `dist/` from `handlers`, `lib`, `schemas`, `tools` when stale. |","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/bin/README.md","text":"+-- compiled-route-status.cjs      # Per-hub serving status with a cause code separating drift from breakage\n+-- compiled-route-guard.cjs       # Freshness gate: serving matches inputs, runtime matches source\n+-- compiled-route-manifest.cjs    # CLI over the activation-manifest library in lib/\n+-- compiled-route-sync.cjs        # Publication tool: trace, stage, verify, swap, finalize or revert\n+-- check-no-spec-imports.cjs      # Proves nothing here reaches into the spec tree at runtime\n+-- compiled-routing-*.vitest.ts   # Routing foundation and flag-propagation suites\n+-- mk-code-index-launcher-*.vitest.ts  # Launcher lease, registry and WAL coverage\n+-- tests/                         # node:test suite for the publication lifecycle\n+-- lib/                           # Shared supervision, IPC bridge, env allowlist, routing library\n`-- README.md\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. KEY FILES\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-spec-memory MCP child. Manages the shared hf-model-server lease, respawn locks, and reaping a dead lease child before respawn. |\n| `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-skill-advisor MCP child. Loads model-server supervision when enabled, enforces a strict single-writer lease, and rebuilds `dist/` from `handlers`, `lib`, `schemas`, `tools` when stale. |\n| `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` | Boots the mk-code-index MCP child. Applies the maintainer-mode `INDEX_*` override, migrates the code-graph database back to the skill-local path, and sets `SPECKIT_CODE_GRAPH_DB_DIR` for the child. |\n| `spec-memory.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-spec-memory. Checks dist freshness and exits `69` when stale, with `SPECKIT_SPEC_MEMORY_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` as the override, ensures the socket dir, then runs `mcp-server/dist/spec-memory-cli.js` with inherited stdio. |\n| `code-index.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-code-index. Same guard pattern (`SPECKIT_CODE_INDEX_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/code-index-cli.js`. Blocked-read payloads render as actionable answers (exit `0`). `detect_changes` `parse_error` exits `64`. |\n| `skill-advisor.cjs` | CLI shim for mk-skill-advisor. Same guard pattern (`MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_DEV_ALLOW_STALE=1` override), runs `mcp-server/dist/mcp-server/skill-advisor-cli.js`. Mutation tools require `--trusted` or `MK_SKILL_ADVISOR_CLI_TRUSTED=1`. calls are sent untrusted by default. |\n| `hf-model-server.cjs` | Loads a transformers embedding model and serves `/api/health` and `/api/embed`. Enforces the loopback bind perimeter guard, socket-dir ownership, request size limits and inference timeouts. |\n\nLifecycle parity note: `mk-spec-memory-launcher.cjs` is the hardened reference for persistent launcher logging, detached daemon re-election/adoption, and owner-release-on-shutdown. `mk-code-index-launcher.cjs` and `mk-skill-advisor-launcher.cjs` currently stop with their child and rely on fresh-session reload plus bridge/respawn paths instead.\n\n---\n\n## 5. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW\n\n| Boundary | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Imports | Launchers require `./lib/model-server-supervision.cjs` and `./lib/launcher-ipc-bridge.cjs`. The model server requires only Node core plus `@huggingface/transformers` loaded at runtime. |\n| Exports | Launchers run as CLI processes. `hf-model-server.cjs` exports `createHfModelServer`, `loadHfModel`, `resolveListenTarget`, `assertLoopbackBindAllowed`, `assertSocketDirOwnership` and `probeSocketResident` for tests and direct callers. |\n| Ownership | This folder owns process bootstrap, lease arbitration and the embedding HTTP surface. MCP request handling, schemas and tools live in each server's own skill directory under `.opencode/skills/`. |\n\nMain flow:\n\n```text\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ OpenCode runtime spawns mk-*-launcher    │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ load .env.local / .env, refresh paths    │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ build dist if artifacts stale            │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ acquire bootstrap + respawn lease        │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ spawn MCP child, bridge stdio to socket  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                  │\n                  ▼\n╭──────────────────────────────────────────╮\n│ runtime talks to the live daemon         │\n╰──────────────────────────────────────────╯\n```","lineStart":88,"lineEnd":157,"totalLines":252,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/bin/README.md","time":{"start":1785134512275,"end":1785134512318}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03fe8c3abcaf7ab2016a66fdb024608191b8ad0509aa5eb217"}},"id":"prt_fa24ef866001fDCrXPilP9DsNZ","sessionID":"ses_05dbebdb4ffe8dApbcbo3OIc7y","messageID":"msg_fa24ec9dc001aS6yDJgiu1b8D3"}}
