en compiler implementations.\n+- Legacy command bodies remain live; agent mirrors have concrete inventory drift.\n+- Root config symlinks are coherent, but skill-advisor database state is split across hyphen and underscore paths.\n+- One rotated log escapes ignore rules; hidden scanners are workstation-pinned.\n+- No CAT-1 or safely deletable CAT-2 file survived adversarial literal verification.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n \n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n ## 7. What Worked\n \n-None yet.\n+- Exact literal search across code and documentation formats.\n+- Direct source reads at producer and consumer boundaries.\n+- File-count, line-count, inode, hash, ignore, and git-status checks.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. What Failed\n \n-None yet.\n+- Broad ripgrep calls exceeded the JSON record limit; narrower scoped searches replaced them.\n+- Code graph evidence was unavailable because the index was empty.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. Exhausted Approaches\n \n-None yet.\n+- Import-graph-only deadness classification.\n+- Treating absence from CI as proof that a manual operator tool is dead.\n+- Treating expected runtime mirror differences as corruption.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n ## 10. Ruled-Out Directions\n \n-None yet.\n+- Deleting `check-no-spec-imports.cjs`, plugin bridges, legacy command bodies, or compiled routers.\n+- Reporting root config symlinks or `.rename-engine-disposable` as residue.\n+- Reporting generated inventory files as accidental without accounting for explicit retention.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n ## 10A. Saturated Directions and Divergence Frontier\n \n-- Completed pivots: 0\n-- Saturated: none yet\n-- Remaining frontier: all named surfaces\n+- Completed pivots: 10\n+- Saturated: all named audit surfaces\